('sahih-al-bukhari',8,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the clothes of a prayer person in prostration touched his wife [would that make his Salat (prayer) invalid]?','باب إِذَا أَصَابَ ثَوْبُ الْمُصَلِّي امْرَأَتَهُ إِذَا سَجَدَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayers) on the Hasir (a mat that is made of the leaves of date-palm trees and is as long as or longer than a man''s stature)','باب الصَّلاَةِ عَلَى الْحَصِيرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayers) on a Khumra (a small mat, hardly sufficient for the face and hands while prostrating during Salat)','باب الصَّلاَةِ عَلَى الْخُمْرَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayers) on the bed','باب الصَّلاَةِ عَلَى الْفِرَاشِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To prostrate on a garment in scorching heat','باب السُّجُودِ عَلَى الثَّوْبِ فِي شِدَّةِ الْحَرِّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer Salat (prayer) with the shoes on','باب الصَّلاَةِ فِي النِّعَالِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayers) wearing Khuff (leather socks)','باب الصَّلاَةِ فِي الْخِفَافِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If someone does not prostrate properly','باب إِذَا لَمْ يُتِمَّ السُّجُودَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'During Prostrations one should show his armpits and separate his forearms from his body','باب يُبْدِي ضَبْعَيْهِ وَيُجَافِي فِي السُّجُودِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Superiority of (praying) facing the Qiblah with the toes toward it as well','باب فَضْلِ اسْتِقْبَالِ الْقِبْلَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Qiblah for the people of Al-Madina, Sham and the East.','باب قِبْلَةِ أَهْلِ الْمَدِينَةِ وَأَهْلِ الشَّأْمِ وَالْمَشْرِقِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Statement of Allah " And take you (people) the Maqam (place) of Ibrahim (Abraham) (or the stone on which Abrahim stood while he was building the Kabah as a place of prayer (for some of your Salat e.g., two Raka after the Tawaf of Kabah)"','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {وَاتَّخِذُوا مِنْ مَقَامِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ مُصَلًّى}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'[During the obligatory Salat (prayers)] one should face the Qiblah (Kabah at Makkah) wherever one may be','باب التَّوَجُّهِ نَحْوَ الْقِبْلَةِ حَيْثُ كَانَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What has been said about (facing) the Qiblah (Kabah at Makkah) and wherever considered that there was no need to repeat the Salat (prayer) if someone offered prayers by mistake facing a direction other than that of the Qiblah','بَابُ مَا جَاءَ فِي الْقِبْلَةِ، وَمَنْ لاَ يَرَى الإِعَادَةَ عَلَى مَنْ سَهَا فَصَلَّى إِلَى غَيْرِ الْقِبْلَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To scrape off the sputum from the mosque with the hand (using some tool or other, or using  n tool)','باب حَكِّ الْبُزَاقِ بِالْيَدِ مِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To scrape the nasal secretion off the mosque with gravel','باب حَكِّ الْمُخَاطِ بِالْحَصَى مِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is forbidden to spit on the right side while in Salat (prayers)','باب لاَ يَبْصُقْ عَنْ يَمِينِهِ، فِي الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One should spit on the left side or under one''s left foot','باب لِيَبْزُقْ عَنْ يَسَارِهِ، أَوْ تَحْتَ قَدَمِهِ الْيُسْرَى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The expiation for spitting in the mosque','باب كَفَّارَةِ الْبُزَاقِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,38,'38',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The burying of the expectoration in the mosque','باب دَفْنِ النُّخَامَةِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,39,'39',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the spit or sputum comes out suddenly then one should spit in the corner of one''s garnet','باب إِذَا بَدَرَهُ الْبُزَاقُ فَلْيَأْخُذْ بِطَرَفِ ثَوْبِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,40,'40',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Preaching of the Imam to the people regarding the proper offering of As-Salat (the prayers) and the mention of the Qiblah (Kabah at Makkah)','باب عِظَةِ الإِمَامِ النَّاسَ فِي إِتْمَامِ الصَّلاَةِ، وَذِكْرِ الْقِبْلَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to say, "Masjid (mosque) of Bani so-and-so?','باب هَلْ يُقَالُ مَسْجِدُ بَنِي فُلاَنٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,42,'42',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The distribution (of goods or wealh) and the hanging of a cluster of dates in the mosque.','باب الْقِسْمَةِ وَتَعْلِيقِ الْقِنْوِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,43,'43',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Receivng and invitation to dinner in the mosque and accepting it','باب مَنْ دَعَا لِطَعَامٍ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ وَمَنْ أَجَابَ فِيهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,44,'44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To give the judicial verdicts in the mosque and to perform the Al-Lian between men and women (husbands and wives) there','باب الْقَضَاءِ وَاللِّعَانِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ بَيْنَ الرِّجَالِ وَالنِّسَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,45,'45',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If someone enters a house, should he offer prayers where he likes, or as he is told? And he should not look out to seek information about the place or do spying','باب إِذَا دَخَلَ بَيْتًا يُصَلِّي حَيْثُ شَاءَ، أَوْ حَيْثُ أُمِرَ، وَلاَ يَتَجَسَّسُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,46,'46',NULL,NULL,NULL,'About (taking) the mosques in the houses','باب الْمَسَاجِدِ فِي الْبُيُوتِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,47,'47',NULL,NULL,NULL,'While entering the mosques etc. one should start with the right foot','باب التَّيَمُّنِ فِي دُخُولِ الْمَسْجِدِ وَغَيْرِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,48,'48',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Is it permissible to dig the graves of pagans of the period of Ignorance, and to use that place as a mosque?','بَابُ هَلْ تُنْبَشُ قُبُورُ مُشْرِكِي الْجَاهِلِيَّةِ، وَيُتَّخَذُ مَكَانَهَا مَسَاجِدَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,49,'49',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) in a sheep-fold','باب الصَّلاَةِ فِي مَرَابِضِ الْغَنَمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,50,'50',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) in the camel yards (the places where the camels are stationed)','باب الصَّلاَةِ فِي مَوَاضِعِ الإِبِلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,51,'51',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever offered Salat (prayer)  with furnace or fire or any other worshipable thing in front of him but he intended Salat solely for Allah','باب مَنْ صَلَّى وَقُدَّامَهُ تَنُّورٌ أَوْ نَارٌ أَوْ شَىْءٌ مِمَّا يُعْبَدُ، فَأَرَادَ بِهِ اللَّهَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,52,'52',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The dislikeness of offering As-Salat (the prayers) in grave-yards','باب كَرَاهِيَةِ الصَّلاَةِ فِي الْمَقَابِرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,53,'53',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(What is said about) offering Salat (Prayer) at the places where the earth had sunk down and Allah''s punishment had fallen','باب الصَّلاَةِ فِي مَوَاضِعِ الْخَسْفِ وَالْعَذَابِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,54,'54',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) in a church or in a temple etc.','باب الصَّلاَةِ فِي الْبِيعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,55,'55',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,56,'56',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The sayings of the Prophet (pbuh) "The earth has been made for me a Masjid (place for praying) and a thing to purify (to perform Tayammum)."','باب قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏"‏ جُعِلَتْ لِيَ الأَرْضُ مَسْجِدًا وَطَهُورًا ‏"‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,57,'57',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sleeping of a woman in the mosque (and residing in it)','باب نَوْمِ الْمَرْأَةِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,58,'58',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sleeping of a men in the mosque','باب نَوْمِ الرِّجَالِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,59,'59',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) whe returning from a journey','باب الصَّلاَةِ إِذَا قَدِمَ مِنْ سَفَرٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,60,'60',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If one entered a mosque, one should offer two Rak''a (Tahayyat-al-Masjid) before sitting','باب إِذَا دَخَلَ الْمَسْجِدَ فَلْيَرْكَعْ رَكْعَتَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,61,'61',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Hadath (passing wind) in the mosque','باب الْحَدَثِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,62,'62',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The construction of (the prophet''s pbuh) mosque','باب بُنْيَانِ الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,63,'63',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To co-operate in building a mosque','باب التَّعَاوُنِ فِي بِنَاءِ الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,64,'64',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Employing the carpenter and the technical hand (artsan) in making the wooden pulpit or building the mosque','باب الاِسْتِعَانَةِ بِالنَّجَّارِ وَالصُّنَّاعِ فِي أَعْوَادِ الْمِنْبَرِ وَالْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,65,'65',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(The superiority of) whoever built a mosque','باب مَنْ بَنَى مَسْجِدًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,66,'66',NULL,NULL,NULL,'While passing through a mosque, (one should better) hold the arrowheads (with the hand)','باب يَأْخُذُ بِنُصُولِ النَّبْلِ إِذَا مَرَّ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,67,'67',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Passing through the mosque (is permissible)','باب الْمُرُورِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,68,'68',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(What is said about) reciting poetry in the mosque?','باب الشِّعْرِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,69,'69',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The presence of spearmen (with their spears) in the mosque (is permissible)','باب أَصْحَابِ الْحِرَابِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,70,'70',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mentioning about sales and purchases on the pulpit in the mosque','باب ذِكْرِ الْبَيْعِ وَالشِّرَاءِ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,71,'71',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Asking a debtor to repay what he owes and catching the debtor in the mosque','باب التَّقَاضِي وَالْمُلاَزَمَةِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,72,'72',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sweeping (cleaning) of the mosque and removing rags, dirt and sticks from it','باب كَنْسِ الْمَسْجِدِ وَالْتِقَاطِ الْخِرَقِ وَالْقَذَى وَالْعِيدَانِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,73,'73',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The order of banning the trade of alcoholic drinks was issues in the mosque','باب تَحْرِيمِ تِجَارَةِ الْخَمْرِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,74,'74',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Servants for the mosque','باب الْخَدَمِ لِلْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,75,'75',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To fasten a prisoner or a debtor in the mosque','باب الأَسِيرِ أَوِ الْغَرِيمِ يُرْبَطُ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,76,'76',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To take a bath on embracing Islam and fasten a prisoner in the mosque','بَابُ الاِغْتِسَالِ إِذَا أَسْلَمَ، وَرَبْطِ الأَسِيرِ أَيْضًا فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,77,'77',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To pitch a tent in the mosque for patients, etc','باب الْخَيْمَةِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ لِلْمَرْضَى وَغَيْرِهِمْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,78,'78',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To take the camel inside the mosque if necessary','باب إِدْخَالِ الْبَعِيرِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ لِلْعِلَّةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,79,'79',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chaper','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,80,'80',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Khaukhah (a small door) and a path in the mosque','باب الْخَوْخَةِ وَالْمَمَرِّ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,81,'81',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The doors and locks of the Kabah and the mosques','باب الأَبْوَابِ وَالْغَلَقِ لِلْكَعْبَةِ وَالْمَسَاجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,82,'82',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The entering of a pagan in the mosque','باب دُخُولِ الْمُشْرِكِ الْمَسْجِدَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,83,'83',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Raising the voice in the mosque','باب رَفْعِ الصَّوْتِ فِي الْمَسَاجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,84,'84',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The religious gathering in circles and sitting in the mosque','باب الْحِلَقِ وَالْجُلُوسِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,85,'85',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To lie flat (on the back) in the mosque','باب الاِسْتِلْقَاءِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ وَمَدِّ الرِّجْلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,86,'86',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(If) a mosque (is built) on a road, it should not be a cause of harm for the people','باب الْمَسْجِدِ يَكُونُ فِي الطَّرِيقِ مِنْ غَيْرِ ضَرَرٍ بِالنَّاسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,87,'87',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayers) in a mosque situated in a market','باب الصَّلاَةِ فِي مَسْجِدِ السُّوقِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,88,'88',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To clasp one''s hands by interlocking the fingers in the mosque or outside the mosque','باب تَشْبِيكِ الأَصَابِعِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ وَغَيْرِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,89,'89',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The mosques which are on the way to Al-Madina and the places where the Prophet (pbuh) had offered Salat (Prayers)','بَابُ الْمَسَاجِدِ الَّتِي عَلَى طُرُقِ الْمَدِينَةِ، وَالْمَوَاضِعِ الَّتِي صَلَّى فِيهَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,90,'90',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Sutra of the Imam is also a Sutra for those who are behind him','باب سُتْرَةُ الإِمَامِ سُتْرَةُ مَنْ خَلْفَهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,91,'91',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What should be the distance between the person offering Salat (prayer) and the Sutra?','باب قَدْرِ كَمْ يَنْبَغِي أَنْ يَكُونَ بَيْنَ الْمُصَلِّي وَالسُّتْرَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,92,'92',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) using a Harba (a short spear) (as a Sutra)','باب الصَّلاَةِ إِلَى الْحَرْبَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,93,'93',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) using an ''Anaza (a spear-headed stick) (as a Sutra)','باب الصَّلاَةِ إِلَى الْعَنَزَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,94,'94',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sutra (for the prayer)in Makkah and elsewhere.','باب السُّتْرَةِ بِمَكَّةَ وَغَيْرِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,95,'95',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) facing a pillar','باب الصَّلاَةِ إِلَى الأُسْطُوَانَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,96,'96',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer non-congregational As-Salat (the prayers) between the pillars','باب الصَّلاَةِ بَيْنَ السَّوَارِي فِي غَيْرِ جَمَاعَةٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,97,'97',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,98,'98',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) facing a Rahila camel, a tree or a camel saddle as a Sutra).','باب الصَّلاَةِ إِلَى الرَّاحِلَةِ وَالْبَعِيرِ وَالشَّجَرِ وَالرَّحْلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,99,'99',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) facing a bed','باب الصَّلاَةِ إِلَى السَّرِيرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,100,'100',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The person offering Salat (prayer) should repulse that person who tries to pass in front of him','باب يَرُدُّ الْمُصَلِّي مَنْ مَرَّ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,101,'101',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The sin of a person who passes in front of a person offering Salat','باب إِثْمِ الْمَارِّ بَيْنَ يَدَىِ الْمُصَلِّي'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,102,'102',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A man facing a man while offering Salat (prayer)','باب اسْتِقْبَالِ الرَّجُلِ صَاحِبَهُ أَوْ غَيْرَهُ فِي صَلاَتِهِ وَهُوَ يُصَلِّي'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,103,'103',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer As-Salat (the prayer) behind a sleeping person','باب الصَّلاَةِ خَلْفَ النَّائِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,104,'104',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer Nawafil (non-obligatory prayers) behind a sleeping woman','باب التَّطَوُّعِ خَلْفَ الْمَرْأَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,105,'105',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever says "Nothing annuls As-Salat (the prayer) (i.e. nothing of what others do, not the praying person himself)."','باب مَنْ قَالَ لاَ يَقْطَعُ الصَّلاَةَ شَىْءٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,106,'106',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a small girl is carried on one''s neck during the Salat (prayer)','باب إِذَا حَمَلَ جَارِيَةً صَغِيرَةً عَلَى عُنُقِهِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,107,'107',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer Salat (prayer) facing a bed occupied by a menstruatng woman','باب إِذَا صَلَّى إِلَى فِرَاشٍ فِيهِ حَائِضٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,108,'108',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Is it permissible to touch or push one''s wife in prostration in order to prostrate properly?','باب هَلْ يَغْمِزُ الرَّجُلُ امْرَأَتَهُ عِنْدَ السُّجُودِ لِكَىْ يَسْجُدَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',8,109,'109',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A woman can remove troublesome or offensive things from a person in Salat (prayer)','باب الْمَرْأَةِ تَطْرَحُ عَنِ الْمُصَلِّي، شَيْئًا مِنَ الأَذَى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The times of As-Salat (the prayers) and the superiority of offering Salat (prayers) in time','باب مَوَاقِيتِ الصَّلاَةِ وَفَضْلِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Statement of Allah عز وجل: (And remain always) turning in repentance to Him (only), and be afraid and dutiful to Him; and perform As-Salat (Iqamat-as-Salat) and be not of Al-Mushrikun (the disbelievers in the Oneness of Allah, polytheists, idolaters). (V.30:31)','بَابُ: {مُنِيبِينَ إِلَيْهِ وَاتَّقُوهُ وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلاَةَ وَلاَ تَكُونُوا مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To give the Bai''ah (pledge) for Iqamat-as-Salat [the offering of As-Salat (the prayers).','باب الْبَيْعَةِ عَلَى إِقَامَةِ الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'As-Salat (the prayers) is expiation (of sins)','باب الصَّلاَةُ كَفَّارَةٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Superiority of offering As-Salat (the prayers) at the stated times','باب فَضْلِ الصَّلاَةِ لِوَقْتِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The five Salat (prayers) are expiations (of sins)','باب الصَّلَوَاتُ الْخَمْسُ كَفَّارَةٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Not offering As-Salat (the prayers) at its stated fixed time','باب تَضْيِيعِ الصَّلاَةِ عَنْ وَقْتِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A person in Salat (prayer) is speaking in private to his Lord (Allah)','باب الْمُصَلِّي يُنَاجِي رَبَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'In severe heat, offer Zuhr prayers when it becomes (a bit) cooler','باب الإِبْرَادِ بِالظُّهْرِ فِي شِدَّةِ الْحَرِّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'When going on a journey, pray Zuhr prayer when it becomes cooler','باب الإِبْرَادِ بِالظُّهْرِ فِي السَّفَرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The time of Zuhr prayer is when the sun declines (just after mid-day)','باب وَقْتِ الظُّهْرِ عِنْدَ الزَّوَالِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To deny the Zuhr (prayer) up to the ''Asr (prayer) time','باب تَأْخِيرِ الظُّهْرِ إِلَى الْعَصْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The time of the Asr prayer','باب وَقْتِ الْعَصْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The sin of one who misses the ''Asr prayer (intentionally)','باب إِثْمِ مَنْ فَاتَتْهُ الْعَصْرُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One who omits (does not offer) the ''Asr prayer (intentionally)','باب مَنْ تَرَكَ الْعَصْرَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Superiority of the ''Asr prayer','باب فَضْلِ صَلاَةِ الْعَصْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever got (or was able to offer) only one Rak''a of the ''Asr prayer before sunset','باب مَنْ أَدْرَكَ رَكْعَةً مِنَ الْعَصْرِ قَبْلَ الْغُرُوبِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',9,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The time of the Maghrib prayer (evening prayer)','باب وَقْتِ الْمَغْرِبِ'),
