('sahih-al-bukhari',10,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The saying of a man to the Prophet (pbuh), "We have not prayed."','باب قَوْلِ الرَّجُلِ مَا صَلَّيْنَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the Imam is confronted with a problem after the Iqama','باب الإِمَامِ تَعْرِضُ لَهُ الْحَاجَةُ بَعْدَ الإِقَامَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To talk after the Iqama','باب الْكَلاَمِ إِذَا أُقِيمَتِ الصَّلاَةُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Congregational Salat (prayer) is obligatory.','باب وُجُوبِ صَلاَةِ الْجَمَاعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Superiority of the congregational Salat (prayer)','باب فَضْلِ صَلاَةِ الْجَمَاعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Superiority of the Fajr (early morning) prayer in congregation.','باب فَضْلِ صَلاَةِ الْفَجْرِ فِي جَمَاعَةٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of offering the Zuhr prayer early','باب فَضْلِ التَّهْجِيرِ إِلَى الظُّهْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Every step towards good deeds is rewarded','باب احْتِسَابِ الآثَارِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of the ''Isha'' prayer in congregation','باب فَضْلِ الْعِشَاءِ فِي الْجَمَاعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Two or more than two persons are considered as a group (for the congregational prayers)','باب اثْنَانِ فَمَا فَوْقَهُمَا جَمَاعَةٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(The reward of a person) who waits for As-Salat (the prayer) in the mosque and the superiority of mosques','باب مَنْ جَلَسَ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ يَنْتَظِرُ الصَّلاَةَ، وَفَضْلِ الْمَسَاجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of going to the mosque (every) morning and in the afternoon and evening [for the congregational Salat (prayers)]','باب فَضْلِ مَنْ غَدَا إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ وَمَنْ رَاحَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,38,'38',NULL,NULL,NULL,'No Salat (prayer) (is to be offered) except the compulsory Salat after the Iqama has been pronounced for that compulsory Salat','باب إِذَا أُقِيمَتِ الصَّلاَةُ فَلاَ صَلاَةَ إِلاَّ الْمَكْتُوبَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,39,'39',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The limit set for a patient to attend the congregational Salat (prayer)?','باب حَدِّ الْمَرِيضِ أَنْ يَشْهَدَ الْجَمَاعَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,40,'40',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to pray at one''s dwelling during rain or if there is a genuine excuse','باب الرُّخْصَةِ فِي الْمَطَرِ وَالْعِلَّةِ أَنْ يُصَلِّيَ فِي رَحْلِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Can the Imam offer the Salat (prayer) with only those who are present (for the prayer)? And can be deliver a Khutba (religious talk) on Friday if it is raining?','باب هَلْ يُصَلِّي الإِمَامُ بِمَنْ حَضَرَ وَهَلْ يَخْطُبُ يَوْمَ الْجُمُعَةِ فِي الْمَطَرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,42,'42',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(What should one do) if the meal has been served and the Iqama has been pronounced for As-Salat(the prayer)','باب إِذَا حَضَرَ الطَّعَامُ وَأُقِيمَتِ الصَّلاَةُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,43,'43',NULL,NULL,NULL,'When the Imam is called for As-Salat (the prayer) while he has in his hands something to eat.','باب إِذَا دُعِيَ الإِمَامُ إِلَى الصَّلاَةِ وَبِيَدِهِ مَا يَأْكُلُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,44,'44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If somebody was busy with his domestic work and Iqama was pronounced and then he came out [for offering the Salat (prayer)]','باب مَنْ كَانَ فِي حَاجَةِ أَهْلِهِ فَأُقِيمَتِ الصَّلاَةُ فَخَرَجَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,45,'45',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Offering Salat (prayer) in front of the people with the sole intention of teaching them the Salat of the Prophet (pbuh) and his Sunnah (legal ways etc.)','باب مَنْ صَلَّى بِالنَّاسِ وَهْوَ لاَ يُرِيدُ إِلاَّ أَنْ يُعَلِّمَهُمْ صَلاَةَ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَسُنَّتَهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,46,'46',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The religious learned men are entitled to precedence in leading the Salat (prayer)','باب أَهْلُ الْعِلْمِ وَالْفَضْلِ أَحَقُّ بِالإِمَامَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,47,'47',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever stood by the side of the Imam because of a genuine cause [in Salat (prayer)]','باب مَنْ قَامَ إِلَى جَنْبِ الإِمَامِ لِعِلَّةٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,48,'48',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If somebody is leading the Salat (prayer) and (in the meanwhile) the first (usual) Imam comes, the Salat is valid whether the former retreats or does not retreat','باب مَنْ دَخَلَ لِيَؤُمَّ النَّاسَ فَجَاءَ الإِمَامُ الأَوَّلُ فَتَأَخَّرَ الأَوَّلُ أَوْ لَمْ يَتَأَخَّرْ جَازَتْ صَلاَتُهُ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,49,'49',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If some people are equally proficient in the recitation of the Quran (and religious knowledge), the oldest of them should lead As-Salat (the prayer)','باب إِذَا اسْتَوَوْا فِي الْقِرَاءَةِ فَلْيَؤُمَّهُمْ أَكْبَرُهُمْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,50,'50',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the Imam visited some people and led them in Salat (prayer)','باب إِذَا زَارَ الإِمَامُ قَومًا فَأَمَّهُمْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,51,'51',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Imam is appointed to be followed','باب إِنَّمَا جُعِلَ الإِمَامُ لِيُؤْتَمَّ بِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,52,'52',NULL,NULL,NULL,'When should those who are behind the Imam prostrate?','باب مَتَى يَسْجُدُ مَنْ خَلْفَ الإِمَامِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,53,'53',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The sin of the one who raises his head before the Imam (raises his head)','باب إِثْمِ مَنْ رَفَعَ رَأْسَهُ قَبْلَ الإِمَامِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,54,'54',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A slave or a manumitted slave can lead the Salat (prayer)','باب إِمَامَةِ الْعَبْدِ وَالْمَوْلَى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,55,'55',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the Imam does not offer the Salat (prayer) perfectly and the followers offer it perfectly','باب إِذَا لَمْ يُتِمَّ الإِمَامُ وَأَتَمَّ مَنْ خَلْفَهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,56,'56',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Offering prayers behind a man who is a victim of Al-Fitan (trials and affections) or a heretic.','باب إِمَامَةِ الْمَفْتُونِ وَالْمُبْتَدِعِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,57,'57',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To stand on the right side of the Imam on the same line if only two persons (counting the Imam) are offering Salat (prayer) in congregation','باب يَقُومُ عَنْ يَمِينِ الإِمَامِ، بِحِذَائِهِ سَوَاءً إِذَا كَانَا اثْنَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,58,'58',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a man stood on the left side of the Imam and the Imam drew him to his right side, then the Salat of none of them would be invalid','باب إِذَا قَامَ الرَّجُلُ عَنْ يَسَارِ الإِمَامِ، فَحَوَّلَهُ الإِمَامُ إِلَى يَمِينِهِ لَمْ تَفْسُدْ صَلاَتُهُمَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,59,'59',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the Imam has not had the intention of leading the prayer and then some persons join him and he leads them','باب إِذَا لَمْ يَنْوِ الإِمَامُ أَنْ يَؤُمَّ ثُمَّ جَاءَ قَوْمٌ فَأَمَّهُمْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,60,'60',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the Imam prolongs the Salat (prayer) and somebody has an urgent work or need and so he leaves the congregation and offers Salat alone.','باب إِذَا طَوَّلَ الإِمَامُ وَكَانَ لِلرَّجُلِ حَاجَةٌ فَخَرَجَ فَصَلَّى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,61,'61',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The shortening of the Qiyam (standing) by the Imam[in Salat (prayer)] but performing the bowings and the prostrations perfectly','باب تَخْفِيفِ الإِمَامِ فِي الْقِيَامِ وَإِتْمَامِ الرُّكُوعِ وَالسُّجُودِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,62,'62',NULL,NULL,NULL,'When offering Salat (prayer) alone, one can prolong the Salat as much as one wishes','باب إِذَا صَلَّى لِنَفْسِهِ فَلْيُطَوِّلْ مَا شَاءَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,63,'63',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Complaining against one''s Imam if he prolongs the prayer.','باب مَنْ شَكَا إِمَامَهُ إِذَا طَوَّلَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,64,'64',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The shortening and perfection of the prayer (by the Imam)','باب الإِيجَازِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ وَإِكْمَالِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,65,'65',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever cuts short As-Salat (the prayer) on hearing the cries of a child.','باب مَنْ أَخَفَّ الصَّلاَةَ عِنْدَ بُكَاءِ الصَّبِيِّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,66,'66',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If one offers Salat (prayer) and the leads the people in Salat.','باب إِذَا صَلَّى ثُمَّ أَمَّ قَوْمًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,67,'67',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One who repeats the Takbir (Allahu Akbar) of the Imam so that the people may hear it.','باب مَنْ أَسْمَعَ النَّاسَ تَكْبِيرَ الإِمَامِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,68,'68',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a person follows the Imam and the others follow that person (then it is all right)','باب الرَّجُلُ يَأْتَمُّ بِالإِمَامِ وَيَأْتَمُّ النَّاسُ بِالْمَأْمُومِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,69,'69',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Can the Imam depend on the people''s saying if he is in doubt (about a certain matter)?','باب هَلْ يَأْخُذُ الإِمَامُ إِذَا شَكَّ بِقَوْلِ النَّاسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,70,'70',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the Imam weeps in As-Salat (the prayers) (will his Salat be valid?)','باب إِذَا بَكَى الإِمَامُ فِي الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,71,'71',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Straightening the rows at the time of Iqama and after it (immediately)','باب تَسْوِيَةِ الصُّفُوفِ عِنْدَ الإِقَامَةِ وَبَعْدَهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,72,'72',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Facing of the Imam towards his followers while straightening the rows.','باب إِقْبَالِ الإِمَامِ عَلَى النَّاسِ عِنْدَ تَسْوِيَةِ الصُّفُوفِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,73,'73',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The first row','باب الصَّفِّ الأَوَّلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,74,'74',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The straightening of the rows is amongst those obligatory and good things which make your As-Salat (the prayer) a correct and perfect one.','باب إِقَامَةِ الصَّفِّ مِنْ تَمَامِ الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,75,'75',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The sin of a person who does not complete the rows (who is out of alignment) for the prayer','باب إِثْمِ مَنْ لَمْ يُتِمَّ الصُّفُوفَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,76,'76',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To stand shoulder to shoulder and foot to foot in a row','باب إِلْزَاقِ الْمَنْكِبِ بِالْمَنْكِبِ وَالْقَدَمِ بِالْقَدَمِ فِي الصَّفِّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,77,'77',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a person stands by the left side of the Imam, and the Imam dress him to the right from behind, the Salat (prayer) is correct.','باب إِذَا قَامَ الرَّجُلُ عَنْ يَسَارِ الإِمَامِ، وَحَوَّلَهُ الإِمَامُ خَلْفَهُ إِلَى يَمِينِهِ، تَمَّتْ صَلاَتُهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,78,'78',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One woman can form a row','باب الْمَرْأَةُ وَحْدَهَا تَكُونُ صَفًّا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,79,'79',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The right side of the mosque and the place to the right of the Imam','باب مَيْمَنَةِ الْمَسْجِدِ وَالإِمَامِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,80,'80',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If there is a wall or a Sutra between the Imam and followers','باب إِذَا كَانَ بَيْنَ الإِمَامِ وَبَيْنَ الْقَوْمِ حَائِطٌ أَوْ سُتْرَةٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,81,'81',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The night prayer.','باب صَلاَةِ اللَّيْلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,82,'82',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The necessity of saying the Takbir, i.e., Allahu Akbar (Allah is the Most Great) and the commencement of As-Salat (the prayer)','باب إِيجَابِ التَّكْبِيرِ وَافْتِتَاحِ الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,83,'83',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To raise both hands on saying the first Takbir simultaneously with opening the Salat (prayer)','باب رَفْعِ الْيَدَيْنِ فِي التَّكْبِيرَةِ الأُولَى مَعَ الاِفْتِتَاحِ سَوَاءً'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,84,'84',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To raise both hands while saying the Takbir [on opening As-Salat (the prayer)], and while bowing and on raising up the head (after bowing)','باب رَفْعِ الْيَدَيْنِ إِذَا كَبَّرَ وَإِذَا رَكَعَ وَإِذَا رَفَعَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,85,'85',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To what level should one raise one''s hand.','باب إِلَى أَيْنَ يَرْفَعُ يَدَيْهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,86,'86',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To raise one''s hands after finishing the second Rak''a (on standing for the third Rak''a)','باب رَفْعِ الْيَدَيْنِ إِذَا قَامَ مِنَ الرَّكْعَتَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,87,'87',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To place the right hand on the left [in As-Salt (the prayers)]','باب وَضْعِ الْيُمْنَى عَلَى الْيُسْرَى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,88,'88',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Submissiveness in As-Salat (the prayer)','باب الْخُشُوعِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,89,'89',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What to say after the Takbir','باب مَا يَقُولُ بَعْدَ التَّكْبِيرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,90,'90',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,91,'91',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To cast a look at the Imam during As-Salat (the prayer)','باب رَفْعِ الْبَصَرِ إِلَى الإِمَامِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,92,'92',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Looking towards the sky during As-Salat (the prayer)','باب رَفْعِ الْبَصَرِ إِلَى السَّمَاءِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,93,'93',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To look hither and thither in As-Salat (the prayer)','باب الاِلْتِفَاتِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,94,'94',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Is it permissible to one to look around in Salat (prayer) if something happens to one? Or can one look at something like expectoration in the directn of the Qiblah?','باب هَلْ يَلْتَفِتُ لأَمْرٍ يَنْزِلُ بِهِ أَوْ يَرَى شَيْئًا أَوْ بُصَاقًا فِي الْقِبْلَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,95,'95',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Recitation of the Qur''an (Surat Al-Fatiha) is compulsory for the Imam and the followers, at the home and on journey, in all As-Salat (the prayers) whether the recitation is done silently or aloud.','باب وُجُوبِ الْقِرَاءَةِ لِلإِمَامِ وَالْمَأْمُومِ فِي الصَّلَوَاتِ كُلِّهَا فِي الْحَضَرِ وَالسَّفَرِ وَمَا يُجْهَرُ فِيهَا وَمَا يُخَافَتُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,96,'96',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The recitation of the Qur''an in a Zuhr prayer','باب الْقِرَاءَةِ فِي الظُّهْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,97,'97',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The recitation of the Qur''an in the ''Asr prayer','باب الْقِرَاءَةِ فِي الْعَصْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,98,'98',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The recitation of the Qur''an in the Magrib prayer','باب الْقِرَاءَةِ فِي الْمَغْرِبِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,99,'99',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To recite aloud in the Maghrib prayer.','باب الْجَهْرِ فِي الْمَغْرِبِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,100,'100',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To recite aloud in the ''Isha'' prayer.','باب الْجَهْرِ فِي الْعِشَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,101,'101',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To recite in the ''Isha prayer, with As-Sajda(prostration)','باب الْقِرَاءَةِ فِي الْعِشَاءِ بِالسَّجْدَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,102,'102',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Recitation in the ''Isha prayer','باب الْقِرَاءَةِ فِي الْعِشَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,103,'103',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Prolonging the first two Rak''a and shortening the last two','باب يُطَوِّلُ فِي الأُولَيَيْنِ وَيَحْذِفُ فِي الأُخْرَيَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,104,'104',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The recitation of the Qur''an in the Fajr prayer','باب الْقِرَاءَةِ فِي الْفَجْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,105,'105',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To recite aloud in the Fajr (early morning) prayer.','باب الْجَهْرِ بِقِرَاءَةِ صَلاَةِ الْفَجْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,106,'106',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To recite two Surah in one Rak''a and to recite the last verses of some Surah, or to elite the Surah in their reverse order, or to recite the beginning of a Surah','باب الْجَمْعِ بَيْنَ السُّورَتَيْنِ فِي الرَّكْعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,107,'107',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To recite only Surah Al-Fathiha in the last two Rak''a during a four Rak''a Salat (prayer)','باب يَقْرَأُ فِي الأُخْرَيَيْنِ بِفَاتِحَةِ الْكِتَابِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,108,'108',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To recite (the Qur''an) quietly in the Zuhr and ''Asr prayers','باب مَنْ خَافَتَ الْقِرَاءَةَ فِي الظُّهْرِ وَالْعَصْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,109,'109',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(In a quiet prayer) if the Imam recites a Verse or so audibly','باب إِذَا أَسْمَعَ الإِمَامُ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,110,'110',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To prolong the first Rak''a','باب يُطَوِّلُ فِي الرَّكْعَةِ الأُولَى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,111,'111',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Saying of Amin aloud by the Imam','باب جَهْرِ الإِمَامِ بِالتَّأْمِينِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,112,'112',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Superiority of saying Amin','باب فَضْلِ التَّأْمِينِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,113,'113',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Saying of Amin aloud by the followers','باب جَهْرِ الْمَأْمُومِ بِالتَّأْمِينِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,114,'114',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If someone bowed behind the rows, [on entering the mosque and before joining the rows of Salat (prayer)]','باب إِذَا رَكَعَ دُونَ الصَّفِّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,115,'115',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Itmam At-Takbir (i.e., to end the number of Takbir or to say the Takbir perfectly) on bowing. [See Fath Al-Bari]','باب إِتْمَامِ التَّكْبِيرِ فِي الرُّكُوعِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,116,'116',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Itmam At-Takbir (i.e., to end the number of Takbir, or to say the Takbir perfectly) on prostrating. [See Fath Al-Bari]','باب إِتْمَامِ التَّكْبِيرِ فِي السُّجُودِ'),
