('sahih-al-bukhari',10,130,'130',NULL,NULL,NULL,'During the prostrations one should keep one''s arms away from one''s sides and the abdomen should be kept away from the thighs.','باب يُبْدِي ضَبْعَيْهِ وَيُجَافِي فِي السُّجُودِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,131,'131',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One should keep the toes in the direction of the Qiblah','بَابُ يَسْتَقْبِلُ بِأَطْرَافِ رِجْلَيْهِ الْقِبْلَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,132,'132',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If one does not perform the prostrations perfectly','باب إِذَا لَمْ يُتِمَّ السُّجُودَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,133,'133',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To prostrate on seven bones','باب السُّجُودِ عَلَى سَبْعَةِ أَعْظُمٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,134,'134',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To prostrate on the nose','باب السُّجُودِ عَلَى الأَنْفِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,135,'135',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To prostrate on the nose and in the mud','باب السُّجُودِ عَلَى الأَنْفِ وَالسُّجُودِ عَلَى الطِّينِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,136,'136',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To tie the clothes and wrap them properly [in Salat (prayer)]; and whoever gathered his clothes for fear that his private parts may become exposed.','باب عَقْدِ الثِّيَابِ وَشَدِّهَا وَمَنْ ضَمَّ إِلَيْهِ ثَوْبَهُ إِذَا خَافَ أَنْ تَنْكَشِفَ عَوْرَتُهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,137,'137',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One should not tuck put the hair [during Salat (prayers)]','باب لاَ يَكُفُّ شَعَرًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,138,'138',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One should not tuck up his garment in As-Salat (the prayer)','باب لاَ يَكُفُّ ثَوْبَهُ فِي الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,139,'139',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To invoke and glorify Allah in prostration','باب التَّسْبِيحِ وَالدُّعَاءِ فِي السُّجُودِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,140,'140',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To sit for a while between the two prostrations','باب الْمُكْثِ بَيْنَ السَّجْدَتَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,141,'141',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One should not put the forearms on the ground during prostrations','باب لاَ يَفْتَرِشُ ذِرَاعَيْهِ فِي السُّجُودِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,142,'142',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sitting Straight in a Witr payer (i.e., an odd Rak''a) and then getting up.','باب مَنِ اسْتَوَى قَاعِدًا فِي وِتْرٍ مِنْ صَلاَتِهِ ثُمَّ نَهَضَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,143,'143',NULL,NULL,NULL,'How to support oneself on the ground while standing after finishing the Rak''a (after the two prostrations)','باب كَيْفَ يَعْتَمِدُ عَلَى الأَرْضِ إِذَا قَامَ مِنَ الرَّكْعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,144,'144',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Saying Takbir on rising from the two prostrations','باب يُكَبِّرُ وَهْوَ يَنْهَضُ مِنَ السَّجْدَتَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,145,'145',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prophet''s Sunna (legal way) for the sitting in the Tashah-hud [in the Salat (prayer)].','باب سُنَّةِ الْجُلُوسِ فِي التَّشَهُّدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,146,'146',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever considered that the first Tashah-hud is not compulsory','باب مَنْ لَمْ يَرَ التَّشَهُّدَ الأَوَّلَ وَاجِبًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,147,'147',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(Saying of the) Tashah-hud in the first sitting.','باب التَّشَهُّدِ فِي الأُولَى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,148,'148',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(Saying of the) Tashah-hud in the last Rak''a','باب التَّشَهُّدِ فِي الآخِرَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,149,'149',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Invocation before the Taslim','باب الدُّعَاءِ قَبْلَ السَّلاَمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,150,'150',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What optional invocation may be selected after the Tashah-hud, and it is not obligatory.','باب مَا يُتَخَيَّرُ مِنَ الدُّعَاءِ بَعْدَ التَّشَهُّدِ وَلَيْسَ بِوَاجِبٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,151,'151',NULL,NULL,NULL,'No cleaning (rubbing) one''s forehead and nose till one has completed As-Salat (the prayer)','باب مَنْ لَمْ يَمْسَحْ جَبْهَتَهُ وَأَنْفَهُ حَتَّى صَلَّى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,152,'152',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Taslim [turning the face to the right and then to the left and saying "As-Salamu alikum wa rah mat-ullah" at the end of the Salat (prayers)]','باب التَّسْلِيمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,153,'153',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To finish the Salat (prayer) with Taslim along with the Imam','باب يُسَلِّمُ حِينَ يُسَلِّمُ الإِمَامُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,154,'154',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever did not say (a Taslim) in addition to the Taslim of the Imam but thought that Taslim of the Salat (prayer) was sufficient','باب مَنْ لَمْ يَرَ رَدَّ السَّلاَمِ عَلَى الإِمَامِ وَاكْتَفَى بِتَسْلِيمِ الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,155,'155',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Dhikr (remembering Allah by Glorifying, Praising and Magnifying Him) after As-Salat (the prayer)','باب الذِّكْرِ بَعْدَ الصَّلاَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,156,'156',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Imam should face the followers after finishing the prayer with Taslim.','باب يَسْتَقْبِلُ الإِمَامُ النَّاسَ إِذَا سَلَّمَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,157,'157',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The staying of the Imam at his Musalla (praying place) after (finishing the prayer with) Taslim','باب مُكْثِ الإِمَامِ فِي مُصَلاَّهُ بَعْدَ السَّلاَمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,158,'158',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever led the people in Salat (prayer) and remembered an rent matter or necessity and had to pass over the people (to carry out that)','باب مَنْ صَلَّى بِالنَّاسِ فَذَكَرَ حَاجَةً فَتَخَطَّاهُمْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,159,'159',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To leave or depart from the right and from the left after finishing from the Salat (prayers).','باب الاِنْفِتَالِ وَالاِنْصِرَافِ عَنِ الْيَمِينِ، وَالشِّمَالِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,160,'160',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What has been said about uncooked garlic, onion and leek.','باب مَا جَاءَ فِي الثُّومِ النَّىِّ وَالْبَصَلِ وَالْكُرَّاثِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,161,'161',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The ablution for boys (youngsters). When they should perform Ghusl (take a bath) and Tuhur (purification). Their attendance at congregational prayers and their rows in the prayers.','باب وُضُوءِ الصِّبْيَانِ, وَمَتَى يَجِبُ عَلَيْهِمُ الْغَسْلُ وَالطُّهُورُ وَحُضُورِهِمِ الْجَمَاعَةَ وَالْعِيدَيْنِ وَالْجَنَائِزَ وَصُفُوفِهِمْ.'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,162,'162',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Going of women to the mosque at night and in darkness','باب خُرُوجِ النِّسَاءِ إِلَى الْمَسَاجِدِ بِاللَّيْلِ وَالْغَلَسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,163,'163',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The waiting of the people for the religious learned Imam to get up (after the prayer to depart)','باب انْتِظَارِ النَّاسِ قِيَامَ الإِمَامِ الْعَالِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,164,'164',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Salat (prayer) of women behind men','باب صَلاَةِ النِّسَاءِ خَلْفَ الرِّجَالِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,165,'165',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Returning of the women immediately after the Fajr prayer and their staying in the mosque for a short period only','باب سُرْعَةِ انْصِرَافِ النِّسَاءِ مِنَ الصُّبْحِ، وَقِلَّةِ مَقَامِهِنَّ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,166,'166',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A women shall ask her husband''s permission (on wishing) to go to the mosque.','باب اسْتِئْذَانِ الْمَرْأَةِ زَوْجَهَا بِالْخُرُوجِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',10,167,'166',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Women praying behind men','باب صَلاَةِ النِّسَاءِ خَلْفَ الرِّجَالِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prescription of Friday [Salat-ul-Jumu''ah (Jumu''ah prayer)] and Khutba (religious talk) according to the Statement of Allah تعالى: "When the call is proclaimed for the Salat (prayer) of Friday (Jumu''ah prayer) come to the remembrance of Allah [Jumu''ah religious talk (Khutba) and Salat (prayer)] and leave off business (and every other thing)." (V.62:9)','باب فَرْضِ الْجُمُعَةِ لِقَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {إِذَا نُودِيَ لِلصَّلاَةِ مِنْ يَوْمِ الْجُمُعَةِ فَاسْعَوْا إِلَى ذِكْرِ اللَّهِ وَذَرُوا الْبَيْعَ ذَلِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ}.'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of taking a bath on friday','باب فَضْلِ الْغُسْلِ يَوْمَ الْجُمُعَةِ، وَهَلْ عَلَى الصَّبِيِّ شُهُودُ يَوْمِ الْجُمُعَةِ أَوْ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To perfume before going for the Friday (prayer)','باب الطِّيبِ لِلْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of Jumu''ah (prayer and Khutba)','باب فَضْلِ الْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To use (hair) oil for the Friday prayer','باب الدُّهْنِ لِلْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To wear the best clothes (for the Jumu''ah prayer)','باب يَلْبَسُ أَحْسَنَ مَا يَجِدُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To clean the teeth with Siwak on Friday','باب السِّوَاكِ يَوْمَ الْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever cleans his teeth with Siwak','باب مَنْ تَسَوَّكَ بِسِوَاكِ غَيْرِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What should be recited in the Fajr prayer on Friday','باب مَا يُقْرَأُ فِي صَلاَةِ الْفَجْرِ يَوْمَ الْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To offer Jumu''ah prayer and Khutba in villages and towns','باب الْجُمُعَةِ فِي الْقُرَى وَالْمُدْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Is the bath necessary for those who do not present themselves for the Jumu''ah prayer','باب هَلْ عَلَى مَنْ لَمْ يَشْهَدِ الْجُمُعَةَ غُسْلٌ مِنَ النِّسَاءِ وَالصِّبْيَانِ وَغَيْرِهِمْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Not to attend the Jumu''ah (prayer) if it is raining.','باب الرُّخْصَةِ إِنْ لَمْ يَحْضُرِ الْجُمُعَةَ فِي الْمَطَرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'For whom is the Jumu''ah (prayer) compulsory?','بَابُ مِنْ أَيْنَ تُؤْتَى الْجُمُعَةُ، وَعَلَى مَنْ تَجِبُ؟'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The time for the Jumu''ah (prayer) is due when the sun declines (i.e. just after mid-day)','باب وَقْتُ الْجُمُعَةِ إِذَا زَالَتِ الشَّمْسُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If it becomes very hot on Fridays','باب إِذَا اشْتَدَّ الْحَرُّ يَوْمَ الْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To go walking unhurriedly','باب الْمَشْىِ إِلَى الْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One should not separate two persons on Fridays','باب لاَ يُفَرَّقُ بَيْنَ اثْنَيْنِ يَوْمَ الْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A man should not make his brother get up to sit in his place','باب لاَ يُقِيمُ الرَّجُلُ أَخَاهُ يَوْمَ الْجُمُعَةِ وَيَقْعُدُ فِي مَكَانِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Adhan on Friday (for the Jumu''ah prayer)','باب الأَذَانِ يَوْمَ الْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One Mu''adh-dhin on Friday','باب الْمُؤَذِّنِ الْوَاحِدِ يَوْمَ الْجُمُعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Imam repeats the wordings of the Adhan when he hears it','باب يُؤَذِّنُ الإِمَامُ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ إِذَا سَمِعَ النِّدَاءَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To sit on the pulpit while Adhan is pronounced','باب الْجُلُوسِ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ عِنْدَ التَّأْذِينِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Adhan before delivering the Khutba','باب التَّأْذِينِ عِنْدَ الْخُطْبَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',11,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(To deliver) the Khutba on the pulpit','باب الْخُطْبَةِ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ'),
