('sahih-al-bukhari',27,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Statement of Allah تعالى: "...Then he should not have sexual relations (with his wife) ..." (V.2:197)','باب قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى ‏ {‏فَلاَ رَفَثَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',27,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Statement of Allah عز وجل "...nor commit sin nor dispute unjustly during Hajj..." (V.2:197)','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: {وَلاَ فُسُوقَ وَلاَ جِدَالَ فِي الْحَجِّ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The penalty for hunting (by a Muhrim). And the Statement of Allah تعالى: "...Kill not game while you are in the state of Ihram for Hajj or Umra (pilgrimage), and whosoever of you kills it intentionally, the penalty is an offering, brought to the Ka''bah, of an eatable animal (i.e., sheep, goat, cow, etc.) brought to the Ka''bah, equivalent to the one he killed... to the end of the Verse... And fear Allah to Whom you shall be gathered back." (V.5:95-96).','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {لاَ تَقْتُلُوا الصَّيْدَ وَأَنْتُمْ حُرُمٌ وَمَنْ قَتَلَهُ مِنْكُمْ مُتَعَمِّدًا فَجَزَاءٌ مِثْلُ مَا قَتَلَ مِنَ النَّعَمِ يَحْكُمُ بِهِ ذَوَا عَدْلٍ مِنْكُمْ هَدْيًا بَالِغَ الْكَعْبَةِ أَوْ كَفَّارَةٌ طَعَامُ مَسَاكِينَ أَوْ عَدْلُ ذَلِكَ صِيَامًا لِيَذُوقَ وَبَالَ أَمْرِهِ عَفَا اللَّهُ عَمَّا سَلَفَ وَمَنْ عَادَ فَيَنْتَقِمُ اللَّهُ مِنْهُ وَاللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ ذُو انْتِقَامٍ أُحِلَّ لَكُمْ صَيْدُ الْبَحْرِ وَطَعَامُهُ مَتَاعًا لَكُمْ وَلِلسَّيَّارَةِ وَحُرِّمَ عَلَيْكُمْ صَيْدُ الْبَرِّ مَا دُمْتُمْ حُرُمًا وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ الَّذِي إِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُونَ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a non-Muhrim hunts (an animal) and gives it as a present to a Muhrim, (it is permissible for) the latter to eat it','باب إِذَا صَادَ الْحَلاَلُ فَأَهْدَى لِلْمُحْرِمِ الصَّيْدَ أَكَلَهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the Muhrimun saw game and laughed and a non-Muhrim understood, they are allowed to eat the game','باب إِذَا رَأَى الْمُحْرِمُونَ صَيْدًا فَضَحِكُوا فَفَطِنَ الْحَلاَلُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A Muhrim should not help a non-Muhrim in the hunting of a game','باب لاَ يُعِينُ الْمُحْرِمُ الْحَلاَلَ فِي قَتْلِ الصَّيْدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A Muhrim should not point at a game','باب لاَ يُشِيرُ الْمُحْرِمُ إِلَى الصَّيْدِ لِكَىْ يَصْطَادَهُ الْحَلاَلُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a person gave onager to a Muhrim then he should not accept it','باب إِذَا أَهْدَى لِلْمُحْرِمِ حِمَارًا وَحْشِيًّا حَيًّا لَمْ يَقْبَلْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(What kind of) animals can be killed by a Muhrim','باب مَا يَقْتُلُ الْمُحْرِمُ مِنَ الدَّوَابِّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is not permissible to cut the trees of the Haram','باب لاَ يُعْضَدُ شَجَرُ الْحَرَمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The game in the Haram should not be chased','باب لاَ يُنَفَّرُ صَيْدُ الْحَرَمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Fighting is prohibited in Makkah','باب لاَ يَحِلُّ الْقِتَالُ بِمَكَّةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Cupping for a Muhrim','باب الْحِجَامَةِ لِلْمُحْرِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The marrying of Muhrim','باب تَزْوِيجِ الْمُحْرِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What is forbidden for a Muhrim as regards perfumes','باب مَا يُنْهَى مِنَ الطِّيبِ لِلْمُحْرِمِ وَالْمُحْرِمَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The taking of a bath by a Muhrim','باب الاِغْتِسَالِ لِلْمُحْرِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wearing of Khuff by a Muhrim if slippers are not available','باب لُبْسِ الْخُفَّيْنِ لِلْمُحْرِمِ إِذَا لَمْ يَجِدِ النَّعْلَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If an Izar is not available, one can wear trousers','باب إِذَا لَمْ يَجِدِ الإِزَارَ فَلْيَلْبَسِ السَّرَاوِيلَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Carrying of arms by a Muhrim','باب لُبْسِ السِّلاَحِ لِلْمُحْرِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Entering the Haram and Makkah without Ihram','باب دُخُولِ الْحَرَمِ وَمَكَّةَ بِغَيْرِ إِحْرَامٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If somebody ignorantly assumed Ihram while wearing a shirt (will Fidya be compulsory?)','باب إِذَا أَحْرَمَ جَاهِلاً وَعَلَيْهِ قَمِيصٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A Muhrim died at ''Arafat and the Prophet (saws) did not order anybody to finish the remaining ceremonies of Hajj on his behalf','باب الْمُحْرِمِ يَمُوتُ بِعَرَفَةَ وَلَمْ يَأْمُرِ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يُؤَدَّى عَنْهُ بَقِيَّةُ الْحَجِّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The legal way of (burying) a dead Muhrim','باب سُنَّةِ الْمُحْرِمِ إِذَا مَاتَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To perform Hajj on behalf of a dead person. A man can perform Hajj on behalf of a woman','باب الْحَجِّ وَالنُّذُورِ عَنِ الْمَيِّتِ وَالرَّجُلُ يَحُجُّ عَنِ الْمَرْأَةِ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Performing Hajj for a person who cannot sit firmly on the mount','باب الْحَجِّ عَمَّنْ لاَ يَسْتَطِيعُ الثُّبُوتَ عَلَى الرَّاحِلَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Performing Hajj by a woman on behalf of a man','باب حَجِّ الْمَرْأَةِ عَنِ الرَّجُلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Hajj of boys (children etc.)','باب حَجِّ الصِّبْيَانِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hajj of women','باب حَجِّ النِّسَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',28,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever vowed to go on foot to the Ka''bah','باب مَنْ نَذَرَ الْمَشْىَ إِلَى الْكَعْبَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Haram (sanctuary) of Al-Madina','باب حَرَمِ الْمَدِينَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Superiority of Al-Madina. It expels (evil) persons','باب فَضْلِ الْمَدِينَةِ، وَأَنَّهَا تَنْفِي النَّاسَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Madina is also called Taba','باب الْمَدِينَةُ طَابَةُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The two mountains of Al-Madina','باب لاَبَتَىِ الْمَدِينَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The one who avoids living in Al-Madina?','باب مَنْ رَغِبَ عَنِ الْمَدِينَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Iman (Belief) returns and goes back to Al-Madina','باب الإِيمَانُ يَأْرِزُ إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sin of that person who harms the people of Al-Madina','باب إِثْمِ مَنْ كَادَ أَهْلَ الْمَدِينَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The high buildings of Al-Madina','باب آطَامِ الْمَدِينَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Ad-Dajjal will not be able to enter Al-Madina','باب لاَ يَدْخُلُ الدَّجَّالُ الْمَدِينَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Madina expels all the evil and bad persons','باب الْمَدِينَةُ تَنْفِي الْخَبَثَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,11,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,12,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The dislike of the Prophet (saws) that Al-Madina should be vacated','باب كَرَاهِيَةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم أَنْ تُعْرَى الْمَدِينَةُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',29,13,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Fasting is obligatory in (the month of) Ramadan','باب وُجُوبِ صَوْمِ رَمَضَانَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of As-Saum (the fasting)','باب فَضْلِ الصَّوْمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'As-Saum (the fasting) is an expiation (for sins)','باب الصَّوْمُ كَفَّارَةٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Ar-Raiyan is for people observing Saum','باب الرَّيَّانُ لِلصَّائِمِينَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Should it be said "Ramadan" or "the month of Ramadan"? And whoever thinks that both are permissible','باب هَلْ يُقَالُ رَمَضَانُ أَوْ شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ وَمَنْ رَأَى كُلَّهُ وَاسِعًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever observed fast in Ramadan out of sincere Faith with honest intention','باب مَنْ صَامَ رَمَضَانَ إِيمَانًا وَاحْتِسَابًا وَنِيَّةً'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prophet saws used to be most generous in the month of Ramadan','باب أَجْوَدُ مَا كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم يَكُونُ فِي رَمَضَانَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever does not give up lying speech while observing Saum','باب مَنْ لَمْ يَدَعْ قَوْلَ الزُّورِ وَالْعَمَلَ بِهِ فِي الصَّوْمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Should one say, "I am observing Saum (fast)" on being abused?','باب هَلْ يَقُولُ إِنِّي صَائِمٌ إِذَا شُتِمَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'As-Saum for those who fear committing illegal sexual acts','باب الصَّوْمِ لِمَنْ خَافَ عَلَى نَفْسِهِ الْعُزْبَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"Start observing Saum on seeing the crescent of Ramadan, and stop on seeing the crescent (of Shawwal)."','بَابُ قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: «إِذَا رَأَيْتُمُ الْهِلاَلَ فَصُومُوا وَإِذَا رَأَيْتُمُوهُ فَأَفْطِرُوا»'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The two months of Eid do not decrease','باب شَهْرَا عِيدٍ لاَ يَنْقُصَانِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"We neither write nor know accounts."','باب قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏"‏ لاَ نَكْتُبُ وَلاَ نَحْسُبُ ‏"‏‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Not to observe Saum for a day or two ahead of Ramadan','باب لاَ يَتَقَدَّمَنَّ رَمَضَانَ بِصَوْمِ يَوْمٍ وَلاَ يَوْمَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Statement of Allah عز وجل: "It is made lawful for you to have sexual relations with your wives on the night of the As-Saum (the fasts). They are Libas, for you, and you are the same for them. Allah knows that you used to deceive yourselves, so He turned to you (accepted your repentance) and forgave you. So, now have sexual relations with them and seek that which Allah has ordained for you (offspring)…” (V.2:187)','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ جَلَّ ذِكْرُهُ: {أُحِلَّ لَكُمْ لَيْلَةَ الصِّيَامِ الرَّفَثُ إِلَى نِسَائِكُمْ هُنَّ لِبَاسٌ لَكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ لِبَاسٌ لَهُنَّ عَلِمَ اللَّهُ أَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَخْتَانُونَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ فَتَابَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَعَفَا عَنْكُمْ فَالآنَ بَاشِرُوهُنَّ وَابْتَغُوا مَا كَتَبَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Statement of Allah Taa''la: "And eat and drink until the white thread of dawn appears to you distinct from the black."','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {وَكُلُوا وَاشْرَبُوا حَتَّى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكُمُ الْخَيْطُ الأَبْيَضُ مِنَ الْخَيْطِ الأَسْوَدِ مِنَ الْفَجْرِ ثُمَّ أَتِمُّوا الصِّيَامَ إِلَى اللَّيْلِ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"The Adhan of Bilal should not stop you from taking Sahur"','باب قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏"‏ لاَ يَمْنَعَنَّكُمْ مِنْ سَحُورِكُمْ أَذَانُ بِلاَلٍ ‏"‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Taking the Sahur hurriedly (shortly before dawn)','باب تَأْخِيرِ السَّحُورِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Interval between the Sahur and Salat-ul-Fajr','باب قَدْرِ كَمْ بَيْنَ السَّحُورِ وَصَلاَةِ الْفَجْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sahur is a blessing but it is not compulsory','باب بَرَكَةِ السَّحُورِ مِنْ غَيْرِ إِيجَابٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the intention of Saum was made in the daytime.','باب إِذَا نَوَى بِالنَّهَارِ صَوْمًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a person observing Saum gets up in the morning in the state of Janaba','باب الصَّائِمِ يُصْبِحُ جُنُبًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To embrace while one is observing Saum (fast)','باب الْمُبَاشَرَةِ لِلصَّائِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kissing by a fasting person','باب الْقُبْلَةِ لِلصَّائِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Taking a bath by a person observing Saum (fast)','باب اغْتِسَالِ الصَّائِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a person observing Saum ate or drank forgetfully','باب الصَّائِمِ إِذَا أَكَلَ أَوْ شَرِبَ نَاسِيًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Siwak for the person observing Saum (fast)','باب سِوَاكِ الرَّطْبِ وَالْيَابِسِ لِلصَّائِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"Whoever performs ablution should put water in his nose and then blow it out."','بَابُ قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: «إِذَا تَوَضَّأَ فَلْيَسْتَنْشِقْ بِمَنْخِرِهِ الْمَاءَ». وَلَمْ يُمَيِّزْ بَيْنَ الصَّائِمِ وَغَيْرِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sexual intercourse with wife in Ramadan.','باب إِذَا جَامَعَ فِي رَمَضَانَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Sexual intercourse with wife in Ramadan and the expiation of that.','باب إِذَا جَامَعَ فِي رَمَضَانَ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُ شَىْءٌ فَتُصُدِّقَ عَلَيْهِ فَلْيُكَفِّرْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To feed family from sin expiation (kaffarah) if they are needy.','باب الْمُجَامِعِ فِي رَمَضَانَ هَلْ يُطْعِمُ أَهْلَهُ مِنَ الْكَفَّارَةِ إِذَا كَانُوا مَحَاوِيجَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Cupping and vomiting in Saum (fast)','باب الْحِجَامَةِ وَالْقَىْءِ لِلصَّائِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To observe Saum (fast) or not during journeys','باب الصَّوْمِ فِي السَّفَرِ وَالإِفْطَارِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a person observed Saum for some days and then went on a journey.','باب إِذَا صَامَ أَيَّامًا مِنْ رَمَضَانَ ثُمَّ سَافَرَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is not righteousness to observe Saum on a journey','بَابُ قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِمَنْ ظُلِّلَ عَلَيْهِ، وَاشْتَدَّ الْحَرُّ: «لَيْسَ مِنَ الْبِرِّ الصَّوْمُ فِي السَّفَرِ»'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Not to criticize each other for observing Saum or not (on journeys)','باب لَمْ يَعِبْ أَصْحَابُ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم بَعْضُهُمْ بَعْضًا فِي الصَّوْمِ وَالإِفْطَارِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,38,'38',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever broke his Saum (fast) on a journey (publicly).','باب مَنْ أَفْطَرَ فِي السَّفَرِ لِيَرَاهُ النَّاسُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,39,'39',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(The Statement of Allah تعالى): “And as for those who can fast with difficulty (e.g. the aged etc.) they have (a choice either to fast or) to feed a Miskin (poor person) (for every day).” (V.2:184)','بَابُ: {وَعَلَى الَّذِينَ يُطِيقُونَهُ فِدْيَةٌ طَعَامُ مِسْكِينٍ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,40,'40',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To make up for the missed days of fasting','باب مَتَى يُقْضَى قَضَاءُ رَمَضَانَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The menstruating should leave the Saum and Salat','باب الْحَائِضِ تَتْرُكُ الصَّوْمَ وَالصَّلاَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,42,'42',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Can somebody else observe Saum instead of the dead?','باب مَنْ مَاتَ وَعَلَيْهِ صَوْمٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,43,'43',NULL,NULL,NULL,'When to break the Saum (fast)?','باب مَتَى يَحِلُّ فِطْرُ الصَّائِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,44,'44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Iftar (to break the Saum (fast))','باب يُفْطِرُ بِمَا تَيَسَّرَ عَلَيْهِ بِالْمَاءِ وَغَيْرِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,45,'45',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To hasten the Iftar','باب تَعْجِيلِ الإِفْطَارِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,46,'46',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If somebody breaks the Saum thinking that the sun has set','باب إِذَا أَفْطَرَ فِي رَمَضَانَ ثُمَّ طَلَعَتِ الشَّمْسُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,47,'47',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Saum (fasting) of boys (children etc.)','باب صَوْمِ الصِّبْيَانِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,48,'48',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To observe Saum (fast) continuously','باب الْوِصَالِ، وَمَنْ قَالَ لَيْسَ فِي اللَّيْلِ صِيَامٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',30,49,'49',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The punishment for the person who practises Al-Wisal very often.','باب التَّنْكِيلِ لِمَنْ أَكْثَرَ الْوِصَالَ'),
