('sahih-al-bukhari',64,83,'82',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The letter of the Prophet (saws) to Kisra (Khosrau) and Qaiser (Caesar)','باب كِتَابِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم إِلَى كِسْرَى وَقَيْصَرَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',64,84,'83',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The sickness of the Prophet (saws) and his death','بَابُ مَرَضِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَوَفَاتِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',64,85,'84',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The last statement, the Prophet (saws) spoke','باب آخِرِ مَا تَكَلَّمَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',64,86,'85',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The death of the Prophet (saws)','باب وَفَاةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',64,87,'86',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',64,88,'87',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The dispatch of Usama bin Zaid رضي الله عنهما by the Prophet (saws) during his fatal illness','باب بَعْثُ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم أُسَامَةَ بْنَ زَيْدٍ ـ رضى الله عنهما ـ فِي مَرَضِهِ الَّذِيتُوُفِّيَ فِيهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',64,89,'88',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',64,90,'89',NULL,NULL,NULL,'How many Ghazawat the Prophet (saws) fought','باب كَمْ غَزَا النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,1,'1',1,'Surat al-Fatiha (The Opening)','سورة الْفَاتِحَةِ','What has been said about Fãtihat al-Kitab (i.e., the Opening of the Book)','باب مَا جَاءَ فِي فَاتِحَةِ الْكِتَابِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,2,'2',1,'Surat al-Fatiha (The Opening)','سورة الْفَاتِحَةِ','"...Not (the way) of those who earned Your Anger, nor of those who went astray." (V.1:7)','باب ‏ {‏غَيْرِ الْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلاَ الضَّالِّينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,3,'1',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah: “And He taught Adam all the names (of everything)..." (V.2:31)','باب قَوْلِ اللَّهِ ‏ {‏وَعَلَّمَ آدَمَ الأَسْمَاءَ كُلَّهَا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,4,'2',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ',NULL,'بَابٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,5,'3',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah "...Then do not set up rivals unto Allah (in  worship) while you know (that He Alone has the right to be worshipped)..." (V.2:22)','باب قَوْلُهُ تَعَالَى ‏ {‏فَلاَ تَجْعَلُوا لِلَّهِ أَنْدَادًا وَأَنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,6,'4',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And We shaded with clouds and sent down on you Al-Manna and the quail,... (up to) wronged themselves." (V.2:57)','باب وَقَوْلُهُ تَعَالَى ‏ {‏وَظَلَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْغَمَامَ وَأَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوَى كُلُوا مِنْ طَيِّبَاتِ مَا رَزَقْنَاكُمْ وَمَا ظَلَمُونَا وَلَكِنْ كَانُوا أَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,7,'5',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And (remember) when We said: Enter this town (Jerusalem) and eat bountifully therein with pleasure and delight wherever you wish..." (V.2:58)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِذْ قُلْنَا ادْخُلُوا هَذِهِ الْقَرْيَةَ فَكُلُوا مِنْهَا حَيْثُ شِئْتُمْ رَغَدًا وَادْخُلُوا الْبَابَ سُجَّدًا وَقُولُوا حِطَّةٌ نَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ خَطَايَاكُمْ وَسَنَزِيدُ الْمُحْسِنِينَ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,8,'6',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"Whoever is an enemy to Jibril (Gabriel)..." (V.2:97)','باب قَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏مَنْ كَانَ عَدُوًّا لِجِبْرِيلَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,9,'7',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','His Statement: "Whatever a Verse (revelation) do We abrogate or cause to be forgotten, We bring a better one or similar to it..." (V.2:106)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏مَا نَنْسَخْ مِنْ آيَةٍ أَوْ نَنْسَأْهَا‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,10,'8',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And they (pagans, Jews and Christians) say: ''Allah has begotten a son (children or offspring).'' Glory is to Him.. (V.2:116)','باب {‏وَ قَالُوا اتَّخَذَ اللَّهُ وَلَدًا سُبْحَانَهُ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,11,'9',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"...And take you (people) the Maqam (place) of Ibrähim (Abraham) (or the stone on which Ibrãhim LiI stood while he was building the Ka''bah) as a place of prayer (for some of your prayers, e.g. two Rak''at after the Tawaf of Ka''bah) . . ." (V.2:125)','بَابُ قَوْلُهُ: {وَاتَّخِذُوا مِنْ مَقَامِ إِبْرَاهِيمَ مُصَلًّى}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,12,'10',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And (remember) when Ibrãhim (Abraham) and (his son) Isma''il (Ishmael) were raising the foundations of the House (Ka''bah at Makkah) (saying): ''Our Lord! Accept (this service) from us. Verily! You are the All-Hearer, the All-Knower''." (V.2:127)','باب قَوْلُهُ تَعَالَى ‏ {‏وَإِذْ يَرْفَعُ إِبْرَاهِيمُ الْقَوَاعِدَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ وَإِسْمَاعِيلُ رَبَّنَا تَقَبَّلْ مِنَّا إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ السَّمِيعُ الْعَلِيمُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,13,'11',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"Say (0 Muslims), We believe in Allah and that which has been sent down to us..." (V.2:136)','باب ‏ {‏قُولُوا آمَنَّا بِاللَّهِ وَمَا أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْنَا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,14,'12',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah "The fools (pagans, hypocrites and Jews) among the people will say, ''What has turned them (Muslims) from their Qiblah [Salat (prayer) direction (towards Jerusalem)]..." (V.2:142)','باب ‏ {‏سَيَقُولُ السُّفَهَاءُ مِنَ النَّاسِ مَا وَلاَّهُمْ عَنْ قِبْلَتِهِمُ الَّتِي كَانُوا عَلَيْهَا قُلْ لِلَّهِ الْمَشْرِقُ وَالْمَغْرِبُ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشَاءُ إِلَى صِرَاطٍ مُسْتَقِيمٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,15,'13',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah Jt: "Thus We have made of you [true Muslims— real believers of Islamic Monotheism, true followers of Prophet Muhammad jR and his Sunna (legal ways)], a just (and the best) nation, that you may be witnesses over mankind, and the Messenger (Muhammad ) will be a witness over you..." (V.2:143)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَكَذَلِكَ جَعَلْنَاكُمْ أُمَّةً وَسَطًا لِتَكُونُوا شُهَدَاءَ عَلَى النَّاسِ وَيَكُونَ الرَّسُولُ عَلَيْكُمْ شَهِيدًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,16,'14',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah: "...And We made the Qiblah (prayer direction towards Jerusalem) which you used to face, only to test those who followed the Messenger (Muhammad ) . . ." (V.2:143)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَمَا جَعَلْنَا الْقِبْلَةَ الَّتِي كُنْتَ عَلَيْهَا إِلاَّ لِنَعْلَمَ مَنْ يَتَّبِعُ الرَّسُولَ مِمَّنْ يَنْقَلِبُ عَلَى عَقِبَيْهِ وَإِنْ كَانَتْ لَكَبِيرَةً إِلاَّ عَلَى الَّذِينَ هَدَى اللَّهُ وَمَا كَانَ اللَّهُ لِيُضِيعَ إِيمَانَكُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ بِالنَّاسِ لَرَءُوفٌ رَحِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,17,'15',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah "Verily! We have seen the turning of your (Muhammad''s ) face towards the heaven..." (V.2:144)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏قَدْ نَرَى تَقَلُّبَ وَجْهِكَ فِي السَّمَاءِ‏} ‏ إِلَى ‏{‏يعْمَلُونَ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,18,'16',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah J: "And even if you were to bring to the people of the Scripture (Jews and Christians), all the Ayãt (proofs, evidences, verses, lessons, signs, revelations,-etc.) they would not follow your Qiblah (prayer direction)..." (V.2:145)','باب ‏ {‏وَلَئِنْ أَتَيْتَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ بِكُلِّ آيَةٍ مَا تَبِعُوا قِبْلَتَكَ‏} ‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّكَ إِذًا لَمِنَ الظَّالِمِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,19,'17',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"Those to whom We gave the Scripture (Jews and Christians) recognise him (Muhammad or the Ka''bah at Makkah) as they recognise their sons..." (V.2:146).','باب ‏ {‏الَّذِينَ آتَيْنَاهُمُ الْكِتَابَ يَعْرِفُونَهُ كَمَا يَعْرِفُونَ أَبْنَاءَهُمْ وَإِنَّ فَرِيقًا مِنْهُمْ لَيَكْتُمُونَ الْحَقَّ‏} ‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏مِنَ الْمُمْتَرِينَ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,20,'18',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"For every nation there is a direction to which they face (in their prayers)..." (V.2:148)','باب ‏{‏وَلِكُلٍّ وِجْهَةٌ هُوَ مُوَلِّيهَا فَاسْتَبِقُوا الْخَيْرَاتِ أَيْنَمَا تَكُونُوا يَأْتِ بِكُمُ اللَّهُ جَمِيعًا إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,21,'19',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And from wheresoever you start forth (for prayers) turn your face in the direction of AI-Masjid-al-Haram (at Makkah)..." (V.2:149)','باب ‏ {‏وَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ وَإِنَّهُ لَلْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكَ وَمَا اللَّهُ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ‏} ‏ شَطْرُهُ تِلْقَاؤُهُ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,22,'20',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And from wheresoever you start forth (for prayers), turn your face in the direction of Al-Masjid-al-Harãm (at Makkah), and wheresoever you are, turn your face towards it [when you pray)]..." (V.2:150)','باب ‏ {‏وَمِنْ حَيْثُ خَرَجْتَ فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ وَحَيْثُمَا كُنْتُمْ‏} ‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,23,'21',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah "Verily! A-afã and Al-Marwa (two mountains in Makkah) are of the Symbols of Allah..." (V.2:158)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةَ مِنْ شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ فَمَنْ حَجَّ الْبَيْتَ أَوِ اعْتَمَرَ فَلاَ جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ يَطَّوَّفَ بِهِمَا وَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ خَيْرًا فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ شَاكِرٌ عَلِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,24,'22',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah :"And of mankind are some who take (for worship) others besides Allah as rivals (to Allah). They love them as they love Allah..." (V.2:165)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَتَّخِذُ مِنْ دُونِ اللَّهِ أَنْدَادًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,25,'23',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"O you who believe! Al- Qisas (the Law of Equality in punishment) is prescribed for you..." (V.2:178)','باب ‏ {‏يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْقِصَاصُ فِي الْقَتْلَى الْحُرُّ بِالْحُرِّ‏} ‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,26,'24',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','“O you who believe! Observing As-Saum (the fasting) is prescribed for you as it was prescribed for those before you that you, may become Al- Muttaqun (V.2:183).','باب ‏ {‏يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا كُتِبَ عَلَيْكُمُ الصِّيَامُ كَمَا كُتِبَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَتَّقُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,27,'25',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah "[Observing Saum (fasts)] for a fixed number of days but if any of you is ill, or on a journey, the same number (should be made up) from other days. And as for those who can fast with difficulty (e.g., an old man, etc.) they have (a choice, either to fast or) to feed a Miskin (poor person) (for every day). But whoever does good of his own accord, it is better for him. And that you fast is better for you, if only you know." (V.2:184)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏أَيَّامًا مَعْدُودَاتٍ فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ مَرِيضًا أَوْ عَلَى سَفَرٍ فَعِدَّةٌ مِنْ أَيَّامٍ أُخَرَ وَعَلَى الَّذِينَ يُطِيقُونَهُ فِدْيَةٌ طَعَامُ مِسْكِينٍ فَمَنْ تَطَوَّعَ خَيْرًا فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَهُ وَأَنْ تَصُومُوا خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,28,'26',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"So whoever of you sights (the crescent on the first night of) the month (of Ramadan, i.e., is present at his home), he must observe Saum (fast) that month... (V.2:185)','باب ‏ {‏فَمَنْ شَهِدَ مِنْكُمُ الشَّهْرَ فَلْيَصُمْهُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,29,'27',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"It is made lawful for you to have sexual relation with your wives on the night of As-Saum (the fasts) ... (till) ... and seek that which Allah has ordained for you (offspring).. ." (V.2:187)','باب ‏ {‏أُحِلَّ لَكُمْ لَيْلَةَ الصِّيَامِ الرَّفَثُ إِلَى نِسَائِكُمْ هُنَّ لِبَاسٌ لَكُمْ وَأَنْتُمْ لِبَاسٌ لَهُنَّ عَلِمَ اللَّهُ أَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَخْتَانُونَ أَنْفُسَكُمْ فَتَابَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَعَفَا عَنْكُمْ فَالآنَ بَاشِرُوهُنَّ وَابْتَغُوا مَا كَتَبَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,30,'28',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"...And eat and drink until the white thread (light) of dawn appears to you distinct from the black thread (darkness of the night).. ." (V.2:187)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَكُلُوا وَاشْرَبُوا حَتَّى يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكُمُ الْخَيْطُ الأَبْيَضُ مِنَ الْخَيْطِ الأَسْوَدِ مِنَ الْفَجْرِ ثُمَّ أَتِمُّوا الصِّيَامَ إِلَى اللَّيْلِ وَلاَ تُبَاشِرُوهُنَّ وَأَنْتُمْ عَاكِفُونَ فِي الْمَسَاجِدِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,31,'29',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"...It is not A1-Birr (piety, righteousness) that you enter the houses from the back, but A1-Birr (is the quality of the one) who fears Allah." (V.2:189)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَلَيْسَ الْبِرُّ بِأَنْ تَأْتُوا الْبُيُوتَ مِنْ ظُهُورِهَا وَلَكِنَّ الْبِرَّ مَنِ اتَّقَى وَأْتُوا الْبُيُوتَ مِنْ أَبْوَابِهَا وَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تُفْلِحُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,32,'30',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "And fight them until there is no more Fitnah (disbelief and worshipping of others along with Allah) and (all and every kind of) worship is for Allah (Alone). But if they cease, let there be no transgression except against Az-Zalimün (the polytheists and wrong-doers) ." (V.2:193)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَقَاتِلُوهُمْ حَتَّى لاَ تَكُونَ فِتْنَةٌ وَيَكُونَ الدِّينُ لِلَّهِ فَإِنِ انْتَهَوْا فَلاَ عُدْوَانَ إِلاَّ عَلَى الظَّالِمِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,33,'31',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "And spend in the Cause of Allah (i.e., Jihad of all kinds), and do not throw yourselves into destruction (by not spending your wealth in the Cause of Allah), and do good. Truly, Allah loves A1-Muhsinun (the good-doers) ." (V.2:195)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَأَنْفِقُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَلاَ تُلْقُوا بِأَيْدِيكُمْ إِلَى التَّهْلُكَةِ وَأَحْسِنُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,34,'32',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','The Statement of Allah "And whosoever of you is ill or has an ailment in his scalp..." (V.2:196)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَمَنْ كَانَ مِنْكُمْ مَرِيضًا أَوْ بِهِ أَذًى مِنْ رَأْسِهِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,35,'33',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"...And whosoever performs the ''Umra in the months of Hajj before (performing) the Hajj (i.e., Hajj At.Tamattu'' and AI-Qiran) ." (V.2:196)','باب ‏ {‏فَمَنْ تَمَتَّعَ بِالْعُمْرَةِ إِلَى الْحَجِّ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,36,'34',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"There is no sin on you if you ask the Bounty of your Lord (during pilgrimage by trading)..." (V.2:198)','باب ‏ {‏لَيْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَنْ تَبْتَغُوا فَضْلاً مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,37,'35',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"Then depart from the place whence all the people depart..." (V.2:199)','باب ‏ {‏ثُمَّ أَفِيضُوا مِنْ حَيْثُ أَفَاضَ النَّاسُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,38,'36',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And of them there are some who say: ''Our Lord! Give us in this world that which is good and in the Hereafter that which is good...''" (V.2:201)','باب ‏ {‏وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَقُولُ رَبَّنَا آتِنَا فِي الدُّنْيَا حَسَنَةً وَفِي الآخِرَةِ حَسَنَةً وَقِنَا عَذَابَ النَّارِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,39,'37',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"...Yet he is the most quarrelsome of the opponents." (V.2:204)','باب ‏ {‏وَهُوَ أَلَدُّ الْخِصَامِ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,40,'38',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"Or think you that you will enter Paradise without such (trials) as came to those who passed away before you?" (V.2:214)','باب ‏ {‏أَمْ حَسِبْتُمْ أَنْ تَدْخُلُوا الْجَنَّةَ وَلَمَّا يَأْتِكُمْ مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ خَلَوْا مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ مَسَّتْهُمُ الْبَأْسَاءُ وَالضَّرَّاءُ‏} ‏ إِلَى ‏{‏قَرِيبٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,41,'39',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"Your wives are a tilth for you; so go to your tilth (have sexual relations with your wives in any manner as long as it is in the vagina and not in the anus) when or how you will..." (V.2:223)','باب ‏ {‏نِسَاؤُكُمْ حَرْثٌ لَكُمْ فَأْتُوا حَرْثَكُمْ أَنَّى شِئْتُمْ وَقَدِّمُوا لأَنْفُسِكُمْ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,42,'40',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And when you have divorced women and they have fulfilled the term of their prescribed period, do not prevent them from marrying their (former) husbands..." (V.2:232)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِذَا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّسَاءَ فَبَلَغْنَ أَجَلَهُنَّ فَلاَ تَعْضُلُوهُنَّ أَنْ يَنْكِحْنَ أَزْوَاجَهُنَّ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,43,'41',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And those of you who die and leave wives behind them, they (the wives) shall wait (as regards their marriage) for four months and ten days. Then when they have fulfilled their term, there is no sin on you if they (the wives) dispose of themselves in a just and honourable manner (i.e., they can marry). And Allah is Well-Acquainted with what you do." (V.2:234)','باب ‏ {‏وَالَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَذَرُونَ أَزْوَاجًا يَتَرَبَّصْنَ بِأَنْفُسِهِنَّ أَرْبَعَةَ أَشْهُرٍ وَعَشْرًا‏} ‏ إِلَى ‏ {‏بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,44,'42',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"Guard strictly the (five obligatory) A.s-Salawãt (the prayers), especially the middle SaM! (i.e., the best prayer - ''Asr) .. ." (V.2:238)','باب ‏ {‏حَافِظُوا عَلَى الصَّلَوَاتِ وَالصَّلاَةِ الْوُسْطَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,45,'43',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"...And stand before Allah with obedience [and do not speak to others during the Salat (prayers)]” (V.2:238)','باب ‏ {‏وَقُومُوا لِلَّهِ قَانِتِينَ‏} ‏ مُطِيعِينَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,46,'44',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "If you fear (an enemy), perform Salãt (prayer) on foot or riding. And when you are in safety..." (V.2:239)','باب قَوْلِهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ‏ {‏فَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ فَرِجَالاً أَوْ رُكْبَانًا فَإِذَا أَمِنْتُمْ فَاذْكُرُوا اللَّهَ كَمَا عَلَّمَكُمْ مَا لَمْ تَكُونُوا تَعْلَمُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,47,'45',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And those of you who die and leave behind wives..." (V.2:240)','باب ‏ {‏وَالَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَذَرُونَ أَزْوَاجًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,48,'46',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And (remember) when Ibrãhim (Abraham) said: My Lord! Show me how You give life to the dead..." (V.2:260)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِذْ قَالَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ رَبِّ أَرِنِي كَيْفَ تُحْيِي الْمَوْتَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,49,'47',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "Would any of you wish to have a garden with date palms and vines ... (till) ... that you may give thought." (V.2:266)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏أَيَوَدُّ أَحَدُكُمْ أَنْ تَكُونَ لَهُ جَنَّةٌ‏} ‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏تَتَفَكَّرُونَ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,50,'48',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"...They do not beg of people at all..." (V.2:273)','باب ‏ {‏لاَ يَسْأَلُونَ النَّاسَ إِلْحَافًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,51,'49',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"...Whereas Allah has permitted trading and forbidden Riba (usury) (V.2 :275)','باب ‏ {‏وَأَحَلَّ اللَّهُ الْبَيْعَ وَحَرَّمَ الرِّبَا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,52,'50',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"Allah will destory Riba (usury) ." (V.2:276)','باب ‏ {‏يَمْحَقُ اللَّهُ الرِّبَا‏} ‏ يُذْهِبُهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,53,'51',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"...Then take a notice of war from Allah and His Messenger..." (V.2:279)','باب ‏ {‏فَأْذَنُوا بِحَرْبٍ‏} ‏ فَاعْلَمُوا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,54,'52',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And if the debtor is in a hard time (has no money), then grant him time till it is easy for him to repay..." (V.2:280)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِنْ كَانَ ذُو عُسْرَةٍ فَنَظِرَةٌ إِلَى مَيْسَرَةٍ‏} ‏ ‏ {‏وَأَنْ تَصَدَّقُوا خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,55,'53',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And be afraid of the Day when you shall be brought back to Allah.. ." (V.2:281)','باب ‏ {‏وَاتَّقُوا يَوْمًا تُرْجَعُونَ فِيهِ إِلَى اللَّهِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,56,'54',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"And whether you disclose what is in your ownselves or conceal it..." (V.2:284)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِنْ تُبْدُوا مَا فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ أَوْ تُخْفُوهُ يُحَاسِبْكُمْ بِهِ اللَّهُ فَيَغْفِرُ لِمَنْ يَشَاءُ وَيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَشَاءُ وَاللَّهُ عَلَى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,57,'55',2,'Surat al-Baqarah (The Cow)','سورة الْبَقَرَةِ','"The Messenger (Muhammad ﷺ) believes in what has been sent down to him from his Lord..." (V.2:285)','باب ‏ {‏آمَنَ الرَّسُولُ بِمَا أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْهِ مِنْ رَبِّهِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,58,'1',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"In it are Verses that are entirely clear." (3:7)','باب ‏ {‏مِنْهُ آيَاتٌ مُحْكَمَاتٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,59,'2',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"...And I seek refuge with You (Allah) for her and her offspring from Shaitan (Satan), the outcast." (V.3:36)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِنِّي أُعِيذُهَا بِكَ وَذُرِّيَّتَهَا مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيمِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,60,'3',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"Verily, those who purchase a small gain at the cost of Allah''s Covenant and their oaths, they shall have no portion in the Hereafter (Paradise)... (till) ... and they shall have a painful torment." (V.3 -77)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يَشْتَرُونَ بِعَهْدِ اللَّهِ وَأَيْمَانِهِمْ ثَمَنًا قَلِيلاً أُولَئِكَ لاَ خَلاَقَ لَهُمْ‏} ‏ لاَ خَيْرَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,61,'4',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"Say (O Muḥammad pbuh), ''O people of the Scripture (Jews and Christians)! Come to a word that is just between us and you, that we worship none but Allah..." (V.3:64)','باب ‏{‏قُلْ يَا أَهْلَ الْكِتَابِ تَعَالَوْا إِلَى كَلِمَةٍ سَوَاءٍ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ أَنْ لاَ نَعْبُدَ إِلاَّ اللَّهَ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,62,'5',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"By no means shall you attain Al-Birr (piety, righteousness; it means here Allah''s Reward, i.e., Paradise) unless you spend (in Allah''s Cause) of that which you love..." (V.3:92)','باب ‏ {‏لَنْ تَنَالُوا الْبِرَّ حَتَّى تُنْفِقُوا مِمَّا تُحِبُّونَ‏} ‏ إِلَى ‏{‏بِهِ عَلِيمٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,63,'6',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"Say (O Muḥammad pbuh): Bring here the Taurāt (Torah) and recite it, if you are truthful." (V.3:93)','باب ‏ {‏قُلْ فَأْتُوا بِالتَّوْرَاةِ فَاتْلُوهَا إِنْ كُنْتُمْ صَادِقِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,64,'7',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"You (true believers in Islamic Monotheism, and real followers of Prophet Muḥammad pbuh and his Sunna) are the best of peoples ever raised up for mankind..." (V.3:110)','باب ‏ {‏كُنْتُمْ خَيْرَ أُمَّةٍ أُخْرِجَتْ لِلنَّاسِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,65,'8',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"When two parties from among you were about to lose heart..." (V.3:122)','باب ‏ {‏إِذْ هَمَّتْ طَائِفَتَانِ مِنْكُمْ أَنْ تَفْشَلاَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,66,'9',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"Not for you (O Muḥammad pbuh, but for Allah) is the decision.." (V.3:128)','باب ‏{‏لَيْسَ لَكَ مِنَ الأَمْرِ شَىْءٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,67,'10',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "...And the Messenger (Muḥammad pbuh) was in your rear calling you back..." (V3:153)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَالرَّسُولُ يَدْعُوكُمْ فِي أُخْرَاكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,68,'11',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','Allah''s Statement: "...He sent down security for you. Slumber..." (V.3:154)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏أَمَنَةً نُعَاسًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,69,'12',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted:  "Those who answered (the Call of) Allah and the Messenger (Muḥammad pbuh) after being wounded; for those of them who did good deeds and feared Allah, there is a great reward." (V.3:172)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏الَّذِينَ اسْتَجَابُوا لِلَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا أَصَابَهُمُ الْقَرْحُ لِلَّذِينَ أَحْسَنُوا مِنْهُمْ وَاتَّقَوْا أَجْرٌ عَظِيمٌ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,70,'13',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','His Statement: "Those (i.e., believers) unto whom the people (hypocrites) said, ''Verily the people (Mushrikūn) have gathered against you (a great army), therefore, fear them..."'' (V .3:173)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّ النَّاسَ قَدْ جَمَعُوا لَكُمْ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,71,'14',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"And let not those who covetously withhold of that which Allah has bestowed on them of His Bounty .. ." (V.3:180)','باب ‏ {‏وَلاَ يَحْسِبَنَّ الَّذِينَ يَبْخَلُونَ بِمَا آتَاهُمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,72,'15',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"...And you shall certainly hear much that will grieve you from those who received the Scripture before you (Jews and Christians) and from those who ascribe partners to Allāh.. ." (V.3:186)','باب ‏ {‏وَلَتَسْمَعُنَّ مِنَ الَّذِينَ أُوتُوا الْكِتَابَ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ وَمِنَ الَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا أَذًى كَثِيرًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,73,'16',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"Think not that those who rejoice in what they have done (or brought about)..." (V.3:188)','باب ‏{‏لاَ يَحْسِبَنَّ الَّذِينَ يَفْرَحُونَ بِمَا أَتَوْا‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,74,'17',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','Allah''s Statement: "Verily! In the creation of the heavens and the earth, and in the alternation of night and day, there are indeed signs for men of understanding." (V.3:190)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّ فِي خَلْقِ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,75,'18',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"Those who remember Allāh (always and in prayers), standing, sitting, and lying down on their sides; and think deeply about the creation of the heavens and the earth...." (V.3:191)','باب ‏ {‏الَّذِينَ يَذْكُرُونَ اللَّهَ قِيَامًا وَقُعُودًا وَعَلَى جُنُوبِهِمْ وَيَتَفَكَّرُونَ فِي خَلْقِ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,76,'19',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"Our Lord! Verily, whom You admit to the Fire, indeed, You have disgraced him and never will the Ẓalimūn (polytheists and wrong-doers) find any helpers." (V.3:192)','باب ‏ {‏رَبَّنَا إِنَّكَ مَنْ تُدْخِلِ النَّارَ فَقَدْ أَخْزَيْتَهُ وَمَا لِلظَّالِمِينَ مِنْ أَنْصَارٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,77,'20',3,'Surat Ale-‘Imran (The Family of ''Imran)','سورة آلِ عِمْرَانَ','"Our Lord! Verily, we have heard the call of one (i.e., Muḥammad pbuh) calling to Faith..." (V.3:193)','باب ‏ {‏رَبَّنَا إِنَّنَا سَمِعْنَا مُنَادِيًا، يُنَادِي لِلإِيمَانِ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,78,'1',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"And if you fear that you shall not be able to deal justly with the orphan girls..." (V.4:3)','باب ‏{‏وَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ أَنْ لاَ تُقْسِطُوا فِي الْيَتَامَى‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,79,'2',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"...But if he (the guardian) is poor, let him have for himself what is just and reasonable (according to his work). And when you release their property to them, take witness in their presence; and Allah is All-Sufficient in taking account." (V.4:6)','باب ‏ {‏وَمَنْ كَانَ فَقِيرًا فَلْيَأْكُلْ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ فَإِذَا دَفَعْتُمْ إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوَالَهُمْ فَأَشْهِدُوا عَلَيْهِمْ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,80,'3',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"And when the relatives and the orphans and the poor are present at the time of division..." (V.4:8)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِذَا حَضَرَ الْقِسْمَةَ أُولُو الْقُرْبَى وَالْيَتَامَى وَالْمَسَاكِينُ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,81,'4',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"Allah commands you as regards your children''s (inheritance)..." (V.4:11)','باب ‏ {‏يُوصِيكُمُ اللَّهُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,82,'5',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','Allah''s Statement "In that which your wives leave, your share is a half..." (V.4:12)','باب ‏ {‏وَلَكُمْ نِصْفُ مَا تَرَكَ أَزْوَاجُكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,83,'6',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"...You are forbidden to inherit women against their will, and you should not treat them with harshness, that you may take back part of the Mahr (bridal money given by the husband to his wife at the time of marriage) you have given them..." (V.4:19)','باب ‏ {‏لاَ يَحِلُّ لَكُمْ أَنْ تَرِثُوا النِّسَاءَ كَرْهًا‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,84,'7',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"And to everyone, We have appointed heirs of that (property) left by parents and relatives. To those, also, with whom you have made a pledge (brotherhood), give them their due portion [by Wasiya (wills)]. Truly, Allah is Ever a Witness over all things." (V.4:33)','باب ‏ {‏وَلِكُلٍّ جَعَلْنَا مَوَالِيَ مِمَّا تَرَكَ الْوَالِدَانِ وَالأَقْرَبُونَ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,85,'8',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"Surely! Allah wrongs not even of the weight of an atom (or a small ant)..." (V.4:40)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّ اللَّهَ لاَ يَظْلِمُ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ‏} ‏ يَعْنِي زِنَةَ ذَرَّةٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,86,'9',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"How (will it be) then when We bring from each nation a witness and We bring you (O Muhammad) as a witness against these people?" (V.4:41)','باب ‏ {‏فَكَيْفَ إِذَا جِئْنَا مِنْ كُلِّ أُمَّةٍ بِشَهِيدٍ وَجِئْنَا بِكَ عَلَى هَؤُلاَءِ شَهِيدًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,87,'10',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"...And if you are ill, or on a journey, or one of you comes after answering the call of nature..." (V.4:43)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَإِنْ كُنْتُمْ مَرْضَى أَوْ عَلَى سَفَرٍ أَوْ جَاءَ أَحَدٌ مِنْكُمْ مِنَ الْغَائِطِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,88,'11',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"Obey Allah and obey the Messenger (Muhammad ﷺ ) and those of you (Muslims) who are in authority..." (V.4:59)','باب ‏ {‏أَطِيعُوا اللَّهَ وَأَطِيعُوا الرَّسُولَ وَأُولِي الْأَمْرِ مِنكُمْ} ‏ ذَوِي الأَمْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,89,'12',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"But no, by your Lord, they can have no Faith, until they make you (Muhammad ﷺ ) judge in all disputes between them..." (V.4:65)','باب ‏ {‏فَلاَ وَرَبِّكَ لاَ يُؤْمِنُونَ حَتَّى يُحَكِّمُوكَ فِيمَا شَجَرَ بَيْنَهُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,90,'13',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"...Then they will be in the company of those on whom A11ah has bestowed His Grace, of the Prophets..." (V.4:69)','باب ‏ {‏فَأُولَئِكَ مَعَ الَّذِينَ أَنْعَمَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنَ النَّبِيِّينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,91,'14',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','Allah''s Statement "And what is wrong with you that you fight not in the Cause of Allah... (till) ... whose people are oppressors..." (V.4:75)','باب قَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏وَمَا لَكُمْ لاَ تُقَاتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ‏} ‏ إِلَى ‏ {‏الظَّالِمِ أَهْلُهَا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,92,'15',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"Then what is the matter with you that you are divided into two parties about the hypocrites? Allah has cast them back (to disbelief) because of what they have earned..." (V.4:88)','باب ‏ {‏فَمَا لَكُمْ فِي الْمُنَافِقِينَ فِئَتَيْنِ وَاللَّهُ أَرْكَسَهُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,93,NULL,4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"When there comes to them some matter touching (public) safety or fear, they make it known..." (V.4:83)','{‏وَإِذَا جَاءَهُمْ أَمْرٌ مِنَ الأَمْنِ أَوِ الْخَوْفِ أَذَاعُوا بِهِ‏} ‏ أَفْشَوْهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,94,'16',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell..." (V.4:93)','باب ‏ {‏وَمَنْ يَقْتُلْ مُؤْمِنًا مُتَعَمِّدًا فَجَزَاؤُهُ جَهَنَّمُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,95,'17',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"And say not to anyone who greets you (by embracing Islam), ''You are not a believer..." (V.4:94)','باب ‏ {‏وَلاَ تَقُولُوا لِمَنْ أَلْقَى إِلَيْكُمُ السَّلاَمَ لَسْتَ مُؤْمِنًا‏} ‏ السِّلْمُ وَالسَّلَمُ وَالسَّلاَمُ وَاحِدٌ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,96,'18',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"Not equal are those of the believers who sit (at home)..." (V.4:95)','باب {لاَ يَسْتَوِي الْقَاعِدُونَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُجَاهِدُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,97,'19',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"Verily! As for those whom the angels take (in death) while they are wronging themselves (as they stayed among the disbelievers even though emigration was obligatory for them), they (angels) say (to them): In what (condition) were you?..."(V.4:97)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَوَفَّاهُمُ الْمَلاَئِكَةُ ظَالِمِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ قَالُوا فِيمَ كُنْتُمْ قَالُوا كُنَّا مُسْتَضْعَفِينَ فِي الأَرْضِ قَالُوا أَلَمْ تَكُنْ أَرْضُ اللَّهِ وَاسِعَةً فَتُهَاجِرُوا فِيهَا‏} ‏ الآيَةَ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,98,'20',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"Except the weak ones among men, women..." (V.4:98)','باب ‏{‏إِلاَّ الْمُسْتَضْعَفِينَ مِنَ الرِّجَالِ وَالنِّسَاءِ وَالْوِلْدَانِ لاَ يَسْتَطِيعُونَ حِيلَةً وَلاَ يَهْتَدُونَ سَبِيلاً‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,99,'21',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"These are they whom Allah is likely to forgive them..." (V.4:99)','باب ‏ {‏فَأُولَئِكَ عَسَى اللَّهُ أَنْ يَعْفُوَ عَنْهُمْ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ عَفُوًّا غَفُورًا ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,100,'22',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"But there is no sin on you if you put away your arms because of the inconvenience of rain…" (V.4:102)','باب ‏ {‏وَلاَ جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ إِنْ كَانَ بِكُمْ أَذًى مِنْ مَطَرٍ أَوْ كُنْتُمْ مَرْضَى أَنْ تَضَعُوا أَسْلِحَتَكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,101,'23',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','Allah''s Statement: "They ask your legal instruction concerning women, say: Allah instructs you about them, and about what is recited unto you in the Book concerning orphan girls.. ." (V.4:127)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَيَسْتَفْتُونَكَ فِي النِّسَاءِ قُلِ اللَّهُ يُفْتِيكُمْ فِيهِنَّ وَمَا يُتْلَى عَلَيْكُمْ فِي الْكِتَابِ فِي يَتَامَى النِّسَاءِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,102,'24',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"If a woman fears cruelty or desertion on her husband''s part..." (V.4:128)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِنِ امْرَأَةٌ خَافَتْ مِنْ بَعْلِهَا نُشُوزًا أَوْ إِعْرَاضًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,103,'25',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"Verily, the hypocrites will be in the lowest depths (grade) of the Fire..." (V.4:145)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ فِي الدَّرَكِ الأَسْفَلِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,104,'26',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','Allah''s Statement: "Verily, We have sent revelation to you, (O Muhammad ﷺ ) ... (till) ... as We sent revelation to Nuh (Noah) and Yunus (Jonah), Hãrün (Aaron) and Sulaimãn (Solomon)..." (V.4:163)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏إِنَّا أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَيْكَ‏}‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَيُونُسَ وَهَارُونَ وَسُلَيْمَانَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,105,'27',4,'Surat an-Nisa’ (Women)','سورة النِّسَاءِ','"They ask you for a legal verdict. Say: ''Allah directs (thus) about Al-Kalal,a (those who leave neither descendants nor ascendants as heirs). If it is a man that dies, leaving a sister, but no child, she shall have half the inheritance. If (such a deceased was) a woman who left no child, her brother takes her inheritance..." (V.4:176)','باب {‏يَسْتَفْتُونَكَ قُلِ اللَّهُ يُفْتِيكُمْ فِي الْكَلاَلَةِ إِنِ امْرُؤٌ هَلَكَ لَيْسَ لَهُ وَلَدٌ وَلَهُ أُخْتٌ فَلَهَا نِصْفُ مَا تَرَكَ وَهُوَ يَرِثُهَا إِنْ لَمْ يَكُنْ لَهَا وَلَدٌ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,106,'1',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','"[Game (also) being unlawful] when you assume Ihrãm for Hail or Umra (pilgrimage)"... (V.5:1) "So, because of their breach of their covenant "... (V.5 :13)','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,107,'2',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "This day, I have perfected your religion for you..." (V.5:3)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏الْيَوْمَ أَكْمَلْتُ لَكُمْ دِينَكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,108,'3',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "...And you find no water, then perform Tayammum with clean earth..." (V.5:6)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَلَمْ تَجِدُوا مَاءً فَتَيَمَّمُوا صَعِيدًا طَيِّبًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,109,'4',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','The Statement of Allah:"...So go you and your Lord and fight you two, we are sitting right here." (V.5:24)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَاذْهَبْ أَنْتَ وَرَبُّكَ فَقَاتِلاَ إِنَّا هَا هُنَا قَاعِدُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,110,'5',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','"The recompense of those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger, and do mischief in the land is only that they shall be killed or crucified or their hands and feet be cut off from opposite sides..." (V.5:33)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّمَا جَزَاءُ الَّذِينَ يُحَارِبُونَ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَيَسْعَوْنَ فِي الأَرْضِ فَسَادًا أَنْ يُقَتَّلُوا أَوْ يُصَلَّبُوا‏} ‏  إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏أَوْ يُنْفَوْا مِنَ الأَرْضِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,111,'6',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "...And wounds, equal for equal (A1-Qisas i.e., the law of equality in punishment)..." (V.5:45)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَالْجُرُوحَ قِصَاصٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,112,'7',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','"O Messenger (Muhammad ﷺ)! Proclaim (the Message) which has been sent down to you from your Lord..." (V.5:67)','باب ‏ {‏يَا أَيُّهَا الرَّسُولُ بَلِّغْ مَا أُنْزِلَ إِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَبِّكَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,113,'8',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "Allah will not punish you for what is unintentional in your oaths..." (V.5:89)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏لاَ يُؤَاخِذُكُمُ اللَّهُ بِاللَّغْوِ فِي أَيْمَانِكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,114,'9',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','The Statement of Allah: "O you who believe! Make not unlawful the Tayyibãt (all that is good as regards foods, things, deeds, beliefs, persons) which Allah has made lawful to you..." (V.5:87)','باب ‏ {‏لاَ تُحَرِّمُوا طَيِّبَاتِ مَا أَحَلَّ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,115,'10',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "Intoxicants (all kinds of alcoholic drinks), gambling, Al-Ansab  and Al-AzIam (arrows for seeking luck or a decision) are an abomination of Satan''s handiwork..." (V.5:90)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّمَا الْخَمْرُ وَالْمَيْسِرُ وَالأَنْصَابُ وَالأَزْلاَمُ رِجْسٌ مِنْ عَمَلِ الشَّيْطَانِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,116,'11',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','"Those who believe and do righteous good deeds, there is no sin on them for what they ate (in the past)..." (V.5:93)','باب ‏{‏لَيْسَ عَلَى الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوا الصَّالِحَاتِ جُنَاحٌ فِيمَا طَعِمُوا‏}‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَاللَّهُ يُحِبُّ الْمُحْسِنِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,117,'12',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "...Ask not about things which, if made plain to you, may cause you trouble..." (V.5:101)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏لاَ تَسْأَلُوا عَنْ أَشْيَاءَ، إِنْ تُبْدَ لَكُمْ تَسُؤْكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,118,'13',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','''Allah has not instituted things like Bahirah or a Sã''ibah, or a Wasilah or a Ham..." (V.5:103)','باب ‏ {‏مَا جَعَلَ اللَّهُ مِنْ بَحِيرَةٍ وَلاَ سَائِبَةٍ وَلاَ وَصِيلَةٍ وَلاَ حَامٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,119,'14',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','"And I was a witness over them while I dwelt amongst them; but when You took me up, You were the Watcher over them, and You are a Witness to all things." (V.5:117)','باب ‏{‏وَكُنْتُ عَلَيْهِمْ شَهِيدًا مَا دُمْتُ فِيهِمْ فَلَمَّا تَوَفَّيْتَنِي كُنْتَ أَنْتَ الرَّقِيبَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَأَنْتَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيدٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,120,'15',5,'Surat al-Ma’idah (The Spread Table)','سورة الْمَائِدَةِ','Allah''s Statement: "If You punish them, they are Your slaves."(V.5:118)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنْ تُعَذِّبْهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ عِبَادُكَ وَإِنْ تَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ فَإِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْعَزِيزُ الْحَكِيمُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,121,'1',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ','"And With Him are the keys of the Ghaib, (all that is hidden), none knows them but He..." (V.6:59)','باب ‏ {‏وَعِنْدَهُ مَفَاتِحُ الْغَيْبِ لاَ يَعْلَمُهَا إِلاَّ هُوَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,122,'2',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ','"Say: He has power to send torment on you from above..." (V.6:65)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏قُلْ هُوَ الْقَادِرُ عَلَى أَنْ يَبْعَثَ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابًا مِنْ فَوْقِكُمْ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,123,'3',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ','"It is those who believe (in the Oneness of Allah and worship none but Him Alone) and confuse not their belief with Zuim (wrong i.e., by worshipping others besides Allah).. ." (V.6:82)','باب ‏ {‏وَلَمْ يَلْبِسُوا إِيمَانَهُمْ بِظُلْمٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,124,'4',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ','The Statement of Allah: "...And Yünus (Jonah) and Lut (Lot), and each one of them We preferred above Al-Alamin (mankind and jinn) (of their times)" (V.6:86)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَيُونُسَ وَلُوطًا وَكُلاًّ فَضَّلْنَا عَلَى الْعَالَمِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,125,'5',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ','The Statement of Allah: "They are those whom Allah had guided. So, follow their guidance..." (V.6:90)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏أُولَئِكَ الَّذِينَ هَدَى اللَّهُ فَبِهُدَاهُمُ اقْتَدِهْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,126,'6',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ','Allah''s Statement: "And unto those who are Jews, We forbade every (animal) with undivided hoof..." (V.6:146)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَعَلَى الَّذِينَ هَادُوا حَرَّمْنَا كُلَّ ذِي ظُفُرٍ وَمِنَ الْبَقَرِ وَالْغَنَمِ حَرَّمْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ شُحُومَهُمَا‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,127,'7',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ','The Statement of Allah: "...Come not near to Al-Fawahish (shameful sins, illegal sexual intercourse), whether committed openly or secretly..." (V.6:151)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَلاَ تَقْرَبُوا الْفَوَاحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,128,'8',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ',NULL,'بَابُ وَكِيلٌ حَفِيظٌ وَمُحِيطٌ بِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,129,'9',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ','The Statement of Allah: "Say: ''Bring forward your witnesses..." (V.6:150)','بَابُ قَوْلِهِ: {هَلُمَّ شُهَدَاءَكُمُ}:'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,130,'10',6,'Surat al-An’am (Cattle)','سورة الأَنْعَامِ','"The day that some of the signs of your Lord do come, no good will it do to a person to believe..." (V.6:158)','باب ‏ {‏لاَ يَنْفَعُ نَفْسًا إِيمَانُهَا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,131,'1',7,'Surat al-A’raf (The Heights)','سورة الأَعْرَافِ','The Statement of Allah: "Say (O Muhammad ﷺ): ''(But) the things that my Lord has indeed forbidden are Al-Fawãhish (great evil sins, every kind of unlawful sexual intercourse) whether committed openly or secretly."'' (V.7:33)','باب قَوْلِ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ‏ {‏قُلْ إِنَّمَا حَرَّمَ رَبِّيَ الْفَوَاحِشَ مَا ظَهَرَ مِنْهَا وَمَا بَطَنَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,132,'2',7,'Surat al-A’raf (The Heights)','سورة الأَعْرَافِ','"And when Musa (Moses) came at the time and place appointed by Us, and his Lord (Allah) spoke to him, he said, ''O my Lord! Show me (Yourself) that I may look upon You." (V.7:143)','باب ‏ {‏وَلَمَّا جَاءَ مُوسَى لِمِيقَاتِنَا وَكَلَّمَهُ رَبُّهُ قَالَ رَبِّ أَرِنِي أَنْظُرْ إِلَيْكَ قَالَ لَنْ تَرَانِي وَلَكِنِ انْظُرْ إِلَى الْجَبَلِ فَإِنِ اسْتَقَرَّ مَكَانَهُ فَسَوْفَ تَرَانِي فَلَمَّا تَجَلَّى رَبُّهُ لِلْجَبَلِ جَعَلَهُ دَكًّا وَخَرَّ مُوسَى صَعِقًا فَلَمَّا أَفَاقَ قَالَ سُبْحَانَكَ تُبْتُ إِلَيْكَ وَأَنَا أَوَّلُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,133,NULL,7,'Surat al-A’raf (The Heights)','سورة الأَعْرَافِ','Manna and quails','الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوَى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,134,'3',7,'Surat al-A’raf (The Heights)','سورة الأَعْرَافِ','"Say (O Muhammad ﷺ : ''O mankind. Verily, I am sent to you all as the Messenger of Allah - to Whom belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. Lailaha ilIa Huwa (none has the right to be worshipped but He). It is He Who gives life and causes death. So believe in Allah and His Messenger (Muhammad ﷺ,), the Prophet who can neither read nor write (i.e., Muhammad ﷺ) ,who believes in Allah and His Words [(this Qur''an), the Taurat (Torah) and the Injeel (Gpspel) and also Allah''s Word: "Be! - and he was, i.e., ''Isa (Jesus) son of Maryam (Mary) ;and follow him so that you may be guided." (V.7:158)','{‏قُلْ يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ إِنِّي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ إِلَيْكُمْ جَمِيعًا الَّذِي لَهُ مُلْكُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ هُوَ يُحْيِي وَيُمِيتُ فَآمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ النَّبِيِّ الأُمِّيِّ الَّذِي يُؤْمِنُ بِاللَّهِ وَكَلِمَاتِهِ وَاتَّبِعُوهُ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَهْتَدُونَ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,135,'4',7,'Surat al-A’raf (The Heights)','سورة الأَعْرَافِ','Allah''s Saying: "And say ... Hittatun..." [i.e., (O Allah) forgive our sins] (V.7:161)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏وَقُولُوا حِطَّةٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,136,'5',7,'Surat al-A’raf (The Heights)','سورة الأَعْرَافِ','"Show forgiveness, enjoin what is good, and turn away from the foolish (i.e., don''t punish them)." (V.7:199)','باب ‏ {‏خُذِ الْعَفْوَ وَأْمُرْ بِالْعُرْفِ وَأَعْرِضْ عَنِ الْجَاهِلِينَ‏} ‏ الْعُرْفُ: الْمَعْرُوفُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,137,'1',8,'Surat al-Anfal (Spoils of War)','سورة الأَنْفَالِ','The Statement of Allah: "They ask you (O Muhammad  ﷺ) about Al-Anfal (the spoils of war). Say: ''The spoils are for Allah and the Messenger ﷺ.'' So fear Allah and adjust all matters of difference among you..." (V.8:1)','باب قَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏يَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الأَنْفَالِ، قُلِ الأَنْفَالُ لِلَّهِ وَالرَّسُولِ فَاتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَأَصْلِحُوا ذَاتَ بَيْنِكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,138,'1',8,'Surat al-Anfal (Spoils of War)','سورة الأَنْفَالِ','"Verily! The worst of (moving) living creatures with Allah are the deaf and the dumb, those who understand not (i.e., the disbelievers) ." (V.8:22)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّ شَرَّ الدَّوَابِّ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ الصُّمُّ الْبُكْمُ الَّذِينَ لاَ يَعْقِلُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,139,'2',8,'Surat al-Anfal (Spoils of War)','سورة الأَنْفَالِ','"O you who believe! Answer Allah (by obeying Him) and (His) Messenger when he () calls you to that which will give you life, and know that Allah comes in between a man and his heart (i.e., He prevents an evil person to decide anything). And verily, to Him you shall (all) be gathered." (V.8:24)','‏ {‏يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اسْتَجِيبُوا لِلَّهِ وَلِلرَّسُولِ إِذَا دَعَاكُمْ لِمَا يُحْيِيكُمْ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَحُولُ بَيْنَ الْمَرْءِ وَقَلْبِهِ وَأَنَّهُ إِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,140,'3',8,'Surat al-Anfal (Spoils of War)','سورة الأَنْفَالِ','The Statement of Allah: "And (remember) when they said, ''O Allah! If this (the Qur''an) is indeed the truth (revealed) from You, then rain down stones on us..." (V.8:32)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَإِذْ قَالُوا اللَّهُمَّ إِنْ كَانَ هَذَا هُوَ الْحَقَّ مِنْ عِنْدِكَ فَأَمْطِرْ عَلَيْنَا حِجَارَةً مِنَ السَّمَاءِ أَوِ ائْتِنَا بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,141,'4',8,'Surat al-Anfal (Spoils of War)','سورة الأَنْفَالِ','The Statement of Allah: "And Allah would not punish them while you (Muhammad ﷺ) are amongst them, nor will He punish them while they seek (Allah''s) forgiveness." (V.8:33)','باب ‏ {‏وَمَا كَانَ اللَّهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُمْ وَأَنْتَ فِيهِمْ وَمَا كَانَ اللَّهُ مُعَذِّبَهُمْ وَهُمْ يَسْتَغْفِرُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,142,'5',8,'Surat al-Anfal (Spoils of War)','سورة الأَنْفَالِ','"And fight them until there is no more Fitnah (disbelief and polytheism, i.e., worshipping others besides Allah) and the religion (worship) will be all for Allah (Alone) (in the whole of the world)..." (V.8:39)','باب ‏ {‏وَقَاتِلُوهُمْ حَتَّى لاَ تَكُونَ فِتْنَةٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,143,'6',8,'Surat al-Anfal (Spoils of War)','سورة الأَنْفَالِ','"0 Prophet (Muhammad ﷺ)! Urge the believers to fight..." (V.8:65)','باب ‏ {‏يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ حَرِّضِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلَى الْقِتَالِ إِنْ يَكُنْ مِنْكُمْ عِشْرُونَ صَابِرُونَ يَغْلِبُوا مِائَتَيْنِ وَإِنْ يَكُنْ مِنْكُمْ مِائَةٌ يَغْلِبُوا أَلْفًا مِنَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِأَنَّهُمْ قَوْمٌ لاَ يَفْقَهُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,144,'7',8,'Surat al-Anfal (Spoils of War)','سورة الأَنْفَالِ','"Now that Allah has lightened your (task), for He knows that there is weakness in you..." (V.8:66)','باب ‏ {‏الآنَ خَفَّفَ اللَّهُ عَنْكُمْ وَعَلِمَ أَنَّ فِيكُمْ ضُعْفًا‏} ‏ الآيَةَ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏وَاللَّهُ مَعَ الصَّابِرِينَ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,145,'1',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','Allah''s Statement: "Freedom from (all) obligations (is declared) from Allah and His Messenger ﷺ to those of the Mushrikin [polytheists, pagans, idolaters, disbelievers in the Oneness of Allah and in His Messenger Muhammad ﷺ] with whom you made a treaty." (V.9:1)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏بَرَاءَةٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ إِلَى الَّذِينَ عَاهَدْتُمْ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,146,'2',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah: "So travel freely (O Mushrikün) for four months (as you will) throughout the land, but know that you cannot escape (from the punishment of) Allah, and Allah will disgrace the disbelievers." (V.9:2)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَسِيحُوا فِي الأَرْضِ أَرْبَعَةَ أَشْهُرٍ وَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِي اللَّهِ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ مُخْزِي الْكَافِرِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,147,'3',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','Allah''s Statement: "And a declaration from Allah and His Messenger... (up to)... Mushrikün ." (V.9:3)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَأَذَانٌ مِنَ اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ إِلَى النَّاسِ يَوْمَ الْحَجِّ الأَكْبَرِ أَنَّ اللَّهَ بَرِيءٌ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ وَرَسُولُهُ فَإِنْ تُبْتُمْ فَهُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ وَإِنْ تَوَلَّيْتُمْ فَاعْلَمُوا أَنَّكُمْ غَيْرُ مُعْجِزِي اللَّهِ وَبَشِّرِ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,148,'4',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','"Except those of the Mushrikün [polytheists, pagans, idolaters, and disbelievers in the Oneness of Allah and in His Messenger Muhammad ﷺ] with whom you (Muslims) have a treaty..." (V.9:4)','‏باب {‏إِلاَّ الَّذِينَ عَاهَدْتُمْ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,149,'5',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah: "Fight you the leaders of disbelief (chiefs of Quraish - Mushrikün of Makkah) for surely their oaths are nothing to them..." (V.9:12)','باب ‏ {‏فَقَاتِلُوا أَئِمَّةَ الْكُفْرِ إِنَّهُمْ لاَ أَيْمَانَ لَهُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,150,'6',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah: "...And those who hoard up gold and silver (AI-Kanz—the money, the Zakãt of which has not been paid) and spend it not in the Way of Allah—announce to them a painful torment." (V.9:34)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَالَّذِينَ يَكْنِزُونَ الذَّهَبَ وَالْفِضَّةَ وَلاَ يُنْفِقُونَهَا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ فَبَشِّرْهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,151,'7',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah "On the Day when that (Al-Kanz—money gold and silver, etc., the Zakät of which has not been paid) will be heated in the fire of Hell, and with it will be branded their foreheads…" (V.9:35)','باب قَوْلِهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ‏ {‏يَوْمَ يُحْمَى عَلَيْهَا فِي نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ فَتُكْوَى بِهَا جِبَاهُهُمْ وَجُنُوبُهُمْ وَظُهُورُهُمْ هَذَا مَا كَنَزْتُمْ لأَنْفُسِكُمْ فَذُوقُوا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَكْنِزُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,152,'8',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah: "Verily, the number of months with Allah is twelve months (in a year) so was it ordained by Allah on the Day when He created the heavens and the earth; of them four are sacred, (i.e., the 1st, the 7th, the 11th, and the 12th months of the Islamic calendar). That is the right religion; so wrong not yourself therein.. ." (V.9:36)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّ عِدَّةَ الشُّهُورِ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ اثْنَا عَشَرَ شَهْرًا فِي كِتَابِ اللَّهِ يَوْمَ خَلَقَ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضَ مِنْهَا أَرْبَعَةٌ حُرُمٌ‏} ‏ ‏{‏الْقَيِّمُ‏}‏ هُوَ الْقَائِمُ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,153,'9',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah: “...The second of two, when they (Muhammad ﷺ and Abü Bakr were in the cave, and he ﷺ said to his companion (Abu Bakr ) ‘Be not sad (or afraid), surely Allah is with us.''" (V.9:40)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏ثَانِيَ اثْنَيْنِ إِذْ هُمَا فِي الْغَارِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,154,'10',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah "...And (for) to attract the hearts of those who have been inclined (towards Islam) ; and to free the captives..." (V.9:60)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَالْمُؤَلَّفَةِ قُلُوبُهُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,155,'11',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah "Those who defame such of the believers who give charity (in Allah''s Cause) voluntarily..." (V.9:79)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏الَّذِينَ يَلْمِزُونَ الْمُطَّوِّعِينَ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,156,'12',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah ''Whether you (O Muhammad ﷺ ask forgiveness for them (hypocrites) or ask not forgiveness for them - (and even) if you ask seventy times for their forgiveness – Allah will not forgive them..." (V.9:80)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏اسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ أَوْ لاَ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ إِنْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ سَبْعِينَ مَرَّةً‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,157,'13',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah: ''And never (O Muhammad ﷺ ) pray (funeral prayer) for any of them (hypocrites) who dies, nor stand at his grave." (V.9:84)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَلاَ تُصَلِّ عَلَى أَحَدٍ مِنْهُمْ مَاتَ أَبَدًا وَلاَ تَقُمْ عَلَى قَبْرِهِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,158,'14',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah: "They will swear by Allah to you (Muslims) when you return to them, that you may turn away from them..." (V.9:95)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏سَيَحْلِفُونَ بِاللَّهِ لَكُمْ إِذَا انْقَلَبْتُمْ إِلَيْهِمْ لِتُعْرِضُوا عَنْهُمْ فَأَعْرِضُوا عَنْهُمْ إِنَّهُمْ رِجْسٌ وَمَأْوَاهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ جَزَاءً بِمَا كَانُوا يَكْسِبُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,159,'15',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah "And (there are) others who have acknowledged their sins..." (V.9:102)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَآخَرُونَ اعْتَرَفُوا بِذُنُوبِهِمْ خَلَطُوا عَمَلاً صَالِحًا وَآخَرَ سَيِّئًا عَسَى اللَّهُ أَنْ يَتُوبَ عَلَيْهِمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,160,'16',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah "It is not (proper) for the Prophet (ﷺ) and those who believe to ask for Allah''s forgiveness for the Mushrikun [polytheists, pagans, idolaters, and disbelievers in the Oneness of Allah and in His Messenger Muhammad ﷺ] . . ."(V.9 :113)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏مَا كَانَ لِلنَّبِيِّ وَالَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنْ يَسْتَغْفِرُوا لِلْمُشْرِكِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,161,'17',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah "Allah has forgiven the Prophet, the Muhãjirun and the Ansãr...'' (V.9:117)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏لَقَدْ تَابَ اللَّهُ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ وَالْمُهَاجِرِينَ وَالأَنْصَارِ الَّذِينَ اتَّبَعُوهُ فِي سَاعَةِ الْعُسْرَةِ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا كَادَ يَزِيغُ قُلُوبُ فَرِيقٍ مِنْهُمْ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ إِنَّهُ بِهِمْ رَءُوفٌ رَحِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,162,'18',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','And (He did forgive also) the three [who did not join the Tabuk expedition] till for them the earth, vast as it is, was straitened..." (V.9:118)','باب ‏ {‏وَعَلَى الثَّلاَثَةِ الَّذِينَ خُلِّفُوا حَتَّى إِذَا ضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمُ الأَرْضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتْ وَضَاقَتْ عَلَيْهِمْ أَنْفُسُهُمْ وَظَنُّوا أَنْ لاَ مَلْجَأَ مِنَ اللَّهِ إِلاَّ إِلَيْهِ ثُمَّ تَابَ عَلَيْهِمْ لِيَتُوبُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ هُوَ التَّوَّابُ الرَّحِيمُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,163,'19',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','"O you who believe! Be afraid of Allah, and be with those who are true (in words and deeds) ." (V.9:119)','باب ‏ {‏يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا اتَّقُوا اللَّهَ وَكُونُوا مَعَ الصَّادِقِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,164,'20',9,'Surat at-Tawbah (Repentance)','سورة بَرَاءَةَ','The Statement of Allah "Verily, there has come unto you a Messenger (Muhammad ﷺ) from amongst yourselves (i.e., whom you know well). It grieves him that you should receive any injury or difficulty..." (V.9:128)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏لَقَدْ جَاءَكُمْ رَسُولٌ مِنْ أَنْفُسِكُمْ عَزِيزٌ عَلَيْهِ مَا عَنِتُّمْ حَرِيصٌ عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْمُؤْمِنِينَ رَءُوفٌ رَحِيمٌ‏} ‏ مِنَ الرَّأْفَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,165,'1',10,'Surat Yunus (Jonah)','سورة يُونُسَ',NULL,'بَابٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,166,'2',10,'Surat Yunus (Jonah)','سورة يُونُسَ','"And We took the Children of Israel across the sea, and Fir''aun (Pharaoh) and his hosts followed them in oppression and enmity, till when the drowning overtook him, he said, ''I believe that La ilaha jib (Huwa) (none has the right to be worshipped but) He (Allah), in Whom the Children of IsrAel believe, and I am one of the Muslims (those who submit to Allah''s Will)." (V.10:90)','باب ‏ {‏وَجَاوَزْنَا بِبَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ الْبَحْرَ فَأَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ وَجُنُودُهُ بَغْيًا وَعَدْوًا حَتَّى إِذَا أَدْرَكَهُ الْغَرَقُ قَالَ آمَنْتُ أَنَّهُ لاَ إِلَهَ إِلاَّ الَّذِي آمَنَتْ بِهِ بَنُو إِسْرَائِيلَ وَأَنَا مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,167,'1',11,'Surat Hud (Hud)','سورة هُودٍ','"No doubt! They did fold up their breasts,  that they may hide from Him. Surely, even when they cover themselves with their garments, He knows what they conceal and what they reveal. Verily, He is the All-Knower of the (innermost secrets) of the breasts." (V.11:5)','باب ‏ {‏أَلاَ إِنَّهُمْ يَثْنُونَ صُدُورَهُمْ لِيَسْتَخْفُوا مِنْهُ أَلاَ حِينَ يَسْتَغْشُونَ ثِيَابَهُمْ يَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّونَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُونَ إِنَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُور‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,168,'2',11,'Surat Hud (Hud)','سورة هُودٍ','The Statement of Allah: "...And His Throne was on the water..." (V.11:7)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَكَانَ عَرْشُهُ عَلَى الْمَاءِ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,169,'3',11,'Surat Hud (Hud)','سورة هُودٍ','"And to the Madyan (Midian) people (We sent) their brother Shu''aib." (11:84)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِلَى مَدْيَنَ أَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,170,'4',11,'Surat Hud (Hud)','سورة هُودٍ','The Statement of Allah:"...The witnesses will say, ''These are the ones who lied..." (V.11:18)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَيَقُولُ الأَشْهَادُ هَؤُلاَءِ الَّذِينَ كَذَبُوا عَلَى رَبِّهِمْ أَلاَ لَعْنَةُ اللَّهِ عَلَى الظَّالِمِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,171,'5',11,'Surat Hud (Hud)','سورة هُودٍ','The Statement of Allah: "Such is the Seizure of your Lord when He seizes the (population of) towns while they are doing wrong. Verily, His Seizure is painful and severe." (V.11:102)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَكَذَلِكَ أَخْذُ رَبِّكَ إِذَا أَخَذَ الْقُرَى وَهِيَ ظَالِمَةٌ إِنَّ أَخْذَهُ أَلِيمٌ شَدِيدٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,172,'6',11,'Surat Hud (Hud)','سورة هُودٍ','The Statement of Allah: "And perform As-Salat (Iqa ma as-SaIãt)" at the two ends of the day, and in some hours of the night; [i.e ., five compulsory Salãt (prayers)]. Verily, the good deeds remove the evil deeds (small sins)…" (''V.11 :114)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏وَأَقِمِ الصَّلاَةَ طَرَفَىِ النَّهَارِ وَزُلَفًا مِنَ اللَّيْلِ إِنَّ الْحَسَنَاتِ يُذْهِبْنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ ذَلِكَ ذِكْرَى لِلذَّاكِرِينَ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,173,'1',12,'Surat Yusuf (Joseph)','سورة يُوسُفَ','The Statement of Allah: "...and perfect His Favour on you and on the offspring of Ya''qub (Jacob)..." (V.12:6)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَيُتِمُّ نِعْمَتَهُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلَى آلِ يَعْقُوبَ كَمَا أَتَمَّهَا عَلَى أَبَوَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ إِبْرَاهِيمَ وَإِسْحَاقَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,174,'2',12,'Surat Yusuf (Joseph)','سورة يُوسُفَ','The Statement of Allah: "Verily, in Yusuf (Joseph) and his brethren, there were Ayat (proofs, evidences, verses, lessons, signs, revelations, etc.) for those who ask." (V.12:7)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏لَقَدْ كَانَ فِي يُوسُفَ وَإِخْوَتِهِ آيَاتٌ لِلسَّائِلِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,175,'3',12,'Surat Yusuf (Joseph)','سورة يُوسُفَ','The Statement of Allah "He said, ''Nay, but your ownselves have made up a tale. So (for me), patience is most fitting. And it is Allah (Alone) Whose help can be sought against that (lie) which you describe." (V.12:18)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏قَالَ بَلْ سَوَّلَتْ لَكُمْ أَنْفُسُكُمْ أَمْرًا‏} ‏ ‏{‏سَوَّلَتْ‏}‏ زَيَّنَتْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,176,'4',12,'Surat Yusuf (Joseph)','سورة يُوسُفَ','The Statement of Allah: "And she, in whose house he was, sought to seduce him (to do an evil act). She closed the doors and said, ''Come on, O you.'' He said: ''I seek refuge in Allah (or Allah forbid)''..." (V.12:23)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَرَاوَدَتْهُ الَّتِي هُوَ فِي بَيْتِهَا عَنْ نَفْسِهِ وَغَلَّقَتِ الأَبْوَابَ وَقَالَتْ هَيْتَ لَكَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,177,'5',12,'Surat Yusuf (Joseph)','سورة يُوسُفَ','The Statement of Allah: "But when the messenger came to him, [Yusuf (Joseph)] said, ''Return to your lord..(up to).. the women said: Allah forbid." (V.12:50,51)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏فَلَمَّا جَاءَهُ الرَّسُولُ قَالَ ارْجِعْ إِلَى رَبِّكَ فَاسْأَلْهُ مَا بَالُ النِّسْوَةِ اللاَّتِي قَطَّعْنَ أَيْدِيَهُنَّ إِنَّ رَبِّي بِكَيْدِهِنَّ عَلِيمٌ * قَالَ مَا خَطْبُكُنَّ إِذْ رَاوَدْتُنَّ يُوسُفَ عَنْ نَفْسِهِ قُلْنَ حَاشَى لِلَّهِ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,178,'6',12,'Surat Yusuf (Joseph)','سورة يُوسُفَ','"(They were reprieved) until, when the Messengers gave up hope..." (V.12:110)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏حَتَّى إِذَا اسْتَيْأَسَ الرُّسُلُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,179,'1',13,'Surat ar-Ra’d (Thunder)','سورة الرَّعْدِ','The Statement of Allah: "Allah knows what every female bears, and by how much the wombs fall short (of their time or number)..." (V.13:8)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏اللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَحْمِلُ كُلُّ أُنْثَى وَمَا تَغِيضُ الأَرْحَامُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,180,'1',14,'Surat Ibraheem (Abraham)','سورة إِبْرَاهِيمَ','The Statement of Allah "... As a goodly tree, whose root is firmly fixed..." (V.14:24)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏كَشَجَرَةٍ طَيِّبَةٍ أَصْلُهَا ثَابِتٌ وَفَرْعُهَا فِي السَّمَاءِ * تُؤْتِي أُكْلَهَا كُلَّ حِينٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,181,'2',14,'Surat Ibraheem (Abraham)','سورة إِبْرَاهِيمَ','"Allah will keep firm those who believe with, the word that stands firm..." (V.14:27)','باب ‏ {‏يُثَبِّتُ اللَّهُ الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا بِالْقَوْلِ الثَّابِتِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,182,'3',14,'Surat Ibraheem (Abraham)','سورة إِبْرَاهِيمَ','"Have you not seen those who have changed the Blessings of Allah into disbelief?..." (V.14:28)','باب ‏ {‏أَلَمْ تَرَ إِلَى الَّذِينَ بَدَّلُوا نِعْمَةَ اللَّهِ كُفْرًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,183,'1',15,'Surat al-Hijr (The Stone Valley)','سورة الْحِجْرِ','The Statement of Allah: "Except him (devil) that gains hearing by stealing, he is pursued by a clear flaming fire." (V.15:18)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِلاَّ مَنِ اسْتَرَقَ السَّمْعَ فَأَتْبَعَهُ شِهَابٌ مُبِينٌ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,184,'2',15,'Surat al-Hijr (The Stone Valley)','سورة الْحِجْرِ','The Statement of Allah: "And verily, the dwellers of AI-Hijr (Rocky Tract, i.e., Thamud people) denied the Messengers." (V.15:80)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَلَقَدْ كَذَّبَ أَصْحَابُ الْحِجْرِ الْمُرْسَلِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,185,'3',15,'Surat al-Hijr (The Stone Valley)','سورة الْحِجْرِ','The Statement of Allah "And indeed, We have bestowed upon you seven Al-Mathãni (i.e., seven repeatedly recited Verses i.e., Sürat AI-Fatiha) and the Grand Qur''an." (V.15:87)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَلَقَدْ آتَيْنَاكَ سَبْعًا مِنَ الْمَثَانِي وَالْقُرْآنَ الْعَظِيمَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,186,'4',15,'Surat al-Hijr (The Stone Valley)','سورة الْحِجْرِ','The Statement of Allah "Who have made the Qur''an into parts (i.e., believed in one part and disbelieved in the other) ." (V.15:91)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏الَّذِينَ جَعَلُوا الْقُرْآنَ عِضِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,187,'5',15,'Surat al-Hijr (The Stone Valley)','سورة الْحِجْرِ','The Statement of Allah: "And worship your Lord until there comes unto you the certainty (i.e., death)." (V.15:99)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَاعْبُدْ رَبَّكَ حَتَّى يَأْتِيَكَ الْيَقِين‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,188,'1',16,'Surat an-Nahl (Bees)','سورة النَّحْلِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "...And of you there are some who are sent back to senility..." (V.16:70)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَمِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرَدُّ إِلَى أَرْذَلِ الْعُمُرِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,189,'1',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,190,'2',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','"And we decreed for the Children of Israel." (17:4)','‏ {‏وَقَضَيْنَا إِلَى بَنِي إِسْرَائِيلَ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,191,'3',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "Glorified (and Exalted) is He (Allah) [above all that (evil) they associate with Him], Who took His slave (Muḥammad pbuh) for a Journey by Night from Al-Masjid-al-Ḥarām (at Makkah) to Al-Masjid-al-Aqsā (in Jerusalem)..." (V.17:1)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏أَسْرَى بِعَبْدِهِ لَيْلاً مِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,192,'4',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "And indeed, We have honoured the Children of Adam..." (V.17:70)','باب قَوْلِهِ تَعَالَى ‏ {‏وَلَقَدْ كَرَّمْنَا بَنِي آدَمَ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,193,'4b',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','"And when We decide to destroy a town (population), We (first) send a definite order (to obey Allāh and be righteous) to those among them [or We (first) increase in number those of its population] who lead a life of luxury. Then they transgress therein..." (V.17:16)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِذَا أَرَدْنَا أَنْ نُهْلِكَ قَرْيَةً أَمَرْنَا مُتْرَفِيهَا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,194,'5',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','"O offspring of those whom We carried (in the ship) with Nūh (Noah)! Verily, he was a grateful slave." (V.17:3)','باب ‏ {‏ذُرِّيَّةَ مَنْ حَمَلْنَا مَعَ نُوحٍ إِنَّهُ كَانَ عَبْدًا شَكُورًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,195,'6',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "...And to Dāwūd (David) We gave the Zabūr (Psalms) ." (V.17:55)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَآتَيْنَا دَاوُدَ زَبُورًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,196,'7',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','"Say (O Muḥammad pbuh): ''Call upon those besides Him whom you pretend (to be gods)..." (V.17:56)','باب ‏ {‏قُلِ ادْعُوا الَّذِينَ زَعَمْتُمْ مِنْ دُونِهِ فَلاَ يَمْلِكُونَ كَشْفَ الضُّرِّ عَنْكُمْ وَلاَ تَحْوِيلاً‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,197,'8',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "Those whom they call upon [like ''Isa (Jesus) the son of Maryam (Mary), ''Uzair (Ezra) angels, etc.] desire (for themselves) means of access to their Lord (Allah)..." (V.17:57)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏أُولَئِكَ الَّذِينَ يَدْعُونَ يَبْتَغُونَ إِلَى رَبِّهِمِ الْوَسِيلَةَ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,198,'9',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','"And We made not the vision which We showed you (O Muḥammad [pbuh] as an actual eye-witness and not as a dream on the night of Al-Isrā'') , but a trial for mankind..." (V.17:60)','باب ‏ {‏وَمَا جَعَلْنَا الرُّؤْيَا الَّتِي أَرَيْنَاكَ إِلاَّ فِتْنَةً لِلنَّاسِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,199,'10',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Verily, the recitation of the Qur''ān in the early dawn (i.e. the morning - Fajr prayer) is ever witnessed (attended by the angels in charge of mankind of the day and the night) ." (V.17:78)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّ قُرْآنَ الْفَجْرِ كَانَ مَشْهُودًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,200,'11',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "It may be that your Lord will raise you to Maqām Mahmūd (a station of praise and glory, i.e., the honour of intercession on the Day of Resurrection) ." (V.17:79)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏عَسَى أَنْ يَبْعَثَكَ رَبُّكَ مَقَامًا مَحْمُودًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,201,'12',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','"And say ''Truth (i.e., Islamic Monotheism or this Qur''ān or Jihād against polytheists) has come and Bāṭil (falsehood i.e., Satan or polytheism, etc.) has vanished...''" (V.17:81)','باب ‏ {‏وَقُلْ جَاءَ الْحَقُّ وَزَهَقَ الْبَاطِلُ إِنَّ الْبَاطِلَ كَانَ زَهُوقًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,202,'13',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','"And they ask you (O Muḥammad pbuh) concerning the Rūḥ (the Spirit)..." (V.17:85)','باب ‏ {‏وَيَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ الرُّوحِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,203,'14',17,'Surat al-Isra’ (The Night Journey)','سورة بَنِى إِسْرَائِيلَ','"...And offer your Salāt (prayer) neither aloud nor in a low voice..." (V.17:110)','باب ‏ {‏وَلاَ تَجْهَرْ بِصَلاَتِكَ وَلاَ تُخَافِتْ بِهَا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,204,'1',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','"But man is ever more quarrelsome than anything." (V.18:54)','باب ‏{‏وَكَانَ الإِنْسَانُ أَكْثَرَ شَىْءٍ جَدَلاً‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,205,'2',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And (remember) when Mūsa (Moses) said to his boy-servant: ''I will not give up (travelling) until I reach the junction of the two seas or (until) I spend years and years in travelling." (V.18:60)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَى لِفَتَاهُ لاَ أَبْرَحُ حَتَّى أَبْلُغَ مَجْمَعَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ أَوْ أَمْضِيَ حُقُبًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,206,'3',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "But when they reached the junction of the two seas, they forgot their fish, and it took its way through the sea as in a tunnel." (V.18:61)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَلَمَّا بَلَغَا مَجْمَعَ بَيْنِهِمَا نَسِيَا حُوتَهُمَا فَاتَّخَذَ سَبِيلَهُ فِي الْبَحْرِ سَرَبًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,207,'4',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "So, when they had passed further on (beyond that fixed place), Mūsa (Moses) said to his boy-servant, ''Bring us our morning meal; truly, we have suffered much fatigue in this, our journey... (up to) retracing their footsteps!" (V.18:62,63)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَلَمَّا جَاوَزَا قَالَ لِفَتَاهُ آتِنَا غَدَاءَنَا لَقَدْ لَقِينَا مِنْ سَفَرِنَا هَذَا نَصَبًا‏} ‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏قَصَصًا}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,208,'5',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Say (O Muḥammad pbuh): ''Shall We tell you the greatest losers in respect of (their) deeds?" (V.18:103)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏قُلْ هَلْ نُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِالأَخْسَرِينَ أَعْمَالاً‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,209,'6',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allāh the Exalted: "He said: ''Do you remember when we betook ourselves to the rock." (V.18:63)','باب ‏ {‏قَالَ أَرَأَيْتَ إِذْ أَوَيْنَا إِلَى الصَّخْرَةِ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,210,'7',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','"They are those who deny in the Ayāt (proofs, evidences, verses, lessons, signs, revelations, etc.) of their Lord and the Meeting with Him (in the Hereafter). So their works are in vain..." (V.18:105)','باب ‏ {‏أُولَئِكَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآيَاتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَلِقَائِهِ فَحَبِطَتْ أَعْمَالُهُمْ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,211,'1',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','"But man is ever more quarrelsome than anything." (V.18:54)','باب ‏{‏وَكَانَ الإِنْسَانُ أَكْثَرَ شَىْءٍ جَدَلاً‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,212,'2',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And (remember) when Mūsa (Moses) said to his boy-servant: ''I will not give up (travelling) until I reach the junction of the two seas or (until) I spend years and years in travelling." (V.18:60)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِذْ قَالَ مُوسَى لِفَتَاهُ لاَ أَبْرَحُ حَتَّى أَبْلُغَ مَجْمَعَ الْبَحْرَيْنِ أَوْ أَمْضِيَ حُقُبًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,213,'3',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "But when they reached the junction of the two seas, they forgot their fish, and it took its way through the sea as in a tunnel." (V.18:61)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَلَمَّا بَلَغَا مَجْمَعَ بَيْنِهِمَا نَسِيَا حُوتَهُمَا فَاتَّخَذَ سَبِيلَهُ فِي الْبَحْرِ سَرَبًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,214,'4',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "So, when they had passed further on (beyond that fixed place), Mūsa (Moses) said to his boy-servant, ''Bring us our morning meal; truly, we have suffered much fatigue in this, our journey... (up to) retracing their footsteps!" (V.18:62,63)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَلَمَّا جَاوَزَا قَالَ لِفَتَاهُ آتِنَا غَدَاءَنَا لَقَدْ لَقِينَا مِنْ سَفَرِنَا هَذَا نَصَبًا‏} ‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏قَصَصًا}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,215,'5',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Say (O Muḥammad pbuh): ''Shall We tell you the greatest losers in respect of (their) deeds?" (V.18:103)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏قُلْ هَلْ نُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِالأَخْسَرِينَ أَعْمَالاً‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,216,'6',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','The Statement of Allāh the Exalted: "He said: ''Do you remember when we betook ourselves to the rock." (V.18:63)','باب ‏ {‏قَالَ أَرَأَيْتَ إِذْ أَوَيْنَا إِلَى الصَّخْرَةِ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,217,'7',18,'Surat al-Kahf (The Cave)','سورة الْكَهْفِ','"They are those who deny in the Ayāt (proofs, evidences, verses, lessons, signs, revelations, etc.) of their Lord and the Meeting with Him (in the Hereafter). So their works are in vain..." (V.18:105)','باب ‏ {‏أُولَئِكَ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا بِآيَاتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَلِقَائِهِ فَحَبِطَتْ أَعْمَالُهُمْ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,218,'1',19,'Surat Maryam (Mary)','كهيعص','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And warn them (O Muḥammad pbuh) of the Day of grief and regrets..." (V.19:39)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَأَنْذِرْهُمْ يَوْمَ الْحَسْرَةِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,219,'2',19,'Surat Maryam (Mary)','كهيعص','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And we (angels) descend not except by the Command of your Lord (O Muḥammad pbuh). To Him belongs what is before us and what is behind us and what is between those two..." (V.19:64)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَمَا نَتَنَزَّلُ إِلاَّ بِأَمْرِ رَبِّكَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,220,'3',19,'Surat Maryam (Mary)','كهيعص','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "Have you seen him who disbelieved in Our Ayāt (this Qur''an and Muḥammad pbuh) and said: ''I shall certainly be given wealth and children?" (V.19:77)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏أَفَرَأَيْتَ الَّذِي كَفَرَ بِآيَاتِنَا وَقَالَ لأُوتَيَنَّ مَالاً وَوَلَدًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,221,'4',19,'Surat Maryam (Mary)','كهيعص','"Has he known the Unseen, or has he taken a convenant from the Most Gracious (Allāh)?" (V.19:78)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏أَطَّلَعَ الْغَيْبَ أَمِ اتَّخَذَ عِنْدَ الرَّحْمَنِ عَهْدًا‏} ‏ قَالَ مَوْثِقًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,222,'5',19,'Surat Maryam (Mary)','كهيعص','"Nay, We shall record what he says, and We shall increase his torment (in the Hell) ." (V.19:79)','باب ‏ {‏كَلاَّ سَنَكْتُبُ مَا يَقُولُ وَنَمُدُّ لَهُ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ مَدًّا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,223,'6',19,'Surat Maryam (Mary)','كهيعص','"And We shall inherit from him (at his death) all that he talks of (i.e., wealth and children which Allah has bestowed upon him in this world), and he shall come to Us alone." (V.19:80)','باب قَوْلِهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ‏ {‏وَنَرِثُهُ مَا يَقُولُ وَيَأْتِينَا فَرْدًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,224,'1',20,'Surat Ta Ha (Ta-Ha)','سورة طه','The Statement of Allāh the Exalted: "And I have chosen you for Myself." (V.20:41) (i.e., for My Revelation and My Message, or created you for Myself or strengthened and taught you as to how to preach My Message to My worshippers)] ."','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَاصْطَنَعْتُكَ لِنَفْسِي‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,225,'2',20,'Surat Ta Ha (Ta-Ha)','سورة طه','"And indeed We revealed to Musa (Moses) (saying): ''Travel by night with ''Ibâdi (My slaves) and strike a dry path for them in the sea, fearing neither to be overtaken [by Fir''aūn (Pharaoh)], nor being afraid (of drowning in the sea).'' Then Fir''aūn (Pharaoh) pursued them with his hosts, but the sea-water completely overwhelmed them and covered them up. And Fir''aun (Pharaoh) led his people astray, and he did not guide them." (V.20:77-79)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَلَقَدْ أَوْحَيْنَا إِلَى مُوسَى أَنْ أَسْرِ بِعِبَادِي فَاضْرِبْ لَهُمْ طَرِيقًا فِي الْبَحْرِ يَبَسًا لاَ تَخَافُ دَرَكًا وَلاَ تَخْشَى * فَأَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ بِجُنُودِهِ فَغَشِيَهُمْ مِنَ الْيَمِّ مَا غَشِيَهُمْ * وَأَضَلَّ فِرْعَوْنُ قَوْمَهُ وَمَا هَدَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,226,'3',20,'Surat Ta Ha (Ta-Ha)','سورة طه','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "...So let him not get you both out of Paradise, so that you be distressed." (V.20:117)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَلاَ يُخْرِجَنَّكُمَا مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ فَتَشْقَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,227,NULL,21,'Surat al-Anbiya’ (The Prophets)','سورة الأَنْبِيَاءِ','Surat al-Anbiya’ (The Prophets)','سورة الأَنْبِيَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,228,'2',21,'Surat al-Anbiya’ (The Prophets)','سورة الأَنْبِيَاءِ','"As We began the first creation, We shall repeat it. (It is) a promise binding upon Us. Truly, We shall do it." (V.21:104)','باب ‏ {‏كَمَا بَدَأْنَا أَوَّلَ خَلْقٍ نُّعِيدُهُ ۚ وَعْدًا عَلَيْنَا ۚ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,229,'1',22,'Surat al-Hajj (The Pilgrimage)','سورة الْحَجِّ','The Statement of Allah the Most High.: "...And you shall see mankind as in a drunken state..." (V.22:2)','باب ‏ {‏وَتَرَى النَّاسَ سُكَارَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,230,'2',22,'Surat al-Hajj (The Pilgrimage)','سورة الْحَجِّ','"And among mankind is he who worships Allah as it were, upon the very edge (i.e., in doubt)..." (V.22:11)','باب ‏ {‏وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَعْبُدُ اللَّهَ عَلَى حَرْفٍ فَإِنْ أَصَابَهُ خَيْرٌ اطْمَأَنَّ بِهِ وَإِنْ أَصَابَتْهُ فِتْنَةٌ انْقَلَبَ عَلَى وَجْهِهِ خَسِرَ الدُّنْيَا وَالآخِرَةَ‏} ‏ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏ذَلِكَ هُوَ الضَّلاَلُ الْبَعِيدُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,231,'3',22,'Surat al-Hajj (The Pilgrimage)','سورة الْحَجِّ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "These two opponents (believers and disbelievers) dispute with each other about their Lord..." (V.22:19)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏هَذَانِ خَصْمَانِ اخْتَصَمُوا فِي رَبِّهِمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,232,'1',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And for those who accuse their wives, but have no witnesses except themselves..." (V.24:6)','باب قَوْلِهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ‏ {‏وَالَّذِينَ يَرْمُونَ أَزْوَاجَهُمْ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ لَهُمْ شُهَدَاءُ إِلاَّ أَنْفُسُهُمْ فَشَهَادَةُ أَحَدِهِمْ أَرْبَعُ شَهَادَاتٍ بِاللَّهِ إِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,233,'2',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','"And the fifth (testimony should be) the invoking of the Curse of Allah on him if he is of those who tell a lie (against her) ." (V.24:7)','باب ‏ {‏وَالْخَامِسَةُ أَنَّ لَعْنَةَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ إِنْ كَانَ مِنَ الْكَاذِبِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,234,'3',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','"But it shall avert the punishment (of stoning to death) from her..." (V.24:8)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَيَدْرَأُ عَنْهَا الْعَذَابَ أَنْ تَشْهَدَ أَرْبَعَ شَهَادَاتٍ بِاللَّهِ إِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الْكَاذِبِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,235,'4',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And the fifth (testimony) should be that the Wrath of Allah be upon her if he (her husband) speaks the truth." (V.24:9)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَالْخَامِسَةُ أَنَّ غَضَبَ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهَا إِنْ كَانَ مِنَ الصَّادِقِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,236,'5',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "Verily! Those who brought forth the slander (against ''Aishah [May Allah be pleased with her] the wife of the Prophet pbuh) are a group among you." (V.24:11)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّ الَّذِينَ جَاءُوا بِالإِفْكِ عُصْبَةٌ مِنْكُمْ لاَ تَحْسِبُوهُ شَرًّا لَكُمْ بَلْ هُوَ خَيْرٌ لَكُمْ لِكُلِّ امْرِئٍ مِنْهُمْ مَا اكْتَسَبَ مِنَ الإِثْمِ وَالَّذِي تَوَلَّى كِبْرَهُ مِنْهُمْ لَهُ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ‏} ‏ أَفَّاكٌ كَذَّابٌ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,237,'6',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','"Why then did not the believers, men and women, when you heard it (the slander) think good of their own people and say: ''This (charge) is an obvious lie... (up to) ... Then with Allah they are the liars." (V.24: 12-13)','باب ‏ {‏لَوْلاَ إِذْ سَمِعْتُمُوهُ ظَنَّ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ، وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتُ، بِأَنْفُسِهِمْ خَيْرًا وَقَالُوا هَذَا إِفْكٌ مُبِينٌ. لَّوْلَا جَاءُوا عَلَيْهِ بِأَرْبَعَةِ شُهَدَاءَ ۚ فَإِذْ لَمْ يَأْتُوا بِالشُّهَدَاءِ فَأُولَٰئِكَ عِندَ اللَّهِ هُمُ الْكَاذِبُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,238,'7',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Had it not been for the Grace of Allah and His Mercy unto you in this world and in the Hereafter, a great torment would have touched you for that whereof you had spoken." (V.24:14)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَلَوْلاَ فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهُ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالآخِرَةِ لَمَسَّكُمْ فِيمَا أَفَضْتُمْ فِيهِ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,239,'8',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','"When you were propagating it with your tongues, and uttering with your mouths that whereof you had no knowledge..." (V.24:15)','باب ‏ {‏إِذْ تَلَقَّوْنَهُ بِأَلْسِنَتِكُمْ وَتَقُولُونَ بِأَفْوَاهِكُمْ مَا لَيْسَ لَكُمْ بِهِ عِلْمٌ وَتَحْسِبُونَهُ هَيِّنًا وَهْوَ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ عَظِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,240,'8b',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','"And why did you not, when you heard it, say: It is not right for us to speak of this..." (V.24:16)','باب ‏ {‏وَلَوْلاَ إِذْ سَمِعْتُمُوهُ قُلْتُمْ، مَا يَكُونُ لَنَا أَنْ نَتَكَلَّمَ، بِهَذَا سُبْحَانَكَ هَذَا بُهْتَانٌ عَظِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,241,'9',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And warns you not to repeat the like of it, forever." (V.24:17)','باب ‏ {‏يَعِظُكُمُ اللَّهُ أَنْ تَعُودُوا لِمِثْلِهِ أَبَدًا‏} ‏  الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,242,'10',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','The Statement of Allah: "And Allāh makes the Ayāt (proofs, evidences, verses, lessons, signs, revelations, etc.) plain to you. And Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise." (V.24:18)','باب ‏ {‏وَيُبَيِّنُ اللَّهُ لَكُمُ الآيَاتِ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,243,'11',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','"Verily, those who like that (the crime of) illegal sexual intercourse should be propagated about those who believe... (up to) ... and that Allah is full of kindness, Most Merciful." (V.24:19,20) "And let not those among you who are blessed with graces and wealth swear not to give (any sort of help) to their kinsmen, Al-Masākīn (the poor)... (up to) ... And Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful." (V.24:22)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يُحِبُّونَ أَنْ تَشِيعَ الْفَاحِشَةُ فِي الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالآخِرَةِ وَاللَّهُ يَعْلَمُ وَأَنْتُمْ لاَ تَعْلَمُونَ * وَلَوْلاَ فَضْلُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَتُهُ وَأَنَّ اللَّهَ رَءُوفٌ رَحِيمٌ‏} ‏ ‏{‏وَلاَ يَأْتَلِ أُولُو الْفَضْلِ مِنْكُمْ وَالسَّعَةِ أَنْ يُؤْتُوا أُولِي الْقُرْبَى وَالْمَسَاكِينَ وَالْمُهَاجِرِينَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَلْيَعْفُوا وَلْيَصْفَحُوا أَلاَ تُحِبُّونَ أَنْ يَغْفِرَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ‏}‏‏ .‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,244,'12',24,'Surat an-Nur (The Light)','سورة النُّورِ','"... and to draw their veils all over their Juyubihinna (i.e., their bodies, faces, necks and bosoms)..." (V.24:31)','باب ‏ {‏وَلْيَضْرِبْنَ بِخُمُرِهِنَّ عَلَى جُيُوبِهِنَّ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,245,'1',25,'Surat al-Furqan (The Standard)','سورة الْفُرْقَانِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Those who will be gathered to Hell (prone) on their faces..." (V.25:34)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏الَّذِينَ يُحْشَرُونَ عَلَى وُجُوهِهِمْ إِلَى جَهَنَّمَ أُولَئِكَ شَرٌّ مَكَانًا وَأَضَلُّ سَبِيلاً‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,246,'2',25,'Surat al-Furqan (The Standard)','سورة الْفُرْقَانِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And those who invoke not any other ilāh (God) along with Allah, nor kill such person..." (V.25:68)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَالَّذِينَ لاَ يَدْعُونَ مَعَ اللَّهِ إِلَهًا آخَرَ وَلاَ يَقْتُلُونَ النَّفْسَ الَّتِي حَرَّمَ اللَّهُ إِلاَّ بِالْحَقِّ وَلاَ يَزْنُونَ وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ ذَلِكَ يَلْقَ أَثَامًا‏} ‏ الْعُقُوبَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,247,'3',25,'Surat al-Furqan (The Standard)','سورة الْفُرْقَانِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "The torment will be doubled to him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will abide therein in disgrace." (V.25:69)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏يُضَاعَفْ لَهُ الْعَذَابُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَيَخْلُدْ فِيهِ مُهَانًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,248,'4',25,'Surat al-Furqan (The Standard)','سورة الْفُرْقَانِ','"Except those who repent and believe (in the Islamic Monotheism) and do righteous deeds, for those, Allah will change their sins into good deeds, and Allah is Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful." (V.25:70)','باب ‏{‏إِلاَّ مَنْ تَابَ وَآمَنَ وَعَمِلَ عَمَلاً صَالِحًا فَأُولَئِكَ يُبَدِّلُ اللَّهُ سَيِّئَاتِهِمْ حَسَنَاتٍ وَكَانَ اللَّهُ غَفُورًا رَحِيمًا‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,249,'5',25,'Surat al-Furqan (The Standard)','سورة الْفُرْقَانِ','. "... So the torment will be yours for ever" (V.25:77)','باب ‏ {‏فَسَوْفَ يَكُونُ لِزَامًا‏} ‏ هَلَكَةً'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,250,'1',26,'Surat ash-Shu’ara’ (The Poets)','سورة الشُّعَرَاءِ','"And disgrace me not on the day when (all the creatures) will be resurrected." (V.26:87)','باب ‏ {‏وَلاَ تُخْزِنِي يَوْمَ يُبْعَثُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,251,'2',26,'Surat ash-Shu’ara’ (The Poets)','سورة الشُّعَرَاءِ','"And warn your tribe (O Muḥammad pbuh) of near kindred. And be kind and humble to the believers who follow you.. ." (V.26:214-215)','باب ‏ {‏وَأَنْذِرْ عَشِيرَتَكَ الأَقْرَبِينَ * وَاخْفِضْ جَنَاحَكَ‏} ‏ أَلِنْ جَانِبَكَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,252,'1',28,'Surat al-Qasas (The Whole Story)','سورة الْقَصَصِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "Verily! You (O Muḥammad pbuh) guide not whom you like, but Allah guides whom He wills..." (V.28:56)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّكَ لاَ تَهْدِي مَنْ أَحْبَبْتَ وَلَكِنَّ اللَّهَ يَهْدِي مَنْ يَشَاءُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,253,'2',28,'Surat al-Qasas (The Whole Story)','سورة الْقَصَصِ','"Verily, He Who has given you  (O Muḥammad pbuh) the Qur''an..." (V.28:85)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّ الَّذِي فَرَضَ عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْآنَ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,254,NULL,30,'Surat ar-Rum (The Romans)','سورة الرُّومِ','Surat ar-Rum (The Romans)','سورة الرُّومِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,255,NULL,30,'Surat ar-Rum (The Romans)','سورة الرُّومِ','Allah''s Statement: "...No change let there be in Khalq-illāh (i.e., the religion of Allāh - Islamic Monotheism)..." (V.30:30)','باب ‏ {‏لاَ تَبْدِيلَ لِخَلْقِ اللَّهِ‏} ‏ لِدِينِ اللَّهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,256,'1',31,'Surat Luqman (Luqman)','سورة لُقْمَانَ','"... Join not in worship others with Allah. Verily! Joining others in worship with Allah is a great Ẓulm (wrong) indeed." (V.31:13)','باب ‏{‏لاَ تُشْرِكْ بِاللَّهِ إِنَّ الشِّرْكَ لَظُلْمٌ عَظِيمٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,257,'2',31,'Surat Luqman (Luqman)','سورة لُقْمَانَ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "Verily, Allah! With Him (Alone) is the knowledge of the Hour..." (V.31:34)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّ اللَّهَ عِنْدَهُ عِلْمُ السَّاعَةِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,258,'1',32,'Surat as-Sajdah (The Prostration)','سورة السَّجْدَةِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "No person knows what is kept hidden for them of joy..." (V.32:17)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَلاَ تَعْلَمُ نَفْسٌ مَا أُخْفِيَ لَهُمْ‏ مِّن قُرَّةِ أَعْيُنٍ} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,259,'1',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,260,'2',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','"Call them (adopted sons) by (the names of) their fathers. That is more just with Allah..." (V.33:5)','باب ‏ {‏ادْعُوهُمْ لآبَائِهِمْ هُوَ أَقْسَطُ عِندَ اللَّهِ ۚ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,261,'3',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','"Of them, some have fulfilled their obligations (i.e ., have been martyred) and some of them are still waiting, but they have never changed (i.e., they never proved treacherous to their covenant which they concluded with Allah) in the least." (V.33:23)','باب ‏ {‏فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ قَضَى نَحْبَهُ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَنْتَظِرُ وَمَا بَدَّلُوا تَبْدِيلاً‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,262,'4',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','The Statement of Allah (the Exalted): "O Prophet! (Muḥammad pbuh)! Say to your wives: ''If you desire the life of this world and its glitter, - then come! I will make a provision for you and set you free in a handsome manner (divorce)''." (V.33:28)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ قُلْ لأَزْوَاجِكَ إِنْ كُنْتُنَّ تُرِدْنَ الْحَيَاةَ الدُّنْيَا وَزِينَتَهَا فَتَعَالَيْنَ أُمَتِّعْكُنَّ وَأُسَرِّحْكُنَّ سَرَاحًا جَمِيلاً‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,263,'5',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "But if you desire Allah and His Messenger, and the home of the Hereafter, then verily, Allah has prepared for Al-Muhsināt (good-doers) amongst you an enormous reward." (V.33:29)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَإِنْ كُنْتُنَّ تُرِدْنَ اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ وَالدَّارَ الآخِرَةَ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ أَعَدَّ لِلْمُحْسِنَاتِ مِنْكُنَّ أَجْرًا عَظِيمًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,264,'6',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And (remember) when you said to him (Zaid bin Haritha [may Allah be pleased with him] - the freed slave of the Prophet pbuh) on whom Allah has bestowed grace (by guiding him to Islam) and you (O Muḥammad pbuh too) have done favour (by manumitting him): ''Keep your wife to yourself and fear Allah.'' But you did hide in yourself (i.e., what Allah has already made known to you that He will give her to you in marriage) that which Allah will make manifest, you did fear people (i.e., Muḥammad pbuh married the divorced wife of his manumitted slave) whereas Allah had a better right that you should fear Him..." (V.33:37)','باب ‏ {‏وَتُخْفِي فِي نَفْسِكَ مَا اللَّهُ مُبْدِيهِ وَتَخْشَى النَّاسَ وَاللَّهُ أَحَقُّ أَنْ تَخْشَاهُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,265,'7',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "You (O Muḥammad pbuh) can postpone (the turn of) whom you will of them (your wives), and you may receive whom you will. And whomsoever you desire of those whom you have set aside (her turn temporarily), it is no sin on you (to receive her again)..." (V.33:51)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏تُرْجِئُ مَنْ تَشَاءُ مِنْهُنَّ وَتُؤْوِي إِلَيْكَ مَنْ تَشَاءُ وَمَنِ ابْتَغَيْتَ مِمَّنْ عَزَلْتَ فَلاَ جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكَ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,266,'8',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "...O you who believe! Enter not the Prophet''s houses, except when leave is given to you for a meal... (up to) ... Verily! With Allah that shall be an enormity." (V.33:53)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏لاَ تَدْخُلُوا بُيُوتَ النَّبِيِّ إِلاَّ أَنْ يُؤْذَنَ لَكُمْ إِلَى طَعَامٍ غَيْرَ نَاظِرِينَ إِنَاهُ وَلَكِنْ إِذَا دُعِيتُمْ فَادْخُلُوا فَإِذَا طَعِمْتُمْ فَانْتَشِرُوا وَلاَ مُسْتَأْنِسِينَ لِحَدِيثٍ إِنَّ ذَلِكُمْ كَانَ يُؤْذِي النَّبِيَّ فَيَسْتَحْيِي مِنْكُمْ وَاللَّهُ لاَ يَسْتَحْيِي مِنَ الْحَقِّ وَإِذَا سَأَلْتُمُوهُنَّ مَتَاعًا فَاسْأَلُوهُنَّ مِنْ وَرَاءِ حِجَابٍ ذَلِكُمْ أَطْهَرُ لِقُلُوبِكُمْ وَقُلُوبِهِنَّ وَمَا كَانَ لَكُمْ أَنْ تُؤْذُوا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ وَلاَ أَنْ تَنْكِحُوا أَزْوَاجَهُ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ أَبَدًا إِنَّ ذَلِكُمْ كَانَ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ عَظِيمًا‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,267,'9',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: “Whether you reveal anything or conceal it, verily, Allah is [the] Ever All-Knower of everything... (up to) ... Verily, Allah is Ever All-Witness over everything." (V-33:54,55)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏إِنْ تُبْدُوا شَيْئًا أَوْ تُخْفُوهُ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيمًا * لاَ جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِنَّ فِي آبَائِهِنَّ وَلاَ أَبْنَائِهِنَّ وَلاَ إِخْوَانِهِنَّ وَلاَ أَبْنَاءِ إِخْوَانِهِنَّ وَلاَ أَبْنَاءِ أَخَوَاتِهِنَّ وَلاَ نِسَائِهِنَّ وَلاَ مَا مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُهُنَّ وَاتَّقِينَ اللَّهَ إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيدً‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,268,'10',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Allah sends His Salāt (Graces, Honours, Blessings and Mercy) on the Prophet (Muḥammad pbuh) and also His angels (ask Allah to bless and forgive him)..." (V.33:56)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّ اللَّهَ وَمَلاَئِكَتَهُ يُصَلُّونَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا صَلُّوا عَلَيْهِ وَسَلِّمُوا تَسْلِيمًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,269,'11',33,'Surat al-Ahzab (The Enemy Alliance)','سورة الأَحْزَابِ','"Be you not like those who annoyed Mūsa (Moses)." (V.33:69)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏لاَ تَكُونُوا كَالَّذِينَ آذَوْا مُوسَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,270,'1',34,'Surat Saba’ (Sheba)','سورة سَبَإٍ','"...So much so that when fear is banished from their (angels'') hearts, they (angels) say: ''What is it that your Lord has said?'' They say: ''The truth. And He is the Most High, the Most Great.''" (V.34:23).','باب ‏ {‏حَتَّى إِذَا فُزِّعَ عَنْ قُلُوبِهِمْ، قَالُوا مَاذَا قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ قَالُوا الْحَقَّ وَهُوَ الْعَلِيُّ الْكَبِيرُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,271,'2',34,'Surat Saba’ (Sheba)','سورة سَبَإٍ','"...He (Muḥammad pbuh) is only a warner to you in face of a severe torment." (V.34:46)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏إِنْ هُوَ إِلاَّ نَذِيرٌ لَكُمْ بَيْنَ يَدَىْ عَذَابٍ شَدِيدٍ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,272,'1',36,'Surat Ya Seen (Ya-Seen)','سورة ‏{‏يس‏}‏','Allah''s Statement: "And the sun runs on its fixed course for a term (appointed). That is the Decree of the All Mighty, the All-Knowing." (V.36:38)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَالشَّمْسُ تَجْرِي لِمُسْتَقَرٍّ لَهَا ذَلِكَ تَقْدِيرُ الْعَزِيزِ الْعَلِيمِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,273,'1',37,'Surat as-Saffat (Those Angles Lined up in Ranks)','سورة الصَّافَّاتِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And, verily, Yūnus (Jonah) was one of the Messengers." (V.37:139)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَإِنَّ يُونُسَ لَمِنَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,274,NULL,38,'Surat Sad (Sad)','سورة ص','Surat Sad (Sad)','سورة ص'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,275,'2',38,'Surat Sad (Sad)','سورة ص','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "He (Solomon peace be upon him) said: "My Lord! Forgive me. And bestow upon me a kingdom such as shall not belong to any other after me. Verily, You are the Bestower." (V.38:35)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏هَبْ لِي مُلْكًا لاَ يَنْبَغِي لأَحَدٍ مِنْ بَعْدِي إِنَّكَ أَنْتَ الْوَهَّابُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,276,'3',38,'Surat Sad (Sad)','سورة ص','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "...Nor am I one of the Mutakallifūn (those who pretend and fabricate things which do not exist) ." (V.38:86)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَمَا أَنَا مِنَ الْمُتَكَلِّفِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,277,'1',39,'Surat az-Zumar (The Successive Groups)','سورة الزُّمَرِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: Say: "O ''Ibādi (My slaves) who have transgressed against themselves (by committing evil deeds and sins)! Despair not of the Mercy of Allah..." (V39:53)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏يَا عِبَادِيَ الَّذِينَ أَسْرَفُوا عَلَى أَنْفُسِهِمْ لاَ تَقْنَطُوا مِنْ رَحْمَةِ اللَّهِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَغْفِرُ الذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًا إِنَّهُ هُوَ الْغَفُورُ الرَّحِيمُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,278,'2',39,'Surat az-Zumar (The Successive Groups)','سورة الزُّمَرِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "They made not a just estimate of Allah such as is due to Him..." (V.39:67)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَمَا قَدَرُوا اللَّهَ حَقَّ قَدْرِهِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,279,'3',39,'Surat az-Zumar (The Successive Groups)','سورة الزُّمَرِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "...And on the Day of Resurrection, the whole of the earth will be grasped by His Hand and the heavens will be rolled up in His Right Hand..." (V.39:67)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَالأَرْضُ جَمِيعًا قَبْضَتُهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ وَالسَّمَوَاتُ مَطْوِيَّاتٌ بِيَمِينِهِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,280,'4',39,'Surat az-Zumar (The Successive Groups)','سورة الزُّمَرِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "And the Trumpet will be blown, and all who are in the heavens and all who are on earth will swoon away, except him whom Allah wills..." (V.39:68)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَنُفِخَ فِي الصُّورِ فَصَعِقَ مَنْ فِي السَّمَوَاتِ وَمَنْ فِي الأَرْضِ إِلاَّ مَنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ ثُمَّ نُفِخَ فِيهِ أُخْرَى فَإِذَا هُمْ قِيَامٌ يَنْظُرُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,281,NULL,40,'Surat Ghafir (The Forgiver)','سورة الْمُؤْمِنُ','Surat Ghafir (The Forgiver)','سورة الْمُؤْمِنُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,282,'1',41,'Surat Fussilat (Verses Perfectly Explained)','سورة حم السَّجْدَةِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "And you have not been hiding yourself (in the world), lest your ears, and your eyes, and your skins should testify against you..." (V.41:22)','باب ‏ {‏وَمَا كُنْتُمْ تَسْتَتِرُونَ أَنْ يَشْهَدَ عَلَيْكُمْ سَمْعُكُمْ وَلاَ أَبْصَارُكُمْ وَلاَ جُلُودُكُمْ وَلَكِنْ ظَنَنْتُمْ أَنَّ اللَّهَ لاَ يَعْلَمُ كَثِيرًا مِمَّا تَعْمَلُونَ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,283,'2',41,'Surat Fussilat (Verses Perfectly Explained)','سورة حم السَّجْدَةِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "And that thought of yours which you thought about your Lord, has brought you to destruction, and you have become (this Day) of those utterly lost!" (V.41:23)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَذَلِكُمْ ظَنُّكُمُ الَّذِي ظَنَنْتُمْ بِرَبِّكُمْ أَرْدَاكُمْ فَأَصْبَحْتُمْ مِنَ الْخَاسِرِينَ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,284,'1',42,'Surat ash-Shura (Consultation)','سورة حم عسق','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "...Except to be kind to me for my kinship with you..." (V.42:23)','باب ‏ {‏إِلاَّ الْمَوَدَّةَ فِي الْقُرْبَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,285,'1',43,'Surat az-Zukhruf (Ornaments)','سورة حم الزُّخْرُفِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And they will cry: "O Mālik (Keeper of Hell)! Let your Lord make an end of us'' He will say, ''Verily, you shall abide forever.''" (V.43:77)','باب ‏ {‏وَنَادَوْا يَا مَالِكُ لِيَقْضِ عَلَيْنَا رَبُّكَ‏} الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,286,'2',43,'Surat az-Zukhruf (Ornaments)','سورة حم الزُّخْرُفِ','"Shall we then (warn you not and) take away the Reminder (this Qur''an) from you, because you are a people Musrifun." (1) (V.43:5)  (1) (Chap. 2) Musrifun: These who transgress the limits, as sinners, polytheists, idolaters, and disbelievers in the Oneness of Allah and in His Messenger Muḥammad peace be upon him.','بَابُ ‏ {‏أَفَنَضْرِبُ عَنْكُمُ الذِّكْرَ صَفْحًا أَنْ كُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا مُسْرِفِينَ‏} ‏ مُشْرِكِينَ‏.'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,287,'1',44,'Surat ad-Dukhan (The Haze )','سورة حم الدُّخَانِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Then wait you for the Day when the sky will bring forth a visible smoke." (V.44:10)','باب ‏ {‏يَوْمَ تَأْتِي السَّمَاءُ بِدُخَانٍ مُبِينٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,288,'2',44,'Surat ad-Dukhan (The Haze )','سورة حم الدُّخَانِ','"Covering the people, this is a painful torment." (V.44:11)','باب ‏ {‏يَغْشَى النَّاسَ هَذَا عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,289,'3',44,'Surat ad-Dukhan (The Haze )','سورة حم الدُّخَانِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "(They will say) Our Lord! Remove the torment from us, really we shall become believers!" (V.44:12)','باب ‏ {‏رَبَّنَا اكْشِفْ عَنَّا الْعَذَابَ إِنَّا مُؤْمِنُونَ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,290,'4',44,'Surat ad-Dukhan (The Haze )','سورة حم الدُّخَانِ','"How can there be for them an admonition (at the time when the torment has reached them), when a Messenger explaining things clearly, has already come to them?" (V.44:13)','باب ‏ {‏أَنَّى لَهُمُ الذِّكْرَى وَقَدْ جَاءَهُمْ رَسُولٌ مُبِينٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,291,'5',44,'Surat ad-Dukhan (The Haze )','سورة حم الدُّخَانِ','"Then they had turned away from him (Messenger Muḥammad PBUH) and said: (He is) taught (by a human being), a madman!" (V.44:14)','باب ‏ {‏ثُمَّ تَوَلَّوْا عَنْهُ وَقَالُوا مُعَلَّمٌ مَجْنُونٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,292,'6',44,'Surat ad-Dukhan (The Haze )','سورة حم الدُّخَانِ','"On the Day when We shall seize you with the greatest seizure (punishment). Verily, We will exact retribution." (V.44:16)','باب ‏ {‏يَوْمَ نَبْطِشُ الْبَطْشَةَ الْكُبْرَى إِنَّا مُنْتَقِمُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,293,NULL,45,'Surat al-Jathiyah (The Kneeling)','سورة حم الْجَاثِيَةِ','Surat al-Jathiyah (The Kneeling)','سورة حم الْجَاثِيَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,294,'1',46,'Surat al-Ahqaf (The Sand-Hills)','سورة الأَحْقَافِ','"But he who says to his parents: Fie upon you both! Do you hold out the promise to me that I shall be raised up (again)... (up to) ... the tales of the ancient." (V.46:17)','باب ‏ {‏وَالَّذِي قَالَ لِوَالِدَيْهِ أُفٍّ لَكُمَا أَتَعِدَانِنِي أَنْ أُخْرَجَ وَقَدْ خَلَتِ الْقُرُونُ مِنْ قَبْلِي وَهُمَا يَسْتَغِيثَانِ اللَّهَ وَيْلَكَ آمِنْ إِنَّ وَعْدَ اللَّهِ حَقٌّ فَيَقُولُ مَا هَذَا إِلاَّ أَسَاطِيرُ الأَوَّلِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,295,'2',46,'Surat al-Ahqaf (The Sand-Hills)','سورة الأَحْقَافِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Then, when they saw it as a dense cloud coming towards their valleys..." (V.46:24)','باب ‏ {‏فَلَمَّا رَأَوْهُ عَارِضًا مُسْتَقْبِلَ أَوْدِيَتِهِمْ قَالُوا هَذَا عَارِضٌ مُمْطِرُنَا بَلْ هُوَ مَا اسْتَعْجَلْتُمْ بِهِ رِيحٌ فِيهَا عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,296,'1',47,'Surat Muhammad (Muhammad)','سورة مُحَمَّدٍ صلى الله عليه وسلم','"...And sever your ties of kinship." (V.47:22)','باب ‏ {‏وَتُقَطِّعُوا أَرْحَامَكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,297,'1',48,'Surat al-Fath (The Triumph)','سورة الْفَتْحِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Verily, We have given you (O Muḥammad pbuh) a manifest victory." (V.48:1)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّا فَتَحْنَا لَكَ فَتْحًا مُبِينًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,298,'2',48,'Surat al-Fath (The Triumph)','سورة الْفَتْحِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "That Allah may forgive you your sins of the past and the future and complete His Favour on you and guide you on the Straight Path." (V.48:2)','باب ‏ {‏لِيَغْفِرَ لَكَ اللَّهُ مَا تَقَدَّمَ مِنْ ذَنْبِكَ وَمَا تَأَخَّرَ وَيُتِمَّ نِعْمَتَهُ عَلَيْكَ وَيَهْدِيَكَ صِرَاطًا مُسْتَقِيمًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,299,'3',48,'Surat al-Fath (The Triumph)','سورة الْفَتْحِ','"Verily, We have sent you (O Muḥammad pbuh) as a witness, as a bearer of glad tidings, and as a warner." (V.48:8)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّا أَرْسَلْنَاكَ شَاهِدًا وَمُبَشِّرًا وَنَذِيرًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,300,'4',48,'Surat al-Fath (The Triumph)','سورة الْفَتْحِ','"He it is Who sent down As-Sakīnah (tranquillity and calmness) into the hearts of the believers..." (V.48:4)','باب ‏ {‏هُوَ الَّذِي أَنْزَلَ السَّكِينَةَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,301,'5',48,'Surat al-Fath (The Triumph)','سورة الْفَتْحِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "...When they gave their Bai''a (pledge) to you (O Muḥammad pbuh) under the tree..." (V.48:18)','باب ‏ {‏إِذْ يُبَايِعُونَكَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,302,'1',49,'Surat al-Hujurat (The Private Quarters)','سورة الْحُجُرَاتِ','"O you who believe! Raise not your voices above the voice of the Prophet pbuh ..." (V.49:2)','باب ‏ {‏لاَ تَرْفَعُوا أَصْوَاتَكُمْ فَوْقَ صَوْتِ النَّبِيِّ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,303,'2',49,'Surat al-Hujurat (The Private Quarters)','سورة الْحُجُرَاتِ','"Verily! Those who call you from behind the dwellings, most of them have no sense." (V.49:4)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّ الَّذِينَ يُنَادُونَكَ مِنْ وَرَاءِ الْحُجُرَاتِ أَكْثَرُهُمْ لاَ يَعْقِلُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,304,'2b',49,'Surat al-Hujurat (The Private Quarters)','سورة الْحُجُرَاتِ','The Statement of Allah ta''ala: "And if they had patience till you could come out to them, it would have been better for them..." (V.49:5)','بَابُ: {وَلَوْ أَنَّهُمْ صَبَرُوا حَتَّى تَخْرُجَ إِلَيْهِمْ لَكَانَ خَيْرًا لَهُمْ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,305,'1',50,'Surat Qaf (Qaf)','سورة ق','Allah''s Statement: "...It (Hell) will say: ''Are there any more (to come)?" (V.50:30)','باب ‏ {‏وَتَقُولُ هَلْ مِنْ مَزِيدٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,306,'2',50,'Surat Qaf (Qaf)','سورة ق','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "...And glorify the praises of your Lord, before the rising of the sun and before (its) setting (i.e., the Fajr, Ẓuhr and ''Aṣr prayers) ." (V.50:39)','باب ‏ {‏وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ قَبْلَ طُلُوعِ الشَّمْسِ وَقَبْلَ الْغُرُوبِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,307,'1',52,'Surat at-Tur (Mount Tur)','سورة وَالطُّورِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,308,'1',53,'Surat an-Najm (The Stars)','سورة وَالنَّجْمِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,309,'1b',53,'Surat an-Najm (The Stars)','سورة وَالنَّجْمِ','"And was at a distance of two bows'' length or (even) nearer." (V.53:9)','باب ‏ {‏فَكَانَ قَابَ قَوْسَيْنِ أَوْ أَدْنَى‏} ‏ حَيْثُ الْوَتَرُ مِنَ الْقَوْسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,310,'1c',53,'Surat an-Najm (The Stars)','سورة وَالنَّجْمِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "So (Allah) revealed to His slave [Muḥammad pbuh through Jibrīl (Gabriel a.s.)] whatever He revealed." (V.53:10)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَأَوْحَى إِلَى عَبْدِهِ مَا أَوْحَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,311,'1d',53,'Surat an-Najm (The Stars)','سورة وَالنَّجْمِ','"Indeed he (Muḥammad pbuh) did see of the Greatest Signs of his Lord (Allah)." (V.53:18)','باب ‏ {‏لَقَدْ رَأَى مِنْ آيَاتِ رَبِّهِ الْكُبْرَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,312,'2',53,'Surat an-Najm (The Stars)','سورة وَالنَّجْمِ','"Have you then considered Al-Lat and AI-''Uzza? (1) " (V.53:19)  (1) :(Ch. 2) Lat and ''Uzza were two idols worshipped by the pagan Arabs during the Pre-Islamic Period of Ignorance.','باب ‏ {‏أَفَرَأَيْتُمُ اللاَّتَ وَالْعُزَّى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,313,'3',53,'Surat an-Najm (The Stars)','سورة وَالنَّجْمِ','"And Manat (another idol of the pagan Arabs) the other third." (V.53:20)','باب ‏ {‏وَمَنَاةَ الثَّالِثَةَ الأُخْرَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,314,'4',53,'Surat an-Najm (The Stars)','سورة وَالنَّجْمِ','"So, fall you down in prostration to Allah, and worship Him (Alone) ." (V.53:62)','باب ‏ {‏فَاسْجُدُوا لِلَّهِ وَاعْبُدُوا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,315,'1',54,'Surat al-Qamar (The Moon)','سورة اقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ','"...And the moon has been cleft asunder (the people of Makkah requested Prophet Muḥammad pbuh to show them a miracle, so he showed them the splitting of the moon). And if they see a sign, they turn away..." (V.54:1,2)','باب ‏ {‏وَانْشَقَّ الْقَمَرُ * وَإِنْ يَرَوْا آيَةً يُعْرِضُوا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,316,'2',54,'Surat al-Qamar (The Moon)','سورة اقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ','"Floating under Our Eyes, a reward for him who had been rejected! " (V.54:14)','باب ‏ {‏تَجْرِي بِأَعْيُنِنَا جَزَاءً لِمَنْ كَانَ كُفِرَ* وَلَقَدْ تَرَكْنَاهَا آيَةً فَهَلْ مِنْ مُدَّكِرٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,317,'2b',54,'Surat al-Qamar (The Moon)','سورة اقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ','"And We have indeed made the Qur''an easy to understand and remember; then is there any one who will remember (or receive admonition)?" (V.54:17)','باب ‏ {‏وَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْآنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُدَّكِرٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,318,'2c',54,'Surat al-Qamar (The Moon)','سورة اقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ','"... As if they were uprooted stems of date-palms. Then, how (terrible) was My Torment and My Warnings?" (V.54: 20, 21)','باب ‏ {‏أَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ مُنْقَعِرٍ * فَكَيْفَ كَانَ عَذَابِي وَنُذُرِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,319,'3',54,'Surat al-Qamar (The Moon)','سورة اقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ','"... And they became like the dry stubble of a fold-builder. And indeed, We have made the Qur''an easy to understand and remember; then is there any that will remember (or receive admonition) ." (V.54:31,32)','باب ‏ {‏فَكَانُوا كَهَشِيمِ الْمُحْتَظِرِ * وَلَقَدْ يَسَّرْنَا الْقُرْآنَ لِلذِّكْرِ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُدَّكِرٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,320,'4',54,'Surat al-Qamar (The Moon)','سورة اقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ','"And verily, an abiding torment seized them early in the morning. Then, taste you My Torment and My Warnings." (V.54:38,39)','باب ‏ {‏وَلَقَدْ صَبَّحَهُمْ بُكْرَةً عَذَابٌ مُسْتَقِرٌّ * فَذُوقُوا عَذَابِي وَنُذُرِ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,321,'4b',54,'Surat al-Qamar (The Moon)','سورة اقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ','"And We have already destroyed your kinds, so is there any who will remember?"','باب ‏ {‏وَلَقَدْ أَهْلَكْنَا أَشْيَاعَكُمْ فَهَلْ مِنْ مُدَّكِرٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,322,'5',54,'Surat al-Qamar (The Moon)','سورة اقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Their multitude will be put to flight." (V.54:45)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏سَيُهْزَمُ الْجَمْعُ وَيُوَلُّونَ الدُّبُرَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,323,'6',54,'Surat al-Qamar (The Moon)','سورة اقْتَرَبَتِ السَّاعَةُ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Nay, but the Hour is their appointed time (for their full recompense), and the Hour will be more grievous and more bitter." (V.54:46)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏بَلِ السَّاعَةُ مَوْعِدُهُمْ وَالسَّاعَةُ أَدْهَى وَأَمَرُّ‏} ‏ يَعْنِي مِنَ الْمَرَارَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,324,'1',55,'Surat ar-Rahman (The Most Compassionate)','سورة الرَّحْمَنِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "And besides these two, there are two other gardens (i.e., in Paradise) ." (V.55:62)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَمِنْ دُونِهِمَا جَنَّتَانِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,325,'2',55,'Surat ar-Rahman (The Most Compassionate)','سورة الرَّحْمَنِ','"Ḥūr (beautiful fair females) guarded in pavilions." (V.55:72)','باب ‏ {‏حُورٌ مَقْصُورَاتٌ فِي الْخِيَامِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,326,'1',56,'Surat al-Waqi’ah (The Inevitable Event)','سورة الْوَاقِعَةِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And in shade long extended." (V.56:30)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَظِلٍّ مَمْدُودٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,327,'1',59,'Surat al-Hashr (The Banishment)','سورة الْحَشْرِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,328,'2',59,'Surat al-Hashr (The Banishment)','سورة الْحَشْرِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "What you (O Muslims) cut down of the palm-trees (of the enemy)..." (V.59:5)','باب ‏ {‏مَا قَطَعْتُمْ مِنْ لِينَةٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,329,'3',59,'Surat al-Hashr (The Banishment)','سورة الْحَشْرِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "What Allah gave as booty (Fai'') to His Messenger . . ." (V.59:7)','باب قَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏مَا أَفَاءَ اللَّهُ عَلَى رَسُولِهِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,330,'4',59,'Surat al-Hashr (The Banishment)','سورة الْحَشْرِ','"And whatsoever the Messenger (Muḥammad pbuh) gives you take it..." (V.59:7)','باب ‏ {‏وَمَا آتَاكُمُ الرَّسُولُ فَخُذُوهُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,331,'5',59,'Surat al-Hashr (The Banishment)','سورة الْحَشْرِ','"And (it is also for) those who, before them, had homes (in Al-Madīna) and had adopted the Faith..." (V.59:9)','باب ‏ {‏وَالَّذِينَ تَبَوَّءُوا الدَّارَ وَالإِيمَانَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,332,'6',59,'Surat al-Hashr (The Banishment)','سورة الْحَشْرِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "...And give them (emigrants) preference over themselves..." (V.59:9)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَيُؤْثِرُونَ عَلَى أَنْفُسِهِمْ‏} ‏ الآيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,333,'1',60,'Surat al-Mumtahinah (The Test of Faith)','سورة الْمُمْتَحِنَةِ','"(O you who believe!) Take not My enemies and your enemies (i.e., disbelievers and polytheists) as friends..." (V.60:1)','باب ‏ {‏لاَ تَتَّخِذُوا عَدُوِّي وَعَدُوَّكُمْ أَوْلِيَاءَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,334,'2',60,'Surat al-Mumtahinah (The Test of Faith)','سورة الْمُمْتَحِنَةِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "...When believing women come to you as emigrants..." (V.60:10)','باب ‏ {‏إِذَا جَاءَكُمُ الْمُؤْمِنَاتُ مُهَاجِرَاتٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,335,'3',60,'Surat al-Mumtahinah (The Test of Faith)','سورة الْمُمْتَحِنَةِ','"O Prophet! When believing women come to you to give you the Bai''a (pledge).. ." (V.60:12)','باب ‏ {‏إِذَا جَاءَكَ الْمُؤْمِنَاتُ يُبَايِعْنَكَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,336,'1',61,'Surat as-Saff (The Solid Ranks)','سورة الصَّفِّ','"[And (remember) when ''Isā (Jesus a.s.), son of Mary said: "O Children of Israel! I am the Messenger of Allāh unto you, confirming the Torah (which came) before me, and giving glad tidings of a Messenger to come] after me, whose name shall be Ahmad." (61:6)','باب قَوْلُهُ تَعَالَى ‏ {‏مِنْ بَعْدِي اسْمُهُ أَحْمَدُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,337,'1',62,'Surat al-Jumu’ah (Friday Congregation)','سورة الْجُمُعَةِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah ta''ala: "And [He has sent him (Prophet Muḥammad pbuh) also to] others among them (Muslims) who have not yet joined them..." (V.62:3)','باب قَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏وَآخَرِينَ مِنْهُمْ لَمَّا يَلْحَقُوا بِهِمْ‏} ‏‏.‏ وَقَرَأَ عُمَرُ فَامْضُوا إِلَى ذِكْرِ اللَّهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,338,'2',62,'Surat al-Jumu’ah (Friday Congregation)','سورة الْجُمُعَةِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"And when they see some merchandise or some amusement..." (V.62:11)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِذَا رَأَوْا تِجَارَةً‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,339,'1',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allāh the Most High:  "When the hypocrites come to you (O Muḥammad pbuh) they say: ''We bear witness that you are indeed the Messenger of Allah..." (V.63:1)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِذَا جَاءَكَ الْمُنَافِقُونَ قَالُوا نَشْهَدُ إِنَّكَ لَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ‏} ‏ إِلَى ‏{‏لَكَاذِبُونَ‏}‏‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,340,'2',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"They have made their oaths a screen (for their hypocrisy)." (1)  (63:2)                                (1): (Ch. 2) "An-Nifāq": (Hypocrisy is of two types, namely: A - Hypocrisy in Belief B - Hypocrisy in deeds and actions. )','باب ‏ {‏اتَّخَذُوا أَيْمَانَهُمْ جُنَّةً‏} ‏ يَجْتَنُّونَ بِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,341,'3',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah ta''ala: "That is because they believed, then disbelieved, therefore their hearts are sealed, so they understand not." (V.63:3)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏ذَلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ آمَنُوا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوا فَطُبِعَ عَلَى قُلُوبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لاَ يَفْقَهُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,342,'1',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allāh the Most High:  "When the hypocrites come to you (O Muḥammad pbuh) they say: ''We bear witness that you are indeed the Messenger of Allah..." (V.63:1)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِذَا جَاءَكَ الْمُنَافِقُونَ قَالُوا نَشْهَدُ إِنَّكَ لَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ‏} ‏ إِلَى ‏{‏لَكَاذِبُونَ‏}‏‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,343,'2',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"They have made their oaths a screen (for their hypocrisy)." (1)  (63:2)                                (1): (Ch. 2) "An-Nifāq": (Hypocrisy is of two types, namely: A - Hypocrisy in Belief B - Hypocrisy in deeds and actions. )','باب ‏ {‏اتَّخَذُوا أَيْمَانَهُمْ جُنَّةً‏} ‏ يَجْتَنُّونَ بِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,344,'3',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah ta''ala: "That is because they believed, then disbelieved, therefore their hearts are sealed, so they understand not." (V.63:3)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏ذَلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمْ آمَنُوا ثُمَّ كَفَرُوا فَطُبِعَ عَلَى قُلُوبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لاَ يَفْقَهُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,345,'4',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"And when you look at them, their bodies please you, and when they speak, you listen to their words." (V.63:4)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِذَا رَأَيْتَهُمْ تُعْجِبُكَ أَجْسَامُهُمْ وَإِنْ يَقُولُوا تَسْمَعْ لِقَوْلِهِمْ كَأَنَّهُمْ خُشُبٌ مُسَنَّدَةٌ يَحْسِبُونَ كُلَّ صَيْحَةٍ عَلَيْهِمْ هُمُ الْعَدُوُّ فَاحْذَرْهُمْ قَاتَلَهُمُ اللَّهُ أَنَّى يُؤْفَكُونَ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,346,'4',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "And when it is said to them: ''Come, so that the Messenger of Allah may ask forgiveness from Allah for you,'' they turn aside their heads, and you would see them turning away their faces in pride." (V.63:5)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمْ تَعَالَوْا يَسْتَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ لَوَّوْا رُءُوسَهُمْ وَرَأَيْتَهُمْ يَصُدُّونَ وَهُمْ مُسْتَكْبِرُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,347,'5',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "It is equal to them whether you (Muḥammad pbuh) ask for their forgiveness.. ." (V.63:6)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏سَوَاءٌ عَلَيْهِمْ أَسْتَغْفَرْتَ لَهُمْ أَمْ لَمْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ لَنْ يَغْفِرَ اللَّهُ لَهُمْ إِنَّ اللَّهَ لاَ يَهْدِي الْقَوْمَ الْفَاسِقِينَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,348,'6',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "They are the ones who say: ''Spend not on those who are with Allah''s Messenger, until they desert him..." (V.63:7)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏هُمُ الَّذِينَ يَقُولُونَ لاَ تُنْفِقُوا عَلَى مَنْ عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ حَتَّى يَنْفَضُّوا‏} ‏ يَنْفَضُّوا} وَيَتَفَرَّقُوا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,349,NULL,63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"And to Allah belong the treasures of the heavens and the earth, but the hypocrites comprehend not." (63:7)','باب {‏وَلِلَّهِ خَزَائِنُ السَّمَوَاتِ وَالأَرْضِ وَلَكِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ لاَ يَفْقَهُونَ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,350,'7',63,'Surat al-Munafiqun (The Hypocrites)','سورة الْمُنَافِقِينَ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah ta''ala: "They (hypocrites) say: ''If we return to Al- Madīna, indeed the more honourable will expel therefrom the meaner..." (V.63:8)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏يَقُولُونَ لَئِنْ رَجَعْنَا إِلَى الْمَدِينَةِ لَيُخْرِجَنَّ الأَعَزُّ مِنْهَا الأَذَلَّ وَلِلَّهِ الْعِزَّةُ وَلِرَسُولِهِ وَلِلْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَلَكِنَّ الْمُنَافِقِينَ لاَ يَعْلَمُونَ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,351,'1',65,'Surat at-Talaq (Divorce)','سورة الطَّلاَقِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,352,'2',65,'Surat at-Talaq (Divorce)','سورة الطَّلاَقِ','. "... And for those who are pregnant (whether they are divorced or their husbands are dead), their ''Idda (prescribed period) is until they lay down their burdens, and whoever keeps his duty to Allah and fears Him, He will make his matter easy for him." (V.65:4)','باب ‏ {‏وَأُولاَتُ الأَحْمَالِ أَجَلُهُنَّ أَنْ يَضَعْنَ حَمْلَهُنَّ وَمَنْ يَتَّقِ اللَّهَ يَجْعَلْ لَهُ مِنْ أَمْرِهِ يُسْرًا‏} ‏‏.‏ وَأُولاَتُ الأَحْمَالِ وَاحِدُهَا ذَاتُ حَمْلٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,353,'1',66,'Surat at-Tahreem (The Prohibition)','سورة التَّحْرِيمِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"O Prophet! Why do you forbid (for yourself) that which Allah has allowed to you?..." (V.66:1)','باب ‏ {‏يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ لِمَ تُحَرِّمُ مَا أَحَلَّ اللَّهُ لَكَ تَبْتَغِي مَرْضَاةَ أَزْوَاجِكَ وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,354,'2',66,'Surat at-Tahreem (The Prohibition)','سورة التَّحْرِيمِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"... seeking to please your wives..." (V.66:1) "Allah has already ordained for you (O men), the dissolution of your oaths.. ." (V.66:2)','باب ‏ {‏تَبْتَغِي مَرْضَاةَ أَزْوَاجِكَ‏} ‏ ‏ {‏قَدْ فَرَضَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ تَحِلَّةَ أَيْمَانِكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,355,'3',66,'Surat at-Tahreem (The Prohibition)','سورة التَّحْرِيمِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"And (remember) when the Prophet pbuh disclosed a matter in confidence to one of his wives (Ḥafsa) (up to) ... The All-Aware." (V.66:3)','باب ‏ {‏وَإِذْ أَسَرَّ النَّبِيُّ إِلَى بَعْضِ أَزْوَاجِهِ حَدِيثًا فَلَمَّا نَبَّأَتْ بِهِ وَأَظْهَرَهُ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ عَرَّفَ بَعْضَهُ وَأَعْرَضَ عَنْ بَعْضٍ فَلَمَّا نَبَّأَهَا بِهِ قَالَتْ مَنْ أَنْبَأَكَ هَذَا قَالَ نَبَّأَنِيَ الْعَلِيمُ الْخَبِيرُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,356,'4',66,'Surat at-Tahreem (The Prohibition)','سورة التَّحْرِيمِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "If you two (wives of the Prophet, namely, ''Aishah and Hafsa) turn in repentance to Allah, (it will be better for you), your hearts are indeed so inclined (to oppose what the Prophet likes)." (V.66:4)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنْ تَتُوبَا إِلَى اللَّهِ فَقَدْ صَغَتْ قُلُوبُكُمَا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,357,'5',66,'Surat at-Tahreem (The Prohibition)','سورة التَّحْرِيمِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"It may be, if he divorced you (all), that his Lord (Allah) will give him instead of you, wives better than you... (V.66:5)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏عَسَى رَبُّهُ إِنْ طَلَّقَكُنَّ أَنْ يُبَدِّلَهُ أَزْوَاجًا خَيْرًا مِنْكُنَّ مُسْلِمَاتٍ مُؤْمِنَاتٍ قَانِتَاتٍ تَائِبَاتٍ عَابِدَاتٍ سَائِحَاتٍ ثَيِّبَاتٍ وَأَبْكَارًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,358,'1',68,'Surat al-Qalam (The Pen)','سورة ن وَالْقَلَمِ  - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"Cruel, and moreover base-born (of illegitimate birth) ." (V.68:13)','باب ‏ {‏عُتُلٍّ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ زَنِيمٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,359,'2',68,'Surat al-Qalam (The Pen)','سورة ن وَالْقَلَمِ  - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"(Remember) the Day when the Shin shalt be laid bare..." (V.68:42)','باب ‏ {‏يَوْمَ يُكْشَفُ عَنْ سَاقٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,360,'1',71,'Surat Nuh (Noah)','سورة نُوحٍ','"Nor shall you leave Wadd nor Suwā'' nor Yagūth nor Ya''ūq nor Nasr''. . ." (V.71:23)','باب ‏ {‏وَدًّا وَلاَ سُوَاعًا وَلاَ يَغُوثَ وَيَعُوقَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,361,'1',72,'Surat al-Jinn (The Jinn)','سورة قُلْ أُوحِيَ إِلَيَّ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,362,'1',74,'Surat al-Muddathir (The One Covered up)','سورة الْمُدَّثِّرِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,363,'2',74,'Surat al-Muddathir (The One Covered up)','سورة الْمُدَّثِّرِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "Arise and warn." (V.74:3)','باب قَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏قُمْ فَأَنْذِرْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,364,'3',74,'Surat al-Muddathir (The One Covered up)','سورة الْمُدَّثِّرِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "And magnify your Lord (Allah)!" (V.74:3)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَرَبَّكَ فَكَبِّرْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,365,'4',74,'Surat al-Muddathir (The One Covered up)','سورة الْمُدَّثِّرِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"And purify your garments!" (V.74:4)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَثِيَابَكَ فَطَهِّرْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,366,'5',74,'Surat al-Muddathir (The One Covered up)','سورة الْمُدَّثِّرِ - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"And keep away from Ar-Rujz (the idols)" (V.74:5)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَالرِّجْزَ فَاهْجُرْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,367,'1',75,'Surat al-Qiyamah (The Rising for Judgment)','سورة الْقِيَامَةِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "Move not your tongue concerning (the Qur''an, O Muḥammad pbuh) to make haste therewith." (V.75:16)','باب وَقَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏لاَ تُحَرِّكْ بِهِ لِسَانَكَ لِتَعْجَلَ بِهِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,368,'1b',75,'Surat al-Qiyamah (The Rising for Judgment)','سورة الْقِيَامَةِ','"It is for Us to collect it and to give you (O Muḥammad pbuh), the ability to recite it (the Qur''ān) ." (V.75:17)','باب ‏ {‏إِنَّ عَلَيْنَا جَمْعَهُ وَقُرْآنَهُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,369,'2',75,'Surat al-Qiyamah (The Rising for Judgment)','سورة الْقِيَامَةِ','"And when We have recited it to you [O Muḥammad PBUH through Jibril (Gabriel) a.s.], then follow its (the Qur''an''s) recital." (V.75:18)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَإِذَا قَرَأْنَاهُ فَاتَّبِعْ قُرْآنَهُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,370,'1',77,'Surat al-Mursalat (Those Winds Sent Forth)','سورة وَالْمُرْسَلاَتِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,371,'2',77,'Surat al-Mursalat (Those Winds Sent Forth)','سورة وَالْمُرْسَلاَتِ','The Statement of Allah ta''ala: "Verily! It (Hell) throws sparks (huge) as Al-Qasr (a fort or a huge log of wood) ." (V.77:32)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏إِنَّهَا تَرْمِي بِشَرَرٍ كَالْقَصْرِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,372,'3',77,'Surat al-Mursalat (Those Winds Sent Forth)','سورة وَالْمُرْسَلاَتِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "As if they were yellow camels or bundles of ropes." (V.77:33)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏{‏كَأَنَّهُ جِمَالاَتٌ صُفْرٌ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,373,'4',77,'Surat al-Mursalat (Those Winds Sent Forth)','سورة وَالْمُرْسَلاَتِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "That will be a Day when they shall not speak (during some part of it) ." (V.77:35)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏هَذَا يَوْمُ لاَ يَنْطِقُونَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,374,'1',78,'Surat an-Naba’ (The Momentous News)','سورة عَمَّ يَتَسَاءَلُونَ','"The Day when the Trumpet will be blown, and you shall come forth in crowds (groups after groups) ." (V.78:18)','باب ‏ {‏يَوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِي الصُّورِ فَتَأْتُونَ أَفْوَاجًا‏} ‏ زُمَرًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,375,'1',79,'Surat an-Nazi’at (Those Angles Stripping out Souls)','سورة {وَالنَّازِعَاتِ}',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,376,NULL,80,'Surat ‘Abasa (He Frowned)','سورة عَبَسَ','Surat ‘Abasa (He Frowned)','سورة عَبَسَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,377,'1',83,'Surat al-Mutaffifeen (Defrauders)','سورة {وَيْلٌ لِلْمُطَفِّفِينَ} - بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمَٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ','"The Day when (all) mankind will stand before the Lord of the ''Alamīn (mankind, jinn and all that exists)" (V.83:6)','بَابٌ {يَوْمَ يَقُومُ النَّاسُ لِرَبِّ الْعَالَمِينَ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,378,'1',84,'Surat al-Inshiqaq (The Sky Bursting Open)','سورة إِذَا السَّمَاءُ انْشَقَّتْ','"He surely will receive an easy reckoning." (V.84:8)','باب {فَسَوْفَ يُحَاسَبُ حِسَابًا يَسِيرًا}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,379,'2',84,'Surat al-Inshiqaq (The Sky Bursting Open)','سورة إِذَا السَّمَاءُ انْشَقَّتْ','"You shall certainly travel from stage to stage (in this life and in the Hereafter)" (V.84:19)','باب ‏ {‏لَتَرْكَبُنَّ طَبَقًا عَنْ طَبَقٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,380,NULL,87,'Surat al-A’la (The Most High)','سورة {سَبِّحِ اسْمَ رَبِّكَ الأَعْلَى}','Surat al-A’la (The Most High)','سورة {سَبِّحِ اسْمَ رَبِّكَ الأَعْلَى}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,381,NULL,91,'Surat ash-Shams (The Sun)','سورة وَالشَّمْسِ وَضُحَاهَا','Surat ash-Shams (The Sun)','سورة وَالشَّمْسِ وَضُحَاهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,382,'1',92,'Surat al-Layl (The Night)','سورة وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى','"By the day as it appears in brightness." (V.92:2)','باب ‏ {‏وَالنَّهَارِ إِذَا تَجَلَّى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,383,'2',92,'Surat al-Layl (The Night)','سورة وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى','"By Him Who created male and female." (V.92:3)','باب ‏ {‏وَمَا خَلَقَ الذَّكَرَ وَالأُنْثَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,384,'3',92,'Surat al-Layl (The Night)','سورة وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "As for him who gives (in charity) and keeps his duty to Allah and fears Him." (V.92:5)','باب قَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏فَأَمَّا مَنْ أَعْطَى وَاتَّقَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,385,'3b',92,'Surat al-Layl (The Night)','سورة وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى','The Statement of Allah the Most High: ''... and believes in Al-Ḥusnā." (1)(V.92:6)   (1):  (Ch.) The best (i.e., either Lā ilāha illallāh: none has the right to be worshipped but Allah) or a reward from Allah (i.e., Allah will compensate him for what he will spend in Allah''s way or bless him with Paradise).','بَابُ: {وَصَدَّقَ بِالْحُسْنَى}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,386,'4',92,'Surat al-Layl (The Night)','سورة وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى','"We will make smooth for him the path of ease (goodness) ." (V.92:7)','باب ‏ {‏فَسَنُيَسِّرُهُ لِلْيُسْرَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,387,'5',92,'Surat al-Layl (The Night)','سورة وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "But he who is [a] greedy miser and thinks himself self-sufficient." (V.92:8)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَأَمَّا مَنْ بَخِلَ وَاسْتَغْنَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,388,'6',92,'Surat al-Layl (The Night)','سورة وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "And belies Al-Ḥusnā ..." (V.92:9).','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَكَذَّبَ بِالْحُسْنَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,389,'7',92,'Surat al-Layl (The Night)','سورة وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى','"We will make smooth for him the path for evil." (V.92:10)','باب ‏ {‏فَسَنُيَسِّرُهُ لِلْعُسْرَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,390,'1',93,'Surat adh-Dhuha (The Morning Sunlight)','سورة وَالضُّحَى','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Your Lord (O Muḥammad pbuh) has neither forsaken you nor hates you." (V.93:3)','باب قَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏مَا وَدَّعَكَ رَبُّكَ وَمَا قَلَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,391,'2',93,'Surat adh-Dhuha (The Morning Sunlight)','سورة وَالضُّحَى','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "Your Lord (O Muḥammad pbuh) has neither forsaken you nor hates you." (V.93:1-3)','باب قَوْلُهُ ‏ {‏مَا وَدَّعَكَ رَبُّكَ وَمَا قَلَى‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,392,'1',95,'Surat at-Teen (The Fig)','سورة وَالتِّينِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,393,'1',96,'Surat al-‘Alaq (The Clinging Clot of Blood)','سورة اقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,394,'2',96,'Surat al-‘Alaq (The Clinging Clot of Blood)','سورة اقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "He has created man from a clot." (V.96:2)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏خَلَقَ الإِنْسَانَ مِنْ عَلَقٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,395,'3',96,'Surat al-‘Alaq (The Clinging Clot of Blood)','سورة اقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Read! And your Lord is the Most Generous." (V.96:3)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏اقْرَأْ وَرَبُّكَ الأَكْرَمُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,396,'3b',96,'Surat al-‘Alaq (The Clinging Clot of Blood)','سورة اقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ','"Who has taught (the writing) by the pen." (V.96:4)','باب ‏ {‏الَّذِي عَلَّمَ بِالْقَلَمِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,397,'4',96,'Surat al-‘Alaq (The Clinging Clot of Blood)','سورة اقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "Nay! If he (Abu Jahl) ceases not, We will catch him by the forelock, a lying sinful forelock!" (V.96:15,16)','باب ‏ {‏كَلاَّ لَئِنْ لَمْ يَنْتَهِ لَنَسْفَعَنْ بِالنَّاصِيَةِ * نَاصِيَةٍ كَاذِبَةٍ خَاطِئَةٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,398,'1',98,'Surat al-Bayyinah (The Clear Proof)','سورة لَمْ يَكُنْ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,399,'2',98,'Surat al-Bayyinah (The Clear Proof)','سورة لَمْ يَكُنْ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,400,'3',98,'Surat al-Bayyinah (The Clear Proof)','سورة لَمْ يَكُنْ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,401,'1',99,'Surat az-Zalzalah (The Ultimate Quake)','سورة إِذَا زُلْزِلَتِ الأَرْضُ زِلْزَالَهَا','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "So whosoever does good equal to the weight of an atom (or a small ant), shall see it." (V.99:7)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏فَمَنْ يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ خَيْرًا يَرَهُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,402,'2',99,'Surat az-Zalzalah (The Ultimate Quake)','سورة إِذَا زُلْزِلَتِ الأَرْضُ زِلْزَالَهَا','"And whosoever does evil equal to the weight of an atom (or a small ant), shall see it." (V.99:8)','باب ‏ {‏وَمَنْ يَعْمَلْ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ شَرًّا يَرَهُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,403,'1',108,'Surat al-Kawthar (Abundant Goodness)','سورة إِنَّا أَعْطَيْنَاكَ الْكَوْثَرِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,404,'1',110,'Surat an-Nasr (The Ultimate Help)','سورة إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,405,'2',110,'Surat an-Nasr (The Ultimate Help)','سورة إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,406,'3',110,'Surat an-Nasr (The Ultimate Help)','سورة إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "And you see that the people enter Allah''s religion (Islām) in crowds." (V.110:2)','باب ‏ {‏وَرَأَيْتَ النَّاسَ يَدْخُلُونَ فِي دِينِ اللَّهِ أَفْوَاجًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,407,'4',110,'Surat an-Nasr (The Ultimate Help)','سورة إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ','The Statement of Allah the Exalted: "So, glorify the praises of your Lord, and ask His forgiveness. Verily! He is the One Who accepts the repentance and forgives." (V.110:3)','باب ‏ {‏فَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَاسْتَغْفِرْهُ إِنَّهُ كَانَ تَوَّابًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,408,'1',111,'Surat al-Masad (The Palm-Fibre Rope)','سورة تَبَّتْ يَدَا أَبِى لَهَبٍ وَتَبَّ',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,409,'2',111,'Surat al-Masad (The Palm-Fibre Rope)','سورة تَبَّتْ يَدَا أَبِى لَهَبٍ وَتَبَّ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "... and perish he! His wealth and his children will not benefit him!" (V.111:1-2)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏وَتَبَّ * مَا أَغْنَى عَنْهُ مَالُهُ وَمَا كَسَبَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,410,'3',111,'Surat al-Masad (The Palm-Fibre Rope)','سورة تَبَّتْ يَدَا أَبِى لَهَبٍ وَتَبَّ','The Statement of Allah the Most High: "He (Abu Lahab) will be burnt in a Fire of blazing flames!" (V.111:3)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏سَيَصْلَى نَارًا ذَاتَ لَهَبٍ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,411,'4',111,'Surat al-Masad (The Palm-Fibre Rope)','سورة تَبَّتْ يَدَا أَبِى لَهَبٍ وَتَبَّ','"And his wife too, who carries wood." (V.111:4)','باب ‏ {‏وَامْرَأَتُهُ حَمَّالَةُ الْحَطَبِ‏}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,412,'1',112,'Surat al-Ikhlas (Purity of Faith)','سورة {قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ}',NULL,'باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,413,'2',112,'Surat al-Ikhlas (Purity of Faith)','سورة {قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ}','The Statement of Allah ta''ala: "Allāh-uṣ-Ṣamad (The Self-Sufficient Master, Whom all creatures need, He neither eats nor drinks) ." (V.112:2)','باب قَوْلِهِ ‏ {‏اللَّهُ الصَّمَدُ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,414,NULL,113,'Surat al-Falaq (The Daybreak)','سورة ‏ {‏قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِ‏} ‏','Surat al-Falaq (The Daybreak)','سورة ‏ {‏قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ الْفَلَقِ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',65,415,NULL,114,'Surat an-Nas (Humankind)','سورة {قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ النَّاسِ}','Surat an-Nas (Humankind)','سورة {قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ النَّاسِ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'How the Divine Revelation used to be revealed and what was the first thing revealed','باب كَيْفَ نُزُولُ الْوَحْىِ وَأَوَّلُ مَا نَزَلَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Qur''an was revealed in the language of Quraish and the Arabs','باب نَزَلَ الْقُرْآنُ بِلِسَانِ قُرَيْشٍ وَالْعَرَبِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The collection of the Qur''an','باب جَمْعِ الْقُرْآنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The scribe of the Prophet (saws)','باب كَاتِبِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Qur''an was revealed to be recited in seven different ways','باب أُنْزِلَ الْقُرْآنُ عَلَى سَبْعَةِ أَحْرُفٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The compilation of the Qur''an','باب تَأْلِيفِ الْقُرْآنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Jibril used to present the Qur''an to the Prophet (saws)','باب كَانَ جِبْرِيلُ يَعْرِضُ الْقُرْآنَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Qurra from among the Companions of the Prophet (saws)','باب الْقُرَّاءِ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of Fatiha-til-Kitab','باب ‏‏فَضْلِ‏‏ فَاتِحَةِ الْكِتَابِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of Surat Al-Baqarah (No.2)','باب فَضْلُ سُورَةِ الْبَقَرَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of Surat Al-Kahf (No.18)','باب فَضْلُ الْكَهْفِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of Surat Al-Fath (No48)','باب فَضْلُ سُورَةِ الْفَتْحِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of Qul-Huwa Allahu Ahad (Surat Al-Ikhlas) (No.112)','باب فَضْلِ قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of Al-Mu’awwidhat (Surat Al-Falaq and Surat An-Nas) (No.113 & 114)','‏باب فَضْلِ‏‏ الْمُعَوِّذَاتِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The descent of As-Sakinah and angels at the time of the recitation of the Qur''an','باب نُزُولِ السَّكِينَةِ وَالْمَلاَئِكَةِ عِنْدَ قِرَاءَةِ الْقُرْآنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever said that the Prophet (saws) did not leave anything after his death','باب مَنْ قَالَ لَمْ يَتْرُكِ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم إِلاَّ مَا بَيْنَ الدَّفَّتَيْنِ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of the Qur''an above other kinds of speech','باب فَضْلِ الْقُرْآنِ عَلَى سَائِرِ الْكَلاَمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To recommend the Book of Allah عز وجل','باب الْوَصَاةِ بِكِتَابِ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever does not recite the Qur''an in a pleasant tone','باب مَنْ لَمْ يَتَغَنَّ بِالْقُرْآنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wish to be the like of the one who recites the Qur''an','باب اغْتِبَاطِ صَاحِبِ الْقُرْآنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The best among you are those who learn the Qur''an and teach it','باب خَيْرُكُمْ مَنْ تَعَلَّمَ الْقُرْآنَ وَعَلَّمَهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The recitation of the Qur''an by heart','باب الْقِرَاءَةِ عَنْ ظَهْرِ الْقَلْبِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The learning of the Qur''an by heart and the reciting of it repeatedly','باب اسْتِذْكَارِ الْقُرْآنِ وَتَعَاهُدِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The recitation of the Qur''an on an animal','باب الْقِرَاءَةِ عَلَى الدَّابَّةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Teaching the Qur''an to the children','باب تَعْلِيمِ الصِّبْيَانِ الْقُرْآنَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Forgetting the Qur''an. And can one say: “I forgot such and such a Verse?','بَابُ نِسْيَانِ الْقُرْآنِ وَهَلْ يَقُولُ نَسِيتُ آيَةَ كَذَا وَكَذَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever thinks that there is no harm in saying: Surat Al-Baqarah or Surat so-and-so','باب مَنْ لَمْ يَرَ بَأْسًا أَنْ يَقُولَ سُورَةُ الْبَقَرَةِ وَسُورَةُ كَذَا وَكَذَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The recitation of Qur''an in Tartil','باب التَّرْتِيلِ فِي الْقِرَاءَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Prolonging certain sounds while reciting the Qur''an','باب مَدِّ الْقِرَاءَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'At-Tarji’','باب التَّرْجِيعِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To recite the Qur''an in a charming voice','باب حُسْنِ الصَّوْتِ بِالْقِرَاءَةِ لِلْقُرْآنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever likes to hear the Qur''an from another person','باب مَنْ أَحَبَّ أَنْ يَسْمَعَ الْقُرْآنَ مِنْ غَيْرِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The saying of the listener to the reciter: “Enough!”','باب قَوْلِ الْمُقْرِئِ لِلْقَارِئِ حَسْبُكَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What is the proper period for reciting the whole Qur''an','بَابٌ في كَمْ يُقْرَأُ الْقُرْآنُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To weep while reciting the Qur''an','باب الْبُكَاءِ عِنْدَ قِرَاءَةِ الْقُرْآنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The sin of the person who recites the Qur''an to show off or to gain some worldly benefit, or to feel proud etc.','باب مَنْ رَايَا بِقِرَاءَةِ الْقُرْآنِ أَوْ تَأَكَّلَ بِهِ أَوْ فَخَرَ بِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',66,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Recite the Qur''an together as long as you agree about its interpretation','باب اقْرَءُوا الْقُرْآنَ مَا ائْتَلَفَتْ قُلُوبُكُمْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Awakening the desire for marriage','باب التَّرْغِيبُ فِي النِّكَاحِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"Whoever is able to marry, should marry..."','بَابُ قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: «مَنِ اسْتَطَاعَ مِنْكُمُ الْبَاءَةَ فَلْيَتَزَوَّجْ، لأَنَّهُ أَغَضُّ لِلْبَصَرِ وَأَحْصَنُ لِلْفَرْجِ»، وَهَلْ يَتَزَوَّجُ مَنْ لاَ أَرَبَ لَهُ فِي النِّكَاحِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever is not able to marry, is recommended to fast','باب مَنْ لَمْ يَسْتَطِعِ الْبَاءَةَ فَلْيَصُمْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'About (marrying) several women','باب كَثْرَةِ النِّسَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever emigrated with the intention of marrying a woman','باب مَنْ هَاجَرَ أَوْ عَمِلَ خَيْرًا لِتَزْوِيجِ امْرَأَةٍ فَلَهُ مَا نَوَى'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The marrying of a poor man','باب تَزْوِيجِ الْمُعْسِرِ الَّذِي مَعَهُ الْقُرْآنُ وَالإِسْلاَمُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The saying of  a man to his brother (in Islam)','باب قَوْلِ الرَّجُلِ لأَخِيهِ انْظُرْ أَىَّ زَوْجَتَىَّ شِئْتَ حَتَّى أَنْزِلَ لَكَ عَنْهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What is disliked of not marrying and of getting castrated','باب مَا يُكْرَهُ مِنَ التَّبَتُّلِ وَالْخِصَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To marry virgins','باب نِكَاحِ الأَبْكَارِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The marrying of matrons','باب الثَّيِّبَاتِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The marrying of young lady to an elderly man','باب تَزْوِيجِ الصِّغَارِ مِنَ الْكِبَارِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What type of women should one seek in marriage?','باب إِلَى مَنْ يَنْكِحُ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Having female captives and manumitting one''s own slave-girl','باب اتِّخَاذِ السَّرَارِيِّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The manumission of a slave-girl as her Mahr','باب مَنْ جَعَلَ عِتْقَ الأَمَةِ صَدَاقَهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"If they be poor, Allah will enrich them out of His Bounty."','بَابُ تَزْوِيجِ الْمُعْسِرِ لِقَوْلِهِ تَعَالَى: {إِنْ يَكُونُوا فُقَرَاءَ يُغْنِهِمُ اللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Husband and wife should have the same religion','باب الأَكْفَاءِ فِي الدِّينِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The marriage of a poor man with a well-to-do lady','باب الأَكْفَاءِ فِي الْمَالِ، وَتَزْوِيجِ الْمُقِلِّ الْمُثْرِيَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What evil omen of a lady is to be warded off','باب مَا يُتَّقَى مِنْ شُؤْمِ الْمَرْأَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(About) a free lady as the wife of a slave','باب الْحُرَّةِ تَحْتَ الْعَبْدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Not to marry more than four (at a time)','باب لاَ يَتَزَوَّجُ أَكْثَرَ مِنْ أَرْبَعٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"..your foster-mothers who gave you suck."','بَابُ: {وَأُمَّهَاتُكُمُ اللاَّتِي أَرْضَعْنَكُمْ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"No suckling is to be carried on after the baby is two years old."','بَابُ مَنْ قَالَ لاَ رَضَاعَ بَعْدَ حَوْلَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The milk belongs to the husband','باب لَبَنِ الْفَحْلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The witness of a wet nurse','باب شَهَادَةِ الْمُرْضِعَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"Forbidden to you (for marriage) are: your mothers, your daughters..."','باب مَا يَحِلُّ مِنَ النِّسَاءِ وَمَا يَحْرُمُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"....your step-daughters under your guardianship, born of your wives..."','بَابُ: {وَرَبَائِبُكُمُ اللاَّتِي فِي حُجُورِكُمْ مِنْ نِسَائِكُمُ اللاَّتِي دَخَلْتُمْ بِهِنَّ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"(It is prohibited to have) two sisters in wedlock at the same time..."','بَابُ: {وَأَنْ تَجْمَعُوا بَيْنَ الأُخْتَيْنِ إِلاَّ مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A woman should not marry a man already married to her paternal aunt','باب لاَ تُنْكَحُ الْمَرْأَةُ عَلَى عَمَّتِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Ash-Shighar. (Exchange of daughters or sisters in marriage without paying Mahr)','باب الشِّغَارِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Is it permissible for a woman to present herself for marriage to somebody?','باب هَلْ لِلْمَرْأَةِ أَنْ تَهَبَ نَفْسَهَا لأَحَدٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The marriage of Muhrim','باب نِكَاحِ الْمُحْرِمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Allah''s Messenger (saws) prohibited Nikah-al-Mut''a lately.','باب نَهْىِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم عَنْ نِكَاحِ الْمُتْعَةِ آخِرًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A woman can present herself to a righteous man (for marriage)','باب عَرْضِ الْمَرْأَةِ نَفْسَهَا عَلَى الرَّجُلِ الصَّالِحِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The presentation of one''s own daughter or sister (for marriage) to a religious man.','باب عَرْضِ الإِنْسَانِ ابْنَتَهُ أَوْ أُخْتَهُ عَلَى أَهْلِ الْخَيْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"And there is no sin on you if you make a hint of betrothal or conceal it in yourself..."','باب قَوْلِ اللَّهِ جَلَّ وَعَزَّ : {وَلاَ جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ فِيمَا عَرَّضْتُمْ بِهِ مِنْ خِطْبَةِ النِّسَاءِ أَوْ أَكْنَنْتُمْ فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ عَلِمَ اللَّهُ} الآيَةَ إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: {غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٌ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(It is permissible) to look at a woman before marrying.','باب النَّظَرِ إِلَى الْمَرْأَةِ قَبْلَ التَّزْوِيجِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever said, "A marriage is not valid except through the Wali."','بَابُ مَنْ قَالَ لاَ نِكَاحَ إِلاَّ بِوَلِيٍّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,38,'38',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the guardian himself is the suitor','باب إِذَا كَانَ الْوَلِيُّ هُوَ الْخَاطِبَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,39,'39',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Giving one''s young children in marriage','باب إِنْكَاحِ الرَّجُلِ وَلَدَهُ الصِّغَارَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,40,'40',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The marrying of a daughter by her father to a ruler','باب تَزْوِيجِ الأَبِ ابْنَتَهُ مِنَ الإِمَامِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The ruler is regarded as a guardian','بَابُ السُّلْطَانُ وَلِيٌّ بِقَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: «زَوَّجْنَاكَهَا بِمَا مَعَكَ مِنَ الْقُرْآنِ»'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,42,'42',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The father or the guardian cannot give a virgin or matron in marriage without her consent','باب لاَ يُنْكِحُ الأَبُ وَغَيْرُهُ الْبِكْرَ وَالثَّيِّبَ إِلاَّ بِرِضَاهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,43,'43',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a man gives his daughter in marriage while she is averse to it, then such marriage is invalid','باب إِذَا زَوَّجَ ابْنَتَهُ وَهْىَ كَارِهَةٌ فَنِكَاحُهُ مَرْدُودٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,44,'44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The giving of an orphan girl in marriage','باب تَزْوِيجِ الْيَتِيمَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,45,'45',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the suitor says, "Marry me to so-and-so," and the guardian says, "I have married her to you for such Mahr"','بَابُ إِذَا قَالَ الْخَاطِبُ لِلْوَلِيِّ زَوِّجْنِي فُلاَنَةَ. فَقَالَ قَدْ زَوَّجْتُكَ بِكَذَا وَكَذَا. جَازَ النِّكَاحُ، وَإِنْ لَمْ يَقُلْ لِلزَّوْجِ أَرَضِيتَ أَوْ قَبِلْتَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,46,'46',NULL,NULL,NULL,'None should ask for the hand of a lady who is already engaged to his brother (Muslim)','باب لاَ يَخْطُبُ عَلَى خِطْبَةِ أَخِيهِ، حَتَّى يَنْكِحَ أَوْ يَدَعَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,47,'47',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The meaning of the cancelling of the engagement.','باب تَفْسِيرِ تَرْكِ الْخِطْبَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,48,'48',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Khutba (for Nikah)','باب الْخُطْبَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,49,'49',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Beating the tambourine during marriage ceremony and the wedding banquet.','باب ضَرْبِ الدُّفِّ فِي النِّكَاحِ وَالْوَلِيمَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,50,'50',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"And give to the women their Mahr with a good heart..."','باب قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى ‏{‏وَآتُوا النِّسَاءَ صَدُقَاتِهِنَّ نِحْلَةً‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,51,'51',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To marry (a lady to) a man for what he knows of the Qur''an','باب التَّزْوِيجِ عَلَى الْقُرْآنِ وَبِغَيْرِ صَدَاقٍ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,52,'52',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To give Mahr in the form of material things','باب الْمَهْرِ بِالْعُرُوضِ وَخَاتَمٍ مِنْ حَدِيدٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,53,'53',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The conditions stipulated in marriage (contract)','باب الشُّرُوطِ فِي النِّكَاحِ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,54,'54',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Conditions not lawful in the marriage contract','باب الشُّرُوطِ الَّتِي لاَ تَحِلُّ فِي النِّكَاحِ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,55,'55',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Yellow coloured perfume for a bridegroom','باب الصُّفْرَةِ لِلْمُتَزَوِّجِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,56,'56',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','بَابٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,57,'57',NULL,NULL,NULL,'How to invoke good upon a person who has married recently?','باب كَيْفَ يُدْعَى لِلْمُتَزَوِّجِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,58,'58',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The invocation of those women who prepare the bride','باب الدُّعَاءِ لِلنِّسَاءِ اللاَّتِي يَهْدِينَ الْعَرُوسَ، وَلِلْعَرُوسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,59,'59',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To consummate the marriage before going on a military campaign','باب مَنْ أَحَبَّ الْبِنَاءَ قَبْلَ الْغَزْوِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,60,'60',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever consummated his marriage with a lady of nine years of age','باب مَنْ بَنَى بِامْرَأَةٍ وَهْىَ بِنْتُ تِسْعِ سِنِينَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,61,'61',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Consummation of marriage during a journey','باب الْبِنَاءِ فِي السَّفَرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,62,'62',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Consummation of marriage during the daytime without a marriage procession or lighting of fires','باب الْبِنَاءِ بِالنَّهَارِ بِغَيْرِ مَرْكَبٍ وَلاَ نِيرَانٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,63,'63',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The curtains, beddings and similar thins designed for the women','باب الأَنْمَاطِ وَنَحْوِهَا لِلنِّسَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,64,'64',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The women who present the lady to her husband','باب النِّسْوَةِ اللاَّتِي يَهْدِينَ الْمَرْأَةَ إِلَى زَوْجِهَا وَدُعَائِهِنَّ بِالْبَرَكَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,65,'65',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The giving of a present to the bridegroom','باب الْهَدِيَّةِ لِلْعَرُوسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,66,'66',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To borrow the clothes, etc. for the bride','باب اسْتِعَارَةِ الثِّيَابِ لِلْعَرُوسِ وَغَيْرِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,67,'67',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What a man should say on having a sexual intercourse with his wife','باب مَا يَقُولُ الرَّجُلُ إِذَا أَتَى أَهْلَهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,68,'68',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Walima (wedding banquet) is obligatory','باب الْوَلِيمَةُ حَقٌّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,69,'69',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Walima is to be given even with one sheep','باب الْوَلِيمَةِ وَلَوْ بِشَاةٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,70,'70',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A bigger Walima on marrying some wives than the other wives','باب مَنْ أَوْلَمَ عَلَى بَعْضِ نِسَائِهِ أَكْثَرَ مِنْ بَعْضٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,71,'71',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Walima of less than one sheep','باب مَنْ أَوْلَمَ بِأَقَلَّ مِنْ شَاةٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,72,'72',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To accept the invitation to a Walima','باب حَقِّ إِجَابَةِ الْوَلِيمَةِ وَالدَّعْوَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,73,'73',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If somebody refuses an invitation','باب مَنْ تَرَكَ الدَّعْوَةَ فَقَدْ عَصَى اللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,74,'74',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever accepted the invitation to a meal of trotters','باب مَنْ أَجَابَ إِلَى كُرَاعٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,75,'75',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To accept the invitation to a party','باب إِجَابَةِ الدَّاعِي فِي الْعُرْسِ وَغَيْرِه'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,76,'76',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The attendance of women and children at a wedding party','باب ذَهَابِ النِّسَاءِ وَالصِّبْيَانِ إِلَى الْعُرْسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,77,'77',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Should a person return if he sees something objectionable in the party?','باب هَلْ يَرْجِعُ إِذَا رَأَى مُنْكَرًا فِي الدَّعْوَةِ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,78,'78',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The serving of the bride herself for the men at (her) marriage party','باب قِيَامِ الْمَرْأَةِ عَلَى الرِّجَالِ فِي الْعُرْسِ وَخِدْمَتِهِمْ بِالنَّفْسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,79,'79',NULL,NULL,NULL,'An-Naqi and other non-toxicant drinks at a wedding party','باب النَّقِيعِ وَالشَّرَابِ الَّذِي لاَ يُسْكِرُ فِي الْعُرْسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,80,'80',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To be polite and kind to the women','باب الْمُدَارَاةِ مَعَ النِّسَاءِ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,81,'81',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The exhortation of taking care of the women','باب الْوَصَاةِ بِالنِّسَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,82,'82',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"Ward off from yourself and your families a Fire whose fuel is men and stones..."','باب ‏ {‏قُوا أَنْفُسَكُمْ وَأَهْلِيكُمْ نَارًا‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,83,'83',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To treat the family in a polite and kind manner','باب حُسْنِ الْمُعَاشَرَةِ مَعَ الأَهْلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,84,'84',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Advice to a daughter regarding her husband','باب مَوْعِظَةِ الرَّجُلِ ابْنَتَهُ لِحَالِ زَوْجِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,85,'85',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A woman should not observe Saum except husband''s consent        (is ''with her'' missing here?)','باب صَوْمِ الْمَرْأَةِ بِإِذْنِ زَوْجِهَا تَطَوُّعًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,86,'86',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a woman deserts her husband''s bed','باب إِذَا بَاتَتِ الْمَرْأَةُ مُهَاجِرَةً فِرَاشَ زَوْجِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,87,'87',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A woman should not allow anyone to enter the house except husband''s consent     (here too)','باب لاَ تَأْذَنُ الْمَرْأَةُ فِي بَيْتِ زَوْجِهَا لأَحَدٍ إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,88,'88',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,89,'89',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To be unthankful to the husband','باب كُفْرَانِ الْعَشِيرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,90,'90',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Your wife has a right over you','باب لِزَوْجِكَ عَلَيْكَ حَقٌّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,91,'91',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The woman is a guardian in her husband''s house','باب الْمَرْأَةُ رَاعِيَةٌ فِي بَيْتِ زَوْجِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,92,'92',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"Men are protectors and maintainers of women."','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {الرِّجَالُ قَوَّامُونَ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ بِمَا فَضَّلَ اللَّهُ بَعْضَهُمْ عَلَى بَعْضٍ} إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: {إِنَّ اللَّهَ كَانَ عَلِيًّا كَبِيرًا}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,93,'93',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The decision of the Prophet (saws) not to share the beds with his wives and to stay away','باب هِجْرَةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم نِسَاءَهُ فِي غَيْرِ بُيُوتِهِنَّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,94,'94',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The beating of women is disapproved','باب مَا يُكْرَهُ مِنْ ضَرْبِ النِّسَاءِ وَقَوْلِهِ ‏{‏وَاضْرِبُوهُنَّ‏}‏ ضَرْبًا غَيْرَ مُبَرِّحٍ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,95,'95',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Not to obey the husband if he orders to do something sinful','باب لاَ تُطِيعُ الْمَرْأَةُ زَوْجَهَا فِي مَعْصِيَةٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,96,'96',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"If a woman fears cruelty or desertion on her husband''s part..."','باب ‏ {‏وَإِنِ امْرَأَةٌ خَافَتْ مِنْ بَعْلِهَا نُشُوزًا أَوْ  إِعْرَاضًا}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,97,'97',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The coitus interruptus','باب الْعَزْلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,98,'98',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To draw lots among the wives for a journey','باب الْقُرْعَةِ بَيْنَ النِّسَاءِ إِذَا أَرَادَ سَفَرًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,99,'99',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To give up the turn with the husband to one of his other wives','باب الْمَرْأَةِ تَهَبُ يَوْمَهَا مِنْ زَوْجِهَا لِضَرَّتِهَا وَكَيْفَ يُقْسِمُ ذَلِكَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,100,'100',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To deal justly between the women (wives)','بَابُ الْعَدْلِ بَيْنَ النِّسَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,101,'101',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Marrying a virgin while already having a matron wife','باب إِذَا تَزَوَّجَ الْبِكْرَ عَلَى الثَّيِّبِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,102,'102',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Marrying a matron while already having a virgin wife','باب إِذَا تَزَوَّجَ الثَّيِّبَ عَلَى الْبِكْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,103,'103',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever had sexual intercourse with all his wives and then took one bath only','باب مَنْ طَافَ عَلَى نِسَائِهِ فِي غُسْلٍ وَاحِدٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,104,'104',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a man goes to all his wives in one day','باب دُخُولِ الرَّجُلِ عَلَى نِسَائِهِ فِي الْيَوْمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,105,'105',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a man takes the permission of his wives so as to stay in the house of one of them','باب إِذَا اسْتَأْذَنَ الرَّجُلُ نِسَاءَهُ فِي أَنْ يُمَرَّضَ فِي بَيْتِ بَعْضِهِنَّ، فَأَذِنَّ لَهُ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,106,'106',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To love some of the wives more than the others','باب حُبِّ الرَّجُلِ بَعْضَ نِسَائِهِ أَفْضَلَ مِنْ بَعْضٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,107,'107',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To claim having more things or better qualities than one really has','باب الْمُتَشَبِّعِ بِمَا لَمْ يَنَلْ، وَمَا يُنْهَى مِنِ افْتِخَارِ الضَّرَّةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,108,'108',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Ghaira (i.e. honour, prestige or self-respect)','باب الْغَيْرَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,109,'109',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The jealousy of women and their anger','باب غَيْرَةِ النِّسَاءِ وَوَجْدِهِنَّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,110,'110',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Attempt to prevent the daughter''s jealousy','باب ذَبِّ الرَّجُلِ عَنِ ابْنَتِهِ، فِي الْغَيْرَةِ وَالإِنْصَافِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,111,'111',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Men will decrease and women will increase','باب يَقِلُّ الرِّجَالُ وَيَكْثُرُ النِّسَاءُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,112,'112',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A man should not stay with a woman in seclusion','باب لاَ يَخْلُوَنَّ رَجُلٌ بِامْرَأَةٍ إِلاَّ ذُو مَحْرَمٍ، وَالدُّخُولُ عَلَى الْمُغِيبَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,113,'113',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Private meeting between a man and a woman not secluded from the people','باب مَا يَجُوزُ أَنْ يَخْلُوَ الرَّجُلُ بِالْمَرْأَةِ عِنْدَ النَّاسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,114,'114',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Effeminate men should not enter upon women','باب مَا يُنْهَى مِنْ دُخُولِ الْمُتَشَبِّهِينَ بِالنِّسَاءِ عَلَى الْمَرْأَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,115,'115',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The looking of a woman at the Ethiopians and the like','باب نَظَرِ الْمَرْأَةِ إِلَى الْحَبَشِ وَنَحْوِهِمْ مِنْ غَيْرِ رِيبَةٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,116,'116',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The going out of women for their needs','باب خُرُوجِ النِّسَاءِ لِحَوَائِجِهِنَّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,117,'117',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The permission taken by a woman from her husband to go to the mosque','باب اسْتِئْذَانِ الْمَرْأَةِ زَوْجَهَا فِي الْخُرُوجِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ وَغَيْرِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,118,'118',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Visiting or looking at women having foster suckling reltions','باب مَا يَحِلُّ مِنَ الدُّخُولِ وَالنَّظَرِ إِلَى النِّسَاءِ فِي الرَّضَاعِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,119,'119',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A woman should not look at or touch the body of another woman to describe to her husband','باب لاَ تُبَاشِرُ الْمَرْأَةُ الْمَرْأَةَ فَتَنْعَتَهَا لِزَوْجِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,120,'120',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"I will go round all my wives tonight."','باب قَوْلِ الرَّجُلِ لأَطُوفَنَّ اللَّيْلَةَ عَلَى نِسَائِي'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,121,'121',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a man is away for a long time, he should not enter his house at night.','باب لاَ يَطْرُقْ أَهْلَهُ لَيْلاً إِذَا أَطَالَ الْغَيْبَةَ مَخَافَةَ، أَنْ يُخَوِّنَهُمْ أَوْ يَلْتَمِسَ عَثَرَاتِهِمْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,122,'122',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Seeking to beget children','باب طَلَبِ الْوَلَدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,123,'123',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The woman should shave her pubic hair, and should comb the hair.','باب تَسْتَحِدُّ الْمُغِيبَةُ وَتَمْتَشِطُ ‏{‏الشَّعِثَةُ‏}‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,124,'124',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"And not to reveal their adornments except to their husbands,..."','بَابُ: {وَلاَ يُبْدِينَ زِينَتَهُنَّ إِلاَّ لِبُعُولَتِهِنَّ} إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: {لَمْ يَظْهَرُوا عَلَى عَوْرَاتِ النِّسَاءِ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,125,'125',NULL,NULL,NULL,'''And those among you who have not come to the age of puberty."','باب ‏ {‏وَالَّذِينَ لَمْ يَبْلُغُوا الْحُلُمَ مِنْكُمْ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',67,126,'126',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The man''s poking his daughter in the flank while admonishing her','باب قَوْلِ الرَّجُلِ لِصَاحِبِهِ هَلْ أَعْرَسْتُمُ اللَّيْلَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"O Prophet! When you divorce women, divorce them at their ''Idda and count their ''Idda."','بَابُ قَوْلُ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ إِذَا طَلَّقْتُمُ النِّسَاءَ فَطَلِّقُوهُنَّ لِعِدَّتِهِنَّ وَأَحْصُوا الْعِدَّةَ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Divorce during the menses is counted as one legal divorce.','باب إِذَا طُلِّقَتِ الْحَائِضُ يُعْتَدُّ بِذَلِكَ الطَّلاَقِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Should a man tell his wife face to face that she is divorced','باب مَنْ طَلَّقَ وَهَلْ يُوَاجِهُ الرَّجُلُ امْرَأَتَهُ بِالطَّلاَقِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To divorce one''s wife thrice (at a time)','باب مَنْ أَجَازَ طَلاَقَ الثَّلاَثِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Giving option to the wives.','باب مَنْ خَيَّرَ نِسَاءَهُ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a man says (to his wife): "I have parted with you," or "I have released you"','بَابُ إِذَا قَالَ فَارَقْتُكِ أَوْ سَرَّحْتُكِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever said to his wife: "You are  Haram for me."','باب مَنْ قَالَ لاِمْرَأَتِهِ أَنْتِ عَلَىَّ حَرَامٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"O Prophet! Why do you forbid that which Allah has allowed to you...?','باب ‏ {‏لِمَ تُحَرِّمُ مَا أَحَلَّ اللَّهُ لَكَ‏} ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'There is no divorce before marriage','بَابُ لاَ طَلاَقَ قَبْلَ النِّكَاحِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If, under compulsion somebody says about his wife, "She is my sister."','بَابُ إِذَا قَالَ لاِمْرَأَتِهِ وَهْوَ مُكْرَهٌ هَذِهِ أُخْتِي. فَلاَ شَيْءَ عَلَيْهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A divorce given in a state of anger, under compulsion or under the effect of intoxicants or insanity','باب الطَّلاَقِ فِي الإِغْلاَقِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Khul'' and how a divorce is given according to it','باب الْخُلْعِ وَكَيْفَ الطَّلاَقُ فِيهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Ash-Shiqaq (the breach between the man and his wife).','باب الشِّقَاقِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Selling a female slave does not lead to her divorce.','باب لاَ يَكُونُ بَيْعُ الأَمَةِ طَلاَقًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A female slave, whose husband is a slave, has the option to keep him or leave him (when she is manumitted).','باب خِيَارِ الأَمَةِ تَحْتَ الْعَبْدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The intercession of the Prophet (saws) for Barira''s husband.','باب شَفَاعَةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم فِي زَوْجِ بَرِيرَةَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Chapter','باب'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"Do not marry Al-Mushirkat till they believe..."','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {وَلاَ تَنْكِحُوا الْمُشْرِكَاتِ حَتَّى يُؤْمِنَّ وَلأَمَةٌ مُؤْمِنَةٌ خَيْرٌ مِنْ مُشْرِكَةٍ وَلَوْ أَعْجَبَتْكُمْ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Marrying Al-Mushrikat who had embraced Islam; and their ''Idda.','باب نِكَاحِ مَنْ أَسْلَمَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكَاتِ وَعِدَّتِهِنَّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If an idolatress or a Christian woman becomes a Muslim while she is the wife of Dhimmi or a Mushrik at war with the Muslims?','باب إِذَا أَسْلَمَتِ الْمُشْرِكَةُ أَوِ النَّصْرَانِيَّةُ تَحْتَ الذِّمِّيِّ أَوِ الْحَرْبِيِّ‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"Those who take an oath, not to have sexual relations with their wives, must wait four months."','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {لِلَّذِينَ يُؤْلُونَ مِنْ نِسَائِهِمْ تَرَبُّصُ أَرْبَعَةِ أَشْهُرٍ} إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: {سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ} {فَإِنْ فَاءُوا} رَجَعُوا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The regulations concerning the property and family of a lost person','باب حُكْمِ الْمَفْقُودِ فِي أَهْلِهِ وَمَالِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Az-Zihar','بَابُ الظِّهَارِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Using gestures to express the decision of divorce','باب الإِشَارَةِ فِي الطَّلاَقِ وَالأُمُورِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Li''an','باب اللِّعَانِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a husband suspects his paternity to a child.','باب إِذَا عَرَّضَ بِنَفْىِ الْوَلَدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Commanding those who are involved in a case of Li''an to take the oath.','باب إِحْلاَفِ الْمُلاَعِنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The man should start the process of Li''an.','باب يَبْدَأُ الرَّجُلُ بِالتَّلاَعُنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Li''an, and divorce after the process of Li''an.','باب اللِّعَانِ وَمَنْ طَلَّقَ بَعْدَ اللِّعَانِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To carry out Li''an in a  Mosque.','باب التَّلاَعُنِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"If I were to stone any person to death without witnesses."','باب قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏"‏ لَوْ كُنْتُ رَاجِمًا بِغَيْرِ بَيِّنَةٍ ‏"‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Mahr in the case Li''an','باب صَدَاقِ الْمُلاَعَنَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"Surely one of you two is a liar; so will one of you repent (to Allah)?"','باب قَوْلِ الإِمَامِ لِلْمُتَلاَعِنَيْنِ إِنَّ أَحَدَكُمَا كَاذِبٌ فَهَلْ مِنْكُمَا تَائِبٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The separation between those who are involved in a case of Li''an.','باب التَّفْرِيقِ بَيْنَ الْمُتَلاَعِنَيْنِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The child is to be given to the lady (accused by her husband).','باب يَلْحَقُ الْوَلَدُ بِالْمُلاَعِنَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"O Allah! Reveal the truth."','باب قَوْلِ الإِمَامِ اللَّهُمَّ بَيِّنْ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Marriage of a divorced woman to another man but he does not consummate his marriage with her','باب إِذَا طَلَّقَهَا ثَلاَثًا ثُمَّ تَزَوَّجَتْ بَعْدَ الْعِدَّةِ زَوْجًا غَيْرَهُ فَلَمْ يَمَسَّهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,38,'38',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"And those of your women as have passed the age of monthly courses..."','بَابُ: {وَاللاَّئِي يَئِسْنَ مِنَ الْمَحِيضِ مِنْ نِسَائِكُمْ إِنِ ارْتَبْتُمْ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,39,'39',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"For those who are pregnant, their ''Idda is until they laydown their burdens."','بَابُ: {وَأُولاَتُ الأَحْمَالِ أَجَلُهُنَّ أَنْ يَضَعْنَ حَمْلَهُنَّ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,40,'40',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"And divorced women shall wait for three menstrual periods."','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {وَالْمُطَلَّقَاتُ يَتَرَبَّصْنَ بِأَنْفُسِهِنَّ ثَلاَثَةَ قُرُوءٍ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The story of Fatima bint Qais','باب قِصَّةِ فَاطِمَةَ بِنْتِ قَيْسٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,42,'42',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a divorced lady is afraid that she may be attacked in her husband''s house.','باب الْمُطَلَّقَةِ إِذَا خُشِيَ عَلَيْهَا فِي مَسْكَنِ زَوْجِهَا أَنْ يُقْتَحَمَ عَلَيْهَا، أَوْ تَبْذُوَ عَلَى أَهْلِهَا بِفَاحِشَةٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,43,'43',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"And it is not lawful for them to conceal what Allah has created in their wombs."','بَابُ قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {وَلاَ يَحِلُّ لَهُنَّ أَنْ يَكْتُمْنَ مَا خَلَقَ اللَّهُ فِي أَرْحَامِهِنَّ} مِنَ الْحَيْضِ وَالْحَبَلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,44,'44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"And their husbands have the better right to take them back..."','بَابُ: {وَبُعُولَتُهُنَّ أَحَقُّ بِرَدِّهِنَّ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,45,'45',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To take back one''s wife while in her menses.','باب مُرَاجَعَةِ الْحَائِضِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,46,'46',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A widow should mourn for four months and ten days.','باب تُحِدُّ الْمُتَوَفَّى عَنْهَا زَوْجُهَا أَرْبَعَةَ أَشْهُرٍ وَعَشْرًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,47,'47',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Can a mourning lady use kohl?','باب الْكُحْلِ لِلْحَادَّةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,48,'48',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Qust (incense) may be used by a mourning after being cleaned from her menses.','باب الْقُسْطِ لِلْحَادَّةِ عِنْدَ الطُّهْرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,49,'49',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A mourning lady can wear clothes of ''Asb.','باب تَلْبَسُ الْحَادَّةُ ثِيَابَ الْعَصْبِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,50,'50',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"And those of you who die and leave behind wives..."','بَابُ: {وَالَّذِينَ يُتَوَفَّوْنَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَذَرُونَ أَزْوَاجًا} إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: {بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ خَبِيرٌ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,51,'51',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The earnings of a prostitute and the illegal wedding.','باب مَهْرِ الْبَغِيِّ وَالنِّكَاحِ الْفَاسِدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,52,'52',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Mahr of the lady whose husband entered upon her to consummate his marriage.','باب الْمَهْرِ لِلْمَدْخُولِ عَلَيْهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',68,53,'53',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The gift given by a husband to a divorced lady for whom Mahr has not been fixed.','باب الْمُتْعَةِ لِلَّتِي لَمْ يُفْرَضْ لَهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The superiority of providing for one''s family','باب فَضْلِ النَّفَقَةِ عَلَى الأَهْلِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is obligatory to spend for one''s wife and household.','باب وُجُوبِ النَّفَقَةِ عَلَى الأَهْلِ وَالْعِيَالِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To provide one''s family with food sufficient for one year in advance','باب حَبْسِ نَفَقَةِ الرَّجُلِ قُوتَ سَنَةٍ عَلَى أَهْلِهِ، وَكَيْفَ نَفَقَاتُ الْعِيَالِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The expenditure of a woman and her child, whose husband is away from her','باب نَفَقَةِ الْمَرْأَةِ إِذَا غَابَ عَنْهَا زَوْجُهَا وَنَفَقَةِ الْوَلَدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"The mothers shall give suck to their children for two whole years, for those who desire to complete the term of suckling..."','بَابٌ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The working of a lady in her husband''s house.','باب عَمَلِ الْمَرْأَةِ فِي بَيْتِ زَوْجِهَا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A servant for one''s wife','باب خَادِمِ الْمَرْأَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A man''s serving his family.','باب خِدْمَةِ الرَّجُلِ فِي أَهْلِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a man does not provide for his family','باب إِذَا لَمْ يُنْفِقِ الرَّجُلُ فَلِلْمَرْأَةِ أَنْ تَأْخُذَ بِغَيْرِ عِلْمِهِ مَا يَكْفِيهَا وَوَلَدَهَا بِالْمَعْرُوفِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A woman should take care of the wealth of her husband.','باب حِفْظِ الْمَرْأَةِ زَوْجَهَا فِي ذَاتِ يَدِهِ وَالنَّفَقَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Providing one''s wife with clothes reasonably','باب كِسْوَةِ الْمَرْأَةِ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A lady should help her husband in looking after his children','باب عَوْنِ الْمَرْأَةِ زَوْجَهَا فِي وَلَدِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The expenditure of a poor man on his family','باب نَفَقَةِ الْمُعْسِرِ عَلَى أَهْلِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"And on the heir is incumbent the like of that..."','باب ‏ {‏وَعَلَى الْوَارِثِ مِثْلُ ذَلِكَ‏} ‏ ، وَهَلْ عَلَى الْمَرْأَةِ مِنْهُ شَيْءٌ؟'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"If one dies leaving debts to be repaid or dependents to be taken care of, it is for me."','باب قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏"‏ مَنْ تَرَكَ كَلاًّ أَوْ ضَيَاعًا فَإِلَىَّ ‏"‏‏.‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',69,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Freed female slaves or any other women can be wet nurses.','باب الْمَرَاضِعِ مِنَ الْمَوَالِيَاتِ وَغَيْرِهِنَّ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Eat of the lawful things that We have provided you with..."','بَابُ وَقَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {كُلُوا مِنْ طَيِّبَاتِ مَا رَزَقْنَاكُمْ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mention the Name of Allah on starting to eat, and eat with the right hand.','باب التَّسْمِيَةِ عَلَى الطَّعَامِ وَالأَكْلِ بِالْيَمِينِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To eat of the dish what is nearer to you','باب الأَكْلِ مِمَّا يَلِيهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Eating from around the dish while taking meal with someone else.','باب مَنْ تَتَبَّعَ حَوَالَىِ الْقَصْعَةِ مَعَ صَاحِبِهِ، إِذَا لَمْ يَعْرِفْ مِنْهُ كَرَاهِيَةً'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To eat with right hand, and to start with the right side in doing other things.','باب التَّيَمُّنِ فِي الأَكْلِ وَغَيْرِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Whoever ate till he was satisfied','باب مَنْ أَكَلَ حَتَّى شَبِعَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'"There is no restriction on the blind..."','بَابُ: {لَيْسَ عَلَى الأَعْمَى حَرَجٌ} إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: {لَعَلَّكُمْ تَعْقِلُونَ}'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Thin bread and eating at a dining table.','باب الْخُبْزِ الْمُرَقَّقِ وَالأَكْلِ عَلَى الْخِوَانِ وَالسُّفْرَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'As-Sawiq','باب السَّوِيقِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prophet (saws) never used to eat anything unless it was named for him so that he might know what it was','باب مَا كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم لاَ يَأْكُلُ حَتَّى يُسَمَّى لَهُ فَيَعْلَمُ مَا هُوَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The food of one person is sufficient for two persons.','باب طَعَامُ الْوَاحِدِ يَكْفِي الاِثْنَيْنِ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A believer eats in one intestine','باب الْمُؤْمِنُ يَأْكُلُ فِي مِعًى وَاحِدٍ‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To eat while leaning','باب الأَكْلِ مُتَّكِئًا‏'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Roasted (meat).','بَابُ الشِّوَاءِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Khazira (dish prepared with while flour and fat)','باب الْخَزِيرَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Aqit (dried yoghourt)','باب الأَقِطِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'As-Salq (a kind of beet) and barley','باب السِّلْقِ وَالشَّعِيرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To seize and catch flesh with the teeth (while eating).','باب النَّهْسِ وَانْتِشَالِ اللَّحْمِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To eat the flesh of a foreleg (by stripping the bone of its meat with the teeth).','باب تَعَرُّقِ الْعَضُدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To cut the meat with a knife','باب قَطْعِ اللَّحْمِ بِالسِّكِّينِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prophet (saws) never criticized any food.','باب مَا عَابَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم طَعَامًا'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'To blow barley (to remove the husk).','باب النَّفْخِ فِي الشَّعِيرِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What the Prophet (saws) and his Companions used to eat.','باب مَا كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَأَصْحَابُهُ يَأْكُلُونَ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'At-Talbina (a kind of dish prepared from flour or bran)','باب التَّلْبِينَةِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Ath-Tharid (a dish prepared from meat and bread).','باب الثَّرِيدِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A roasted sheep.','باب شَاةٍ مَسْمُوطَةٍ وَالْكَتِفِ وَالْجَنْبِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Storage of food in the houses and on a journey','باب مَا كَانَ السَّلَفُ يَدَّخِرُونَ فِي بُيُوتِهِمْ وَأَسْفَارِهِمْ مِنَ الطَّعَامِ وَاللَّحْمِ وَغَيْرِهِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Hais (dish prepared from dried yoghourt, butter and dates).','باب الْحَيْسِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Eating in a dish decorated with silver','باب الأَكْلِ فِي إِنَاءٍ مُفَضَّضٍ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The mention of food','باب ذِكْرِ الطَّعَامِ'),
('sahih-al-bukhari',70,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Al-Udm (additional food taken with bread).','باب الأُدْمِ'),
