('sahih-muslim',5,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is disliked to delay the prayers beyond their proper times, and what a person should do if the Imam delays the prayer','باب كَرَاهِيَةِ تَأْخِيرِ الصَّلاَةِ عَنْ وَقْتِهَا الْمُخْتَارِ وَمَا يَفْعَلُهُ الْمَأْمُومُ إِذَا أَخَّرَهَا الإِمَامُ'),
('sahih-muslim',5,42,'42',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of prayer in congregation, and clarifying the stern warning against staying away from it, and that it is fard kifayah','باب فَضْلِ صَلاَةِ الجَمَاعَةِ وَبَيَانِ التَّشْدِيدِ فِي التَّخَلُّفِ عَنْهَا ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,43,'43',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is obligatory for the one who hears the call to prayer to come to the masjid','باب يَجِبُ إِتْيَانُ الْمَسْجِدِ عَلَى مَنْ سَمِعَ النِّدَاءَ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,44,'44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Prayer in congregation is one of the sunnah of guidance','باب صَلاَةُ الْجَمَاعَةِ مِنْ سُنَنِ الْهُدَى ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,45,'45',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of leaving the masjid once the Mu’adhdhin has called the Adhan','باب النَّهْىِ عَنِ الْخُرُوجِ، مِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ إِذَا أَذَّنَ الْمُؤَذِّنُ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,46,'46',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of praying `Isha and Subh in congregation','باب فَضْلِ صَلاَةِ الْعِشَاءِ وَالصُّبْحِ فِي جَمَاعَةٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,47,'47',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Concession allowing one to not attend the congregation if there is an excuse','باب الرُّخْصَةِ فِي التَّخَلُّفِ عَنِ الْجَمَاعَةِ، بِعُذْرٍ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,48,'48',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to offer voluntary prayers in congregation, and to pray on hasir (palm-fiber mats), khumrah (small mats), cloth, and other pure things','باب جَوَازِ الْجَمَاعَةِ فِي النَّافِلَةِ وَالصَّلاَةِ عَلَى حَصِيرٍ وَخُمْرَةٍ وَثَوْبٍ وَغَيْرِهَا مِنَ الطَّاهِرَاتِ'),
('sahih-muslim',5,49,'49',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of offering the obligatory prayers in congregation, the virtue of waiting for prayer and taking many steps towards the masjid, the virtue of walking to the masjid','باب فَضْلِ صَلاَةِ الْجَمَاعَةِ وَانْتِظَارِ الصَّلاَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,50,'50',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of taking many steps to the masjid','باب فَضْلِ كَثْرَةِ الْخُطَا إِلَى الْمَسَاجِدِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,51,'51',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Walking to prayer erases sins and raises one in status','باب الْمَشْىُ إِلَى الصَّلاَةِ تُمْحَى بِهِ الْخَطَايَا وَتُرْفَعُ بِهِ الدَّرَجَاتُ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,52,'52',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of sitting in one’s prayer place after Subh, and the virtue of the masajid','باب فَضْلِ الْجُلُوسِ فِي مُصَلاَّهُ بَعْدَ الصُّبْحِ وَفَضْلِ الْمَسَاجِدِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,53,'53',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Who is more entitled to lead the prayer','باب مَنْ أَحَقُّ بِالإِمَامَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',5,54,'54',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to say qunut in all prayers if a calamity befalls the Muslims – and refuge is sought from Allah (regarding that). It is recommended to say qunut in Subh at all times. And the clarification that it is to be said after raising the head from bowing in the final rak`ah, and it is recommended to say it out loud','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ الْقُنُوتِ فِي جَمِيعِ الصَّلاَةِ إِذَا نزَلَتْ بِالْمُسْلِمِينَ نَازِلَةٌ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',5,55,'55',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Making up a missed prayer. And it is recommended to hasten to make it up','باب قَضَاءِ الصَّلاَةِ الْفَائِتَةِ وَاسْتِحْبَابِ تَعْجِيلِ قَضَائِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The travelers’ prayer and shortening it','باب صَلاَةِ الْمُسَافِرِينَ وَقَصْرِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Shortening the prayer in Mina','باب قَصْرِ الصَّلاَةِ بِمِنًى ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Praying in dwellings when it is raining','باب الصَّلاَةِ فِي الرحَالِ فِي الْمَطَرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to offer voluntary prayers atop one’s mount when travelling, no matter what direction it is facing','باب جَوَازِ صَلاَةِ النَّافِلَةِ عَلَى الدَّابَّةِ فِي السَّفَرِ حَيْثُ تَوَجَّهَتْ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to combine two prayers when traveling','باب جَوَازِ الْجَمْعِ بَيْنَ الصَّلاَتَيْنِ فِي السَّفَرِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Joining two prayers when not traveling','باب الْجَمْعِ بَيْنَ الصَّلاَتَيْنِ فِي الْحَضَرِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to leave to the right or left after finishing the prayer','باب جَوَاز الاِنْصِرَافِ مِنَ الصَّلاَةِ عَنِ الْيَمِينِ، وَالشِّمَالِ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to stand to the right of the Imam','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ يَمِينِ الإِمَامِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is disliked to start a voluntary prayer after the Mu’adhdhin has started to say Iqamah for prayer, whether that is a regular sunnah, such as the sunnah of Subh or Zuhr, or anything else, and regardless of whether he knows that he will catch up with the rak`ah with the Imam or not','باب كَرَاهَةِ الشُّرُوعِ فِي نَافِلَةٍ بَعْدَ شُرُوعِ الْمُؤَذِّنِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What to say when entering the masjid','باب مَا يَقُولُ إِذَا دَخَلَ الْمَسْجِدَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to greet the masjid by praying two rak`ah, and it is disliked to sit before praying these two rak`ah, and this is prescribed at all times','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ تَحِيَّةِ الْمَسْجِدِ بِرَكْعَتَيْنِ وَكَرَاهَةِ الْجُلُوسِ قَبْلَ صَلاَتِهِمَا وَأَنَّهَا مَشْرُوعَةٌ فِي جَمِيعِ الأَوْقَاتِ'),
('sahih-muslim',6,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to pray two rak`ah in the masjid for one who has come from a journey, when he first arrives','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ الرَّكْعَتَيْنِ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ لِمَنْ قَدِمَ مِنْ سَفَرٍ أَوَّلَ قُدُومِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to pray Duha, the least of which is two rak`ah, the best of which is eight, and the average of which is four or six, and encouragement to do so regularly','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ صَلاَةِ الضُّحَى وَأَنَّ أَقَلَّهَا رَكْعَتَانِ وَأَكْمَلَهَا ثَمَانِ رَكَعَاتٍ وَأَوْسَطَهَا أَرْبَعُ رَكَعَاتٍ أَوْ سِتٌّ وَالْحَثِّ عَلَى الْمُحَافَظَةِ عَلَيْهَا'),
('sahih-muslim',6,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to pray two rak`ah for the sunnah of Fajr. And encouragement to pray them regularly, and to make them brief, and to persist in offering them, and clarifying what is recommended to recite therein','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ رَكْعَتَيْ سُنَّةِ الْفَجْرِ وَالْحَثِّ عَلَيْهِمَا وَتَخْفِيفِهِمَا وَالْمُحَافَظَةِ عَلَيْهِمَا وَبَيَانِ مَا يُسْتَحَبُّ أَنْ يُقْرَأَ فِيهِمَا'),
('sahih-muslim',6,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of the regular sunnah prayers before and after the obligatory prayers, and their numbers','باب فَضْلِ السُّنَنِ الرَّاتِبَةِ قَبْلَ الْفَرَائِضِ وَبَعْدَهُنَّ وَبَيَانِ عَدَدِهِنَّ'),
('sahih-muslim',6,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to offer voluntary prayers standing or sitting, and to stand and sit in the same rak`ah','باب جَوَازِ النَّافِلَةِ قَائِمًا وَقَاعِدًا وَفِعْلِ بَعْضِ الرَّكْعَةِ قَائِمًا وَبَعْضِهَا قَاعِدًا ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Night prayers and the number of rak`ah offered by the Prophet (saws) at night, and that Witr is one rak`ah, and a one-rak`ah prayer is correct','باب صَلاَةِ اللَّيْلِ وَعَدَدِ رَكَعَاتِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي اللَّيْلِ وَأَنَّ الْوِتْرَ رَكْعَةٌ وَأَنَّ الرَّكْعَةَ صَلاَةٌ صَحِيحَةٌ'),
('sahih-muslim',6,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Night prayer, and the one who sleeps and misses it or is sick','باب جَامِعِ صَلاَةِ اللَّيْلِ وَمَنْ نَامَ عَنْهُ أَوْ مَرِضَ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Salat al-Awwabin (the prayer of the penitent) is when the young camels feel the heat of the hot sand','باب صَلاَةُ الأَوَّابِينَ حِينَ تَرْمَضُ الْفِصَالُ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The night prayers are two by two, and Witr is one rakah at the end of the night','باب صَلاَةُ اللَّيْلِ مَثْنَى مَثْنَى وَالْوِتْرُ رَكْعَةٌ مِنْ آخِرِ اللَّيْلِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One who fears that he will not get up at the end of the night, then he should pray Witr at the beginning of the night','باب مَنْ خَافَ أَنْ لاَ يَقُومَ مِنْ آخِرِ اللَّيْلِ فَلْيُوتِرْ أَوَّلَهُ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The best prayer is that in which one stands for a long time (tuwlul-qunut)','باب أَفْضَلُ الصَّلاَةِ طُولُ الْقُنُوتِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'In the night there is an hour when supplications are answered','باب فِي اللَّيْلِ سَاعَةٌ مُسْتَجَابٌ فِيهَا الدُّعَاءُ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Encouragement to supplicate and recite statements of remembrance at the end of the night, and the response to that','باب التَّرْغِيبِ فِي الدُّعَاءِ وَالذِّكْرِ فِي آخِرِ اللَّيْلِ وَالإِجَابَةِ فِيهِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Encouragement to pray qiyam during Ramadan, which is Tarawih','باب التَّرْغِيبِ فِي قِيَامِ رَمَضَانَ وَهُوَ التَّرَاوِيحُ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prayer and the supplication of the Prophet (saws) at night','باب الدُّعَاءِ فِي صَلاَةِ اللَّيْلِ وَقِيَامِهِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to recite for a long time in the night prayers','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ تَطْوِيلِ الْقِرَاءَةِ فِي صَلاَةِ اللَّيْلِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Encouragement to pray at night even if it is little','باب مَا رُوِيَ فِيمَنْ، نَامَ اللَّيْلَ أَجْمَعَ حَتَّى أَصْبَحَ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to offer voluntary prayers in one’s house although it is permissible to offer them in the masjid','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ صَلاَةِ النَّافِلَةِ فِي بَيْتِهِ وَجَوَازِهَا فِي الْمَسْجِدِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of a deed that is done persistently, whether it be Qiyam al-Lail or anything else. The command to be moderate in worship, which means adopting what one can persist in. The command to the one who gets tired or weary when praying  to stop until that feeling passes','باب فَضِيلَةِ الْعَمَلِ الدَّائِمِ مِنْ قِيَامِ اللَّيْلِ وَغَيْرِهِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The command to one who becomes sleepy while praying, or who starts to falter in his recitation of the Qur’an or statements of remembrance, to lie down or sit down until that goes away','باب أَمْرِ مَنْ نَعَسَ فِي صَلاَتِهِ أَوِ اسْتَعْجَمَ عَلَيْهِ الْقُرْآنُ أَوِ الذِّكْرُ بِأَنْ يَرْقُدَ أَوْ يَقْعُدَ حَتَّى يَذْهَبَ عَنْهُ ذَلِكَ'),
('sahih-muslim',6,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The book of the virtues of the Qur’an etc','باب فَضَائِلِ الْقُرْآنِ وَمَا يَتَعَلَّقُ بِهِ'),
('sahih-muslim',6,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The command to keep refreshing one’s knowledge of the Qur’an and that it is disliked to say I have forgotten such-and-such a verse, but it is permissible to say I have been caused to forget','باب الأَمْرِ بِتَعَهُّدِ الْقُرْآنِ وَكَرَاهَةِ قَوْلِ نَسِيتُ آيَةَ كَذَا. وَجَوَازِ قَوْلِ أُنْسِيتُهَا'),
('sahih-muslim',6,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to make one’s voice beautiful when reciting Qur’an','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ تَحْسِينِ الصَّوْتِ بِالْقُرْآنِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Mentioning the recitation of the Prophet (saws) of Surat al-Fath on the day of the conquest of Makkah','باب ذِكْرِ قِرَاءَةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم سُورَةَ الْفَتْحِ يَوْمَ فَتْحِ مَكَّةَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The descent of tranquility (sakinah) when the Qur’an is recited','باب نُزُولِ السَّكِينَةِ لِقِرَاءَةِ الْقُرْآنِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of the one who memorizes the Qur’an','باب فَضِيلَةِ حَافِظِ الْقُرْآنِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,38,'38',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of the one who is skilled in reciting Qur’an and the one who falters in reciting','باب فَضْلِ الْمَاهِرِ بِالْقُرْآنِ وَالَّذِي يَتَتَعْتَعُ فِيهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,39,'39',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to recite the Qur’an to people of virtue who are skilled in its recitation, even if the reciter is better than the one to whom it is recited','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ قِرَاءَةِ الْقُرْآنِ عَلَى أَهْلِ الْفَضْلِ وَالْحُذَّاقِ فِيهِ وَإِنْ كَانَ الْقَارِئُ أَفْضَلَ مِنَ الْمَقْرُوءِ عَلَيْهِ'),
('sahih-muslim',6,40,'40',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of listening to the Qur’an, asking one who has memorized it to recite so that one may listen, weeping when reciting, and pondering the meanings','باب فَضْلِ اسْتِمَاعِ الْقُرْآنِ وَطَلَبِ الْقِرَاءَةِ مِنْ حَافِظِهِ لِلاِسْتِمَاعِ وَالْبُكَاءِ عِنْدَ الْقِرَاءَةِ وَالتَّدَبُّرِ'),
('sahih-muslim',6,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of reciting the Qur’an in prayer and learning it','باب فَضْلِ قِرَاءَةِ الْقُرْآنِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ وَتَعَلُّمِهِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,42,'42',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of reciting the Qur’an and Surat al-Baqarah','باب فَضْلِ قِرَاءَةِ الْقُرْآنِ وَسُورَةِ الْبَقَرَةِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,43,'43',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of al-Fatihah and the closing verse of Surat al-Baqarah; and the encouragement to recite the two verses at the end of Surat al-Baqarah','اب فَضْلِ الْفَاتِحَةِ وَخَوَاتِيمِ سُورَةِ الْبَقَرَةِ وَالْحَثِّ عَلَى قِرَاءَةِ الآيَتَيْنِ مِنْ آخِرِ الْبَقَرَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',6,44,'44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of Surat al-Kahf and Ayat al-Kursi','باب فَضْلِ سُورَةِ الْكَهْفِ وَآيَةِ الْكُرْسِيِّ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,45,'45',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of reciting Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad','باب فَضْلِ قِرَاءَةِ ‏ {‏ قُلْ هُوَ اللَّهُ أَحَدٌ‏} ‏ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,46,'46',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of reciting al-Mu`awwidhatain (the two surahs seeking refuge with Allah)','باب فَضْلِ قِرَاءَةِ الْمُعَوِّذَتَيْنِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,47,'47',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of one who acts in accordance with the Qur’an and teaches it. And the virtue of one who learns wisdom from Fiqh or other types of knowledge, then acts upon it and teaches it','باب فَضْلِ مَنْ يَقُومُ بِالْقُرْآنِ وَيُعَلِّمُهُ وَفَضْلِ مَنْ تَعَلَّمَ حِكْمَةً مِنْ فِقْهٍ أَوْ غَيْرِهِ فَعَمِلَ بِهَا وَعَلَّمَهَا'),
('sahih-muslim',6,48,'48',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The clarification that the Qur’an was revealed in seven ahruf (modes of recitation), and clarifying its meaning','باب بَيَانِ أَنَّ الْقُرْآنَ عَلَى سَبْعَةِ أَحْرُفٍ وَبَيَانِ مَعْنَاهُ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,49,'49',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Slow, measured pace of recitation (tartil), and to not rush when reciting, and the permissibility of reciting two or more surahs in one rak`ah','باب تَرْتِيلِ الْقِرَاءَةِ وَاجْتِنَابِ الْهَذِّ وَهُوَ الإِفْرَاطُ فِي السُّرْعَةِ وَإِبَاحَةِ سُورَتَيْنِ فَأَكْثَرَ فِي الرَّكْعَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',6,50,'50',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Concerning various recitations','باب مَا يَتَعَلَّقُ بِالْقِرَاءَاتِ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,51,'51',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The times when it is forbidden to offer salat','باب الأَوْقَاتِ الَّتِي نُهِيَ عَنِ الصَّلاَةِ، فِيهَا ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,52,'52',NULL,NULL,NULL,'How `Amr bin `Abasah became Muslim','باب إِسْلاَمِ عَمْرِو بْنِ عَبَسَةَ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,53,'53',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Do not aim to pray when the sun is rising or setting','باب لاَ تَتَحَرَّوْا بِصَلاَتِكُمْ طُلُوعَ الشَّمْسِ وَلاَ غُرُوبَهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',6,54,'54',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Concerning the two rak`ah that the Prophet (saws) used to pray after `Asr','باب مَعْرِفَةِ الرَّكْعَتَيْنِ اللَّتَيْنِ كَانَ يُصَلِّيهِمَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْدَ الْعَصْرِ'),
