('sahih-muslim',27,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The vow of a disbeliever, and what he should do about it if he becomes a muslim','باب نَذْرِ الْكَافِرِ وَمَا يَفْعَلُ فِيهِ إِذَا أَسْلَمَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',27,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Treatment of slaves, and the expiation of one who slaps his slave','باب صُحْبَةِ الْمَمَالِيكِ وَكَفَّارَةِ مَنْ لَطَمَ عَبْدَهُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',27,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Stern warning against accusing a slave of fornication','باب التَّغْلِيظِ عَلَى مَنْ قَذَفَ مَمْلُوكَهُ بِالزِّنَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',27,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Feeding a slave what one eats and clothing him as one clothes oneself, and not burdening him with more than he bear','باب إِطْعَامِ الْمَمْلُوكِ مِمَّا يَأْكُلُ وَإِلْبَاسِهِ مَمَّا يَلْبَسُ وَلاَ يُكَلِّفُهُ مَا يَغْلِبُهُ'),
('sahih-muslim',27,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The reward of a slave who is sincere towards his master and worships Allah properly','باب ثَوَابِ الْعَبْدِ وَأَجْرِهِ إِذَا نَصَحَ لِسَيِّدِهِ وَأَحْسَنَ عِبَادَةَ اللَّهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',27,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One who frees his share in a slave','باب مَنْ أَعْتَقَ شِرْكًا لَهُ فِي عَبْدٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',27,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Permissibility of selling a Mudabbar','باب جَوَازِ بَيْعِ الْمُدَبَّرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',28,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Qasamah (Oaths)','باب الْقَسَامَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',28,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The ruling on Muharibin and Apostates','باب حُكْمِ الْمُحَارِبِينَ وَالْمُرْتَدِّينَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',28,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Confirmation of Qisas in the case of killing with a rock and other sharp or heavy objects, and the killing of a man for a woman','باب ثُبُوتِ الْقِصَاصِ فِي الْقَتْلِ بِالْحَجَرِ وَغَيْرِهِ مِنَ الْمُحَدَّدَاتِ وَالْمُثَقَّلاَتِ وَقَتْلِ الرَّجُلِ بِالْمَرْأَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',28,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a person attacks another person''s life and limb, and the other defends himself and kills him or injures him, there is no penalty on him','باب الصَّائِلُ عَلَى نَفْسِ الإِنْسَانِ أَوْ عُضْوِهِ  إِذَا دَفَعَهُ الْمَصُولُ عَلَيْهِ فَأَتْلَفَ نَفْسَهُ أَوْ عُضْوَهَ لاَ ضَمَانَ عَلَيْهِ'),
('sahih-muslim',28,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The validity of Qisas for teeth and the like','باب إِثْبَاتِ الْقِصَاصِ فِي الأَسْنَانِ وَمَا فِي مَعْنَاهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',28,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'When it is permissible to shed the blood of a muslim','باب مَا يُبَاحُ بِهِ دَمُ الْمُسْلِمِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',28,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The sin of the one who set the precedent of killing','باب بَيَانِ إِثْمِ مَنْ سَنَّ الْقَتْلَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',28,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The punishment for bloodshed in the hereafter, and bloodshed will be the first thing concerning which judgement is passed among the people on the Day of Resurrection','باب الْمُجَازَاةِ بِالدِّمَاءِ فِي الآخِرَةِ  وَأَنَّهَا أَوَّلُ مَا يُقْضَى فِيهِ بَيْنَ النَّاسِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',28,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Emphasis on the sanctity of Blood, Honor and Wealth','باب تَغْلِيظِ تَحْرِيمِ الدِّمَاءِ وَالأَعْرَاضِ وَالأَمْوَالِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',28,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'A confession to murder is valid and the heir of the victim is entitled to Qisas, but it is recommended to ask him to let him go','باب صِحَّةِ الإِقْرَارِ بِالْقَتْلِ وَتَمْكِينِ وَلِيِّ الْقَتِيلِ مِنَ الْقِصَاصِ  وَاسْتِحْبَابِ طَلَبِ الْعَفْوِ مِنْهُ'),
('sahih-muslim',28,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Diyah for a fetus; and the Diyah for accidental killing and the ambiguous killing must be paid by the shahiqilah of the killer','باب دِيَةِ الْجَنِينِ وَوُجُوبِ الدِّيَةِ فِي قَتْلِ الْخَطَإِ وَشِبْهِ الْعَمْدِ عَلَى عَاقِلَةِ الْجَانِي'),
('sahih-muslim',29,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Hadd for stealing and the minimum threshold','باب حَدِّ السَّرِقَةِ وَنِصَابِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',29,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Cutting off the hand of a thief from the nobility and others; the prohibition of interceding with regard to Hudud punishments','باب قَطْعِ السَّارِقِ الشَّرِيفِ وَغَيْرِهِ وَالنَّهْىِ عَنِ الشَّفَاعَةِ فِي الْحُدُودِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',29,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Hadd punishment for Zina (fornication, adultery)','باب حَدِّ الزِّنَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',29,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Stoning of a married person for Zina','باب رَجْمِ الثَّيِّبِ فِي الزِّنَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',29,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One who confesses to Zina','باب مَنِ اعْتَرَفَ عَلَى نَفْسِهِ بِالزِّنَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',29,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Stoning Jews and Ahl Adh-Dhimmah for Zina','باب رَجْمِ الْيَهُودِ أَهْلِ الذِّمَّةِ فِي الزِّنَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',29,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Delaying the Hadd punishment in the case of women who have just given birth','باب تَأْخِيرِ الْحَدِّ عَنِ النُّفَسَاءِ، ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',29,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hadd punishment for drinking alcohol','باب حَدِّ الْخَمْرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',29,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Number of lashes in the case of ta''zeer','باب قَدْرِ أَسْوَاطِ التَّعْزِيرِ'),
('sahih-muslim',29,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Hadd punishments are an expiation for those on whom they are carried out','باب الْحُدُودُ كَفَّارَاتٌ لأَهْلِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',29,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'There is no Diyah for injuries caused by animals or by falling into a mine or well','باب جَرْحُ الْعَجْمَاءِ وَالْمَعْدِنِ وَالْبِئْرِ جُبَارٌ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Oath should be sworn by the defendant','باب الْيَمِينُ عَلَى الْمُدَّعَى عَلَيْهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The obligation of judging on the basis of a witness and an oath','باب الْقَضَاءِ بِالْيَمِينِ وَالشَّاهِدِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'So the judgement of the judge does not change what happened','باب الْحُكْمِ بِالظَّاهِرِ وَاللَّحْنِ بِالْحُجَّةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The case of Hind','باب قَضِيَّةِ هِنْدٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of asking too much with no need. The prohibition of withholding the rights of others and asking of them, which means refusing to give others their rights and asking for that to which one is not entitles','باب النَّهْيِ عَنْ كَثْرَةِ الْمَسَائِلِ مِنْ غَيْرِ حَاجَةٍ وَالنَّهْيِ عَنْ مَنْعٍ وَهَاتٍ وَهُوَ الاِمْتِنَاعُ مِنْ أَدَاءِ حَقٍّ لَزِمَهُ أَوْ طَلَبُ مَا لاَ يَسْتَحِقُّهُ'),
('sahih-muslim',30,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The reward of the judge if he strives to reach a decision, whether he gets it right or wrong','باب بَيَانِ أَجْرِ الْحَاكِمِ إِذَا اجْتَهَدَ فَأَصَابَ أَوْ أَخْطَأَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is disliked for a judge to pass a judgement when he is angry','باب كَرَاهَةِ قَضَاءِ الْقَاضِي وَهُوَ غَضْبَانُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Rejection of wrong rulings and of newly-invented matters','باب نَقْضِ الأَحْكَامِ الْبَاطِلَةِ وَرَدِّ مُحْدَثَاتِ الأُمُورِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The best of witnesses','باب بَيَانِ خَيْرِ الشُّهُودِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Differences between mujtahids','باب بَيَانِ اخْتِلاَفِ الْمُجْتَهِدِينَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',30,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended for a judge to reconcile between disputants','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ إِصْلاَحِ الْحَاكِمِ بَيْنَ الْخَصْمَيْنِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',31,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Picking up property lost by a pilgrim','باب'),
('sahih-muslim',31,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Milking animals is unlawful if the owner has not given permission','باب فِي لُقَطَةِ الْحَاجِّ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',31,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hospitality etc','باب تَحْرِيمِ حَلْبِ الْمَاشِيَةِ بِغَيْرِ إِذْنِ مَالِكِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',31,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to spend surplus wealth','باب الضِّيَافَةِ وَنَحْوِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',31,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to mix provisions if they are few, and to share them out','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ الْمُؤَاسَاةِ بِفُضُولِ الْمَالِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',31,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'باب اسْتِحْبَابِ خَلْطِ الأَزْوَادِ إِذَا قَلَّتْ وَالْمُؤَاسَاةِ فِيهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Permissibility of raiding the Kuffar, who have been reached with the call of Islam, without giving prior warning','باب جَوَازِ الإِغَارَةِ عَلَى الْكُفَّارِ الَّذِينَ بَلَغَتْهُمْ دَعْوَةُ الإِسْلاَمِ  مِنْ غَيْرِ تَقَدُّمِ الإِعْلاَمِ بِالإِغَارَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',32,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Ruler appointing leaders of expeditions and advising them of the etiquette of war, etc.','باب تَأْمِيرِ الإِمَامِ الأُمَرَاءَ عَلَى الْبُعُوثِ وَوَصِيَّتِهِ إِيَّاهُمْ بِآدَابِ الْغَزْوِ وَغَيْرِهَا'),
('sahih-muslim',32,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The command to show leniency and avoid causing aversion (towards Islam)','باب فِي الأَمْرِ بِالتَّيْسِيرِ وَتَرْكِ التَّنْفِيرِ'),
('sahih-muslim',32,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of betrayal','باب تَحْرِيمِ الْغَدْرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Permissibility of deceit in war','باب جَوَازِ الْخِدَاعِ فِي الْحَرْبِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is disliked to wish to meet the enemy, and the command to be steadfast when meeting the enemy','باب كَرَاهَةِ تَمَنِّي لِقَاءِ الْعَدُوِّ وَالأَمْرِ بِالصَّبْرِ عِنْدَ اللِّقَاءِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to pray for victory when meeting the enemy','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ الدُّعَاءِ بِالنَّصْرِ عِنْدَ لِقَاءِ الْعَدُوِّ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of killing women and children in war','باب تَحْرِيمِ قَتْلِ النِّسَاءِ وَالصِّبْيَانِ فِي الْحَرْبِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Permissibility of killing women and children in night raids, so long as it is not done deliberately','باب جَوَازِ قَتْلِ النِّسَاءِ وَالصِّبْيَانِ فِي الْبَيَاتِ مِنْ غَيْرِ تَعَمُّدٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Permissibility of cutting down the trees of the Kuffar and burning them','باب جَوَازِ قَطْعِ أَشْجَارِ الْكُفَّارِ وَتَحْرِيقِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'War booty has been made permissible for this Ummah only','باب تَحْلِيلِ الْغَنَائِمِ لِهَذِهِ الأُمَّةِ خَاصَّةً ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Spoils of War','باب الأَنْفَالِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The killer is entitled to the belongings of the one who is killed','باب اسْتِحْقَاقِ الْقَاتِلِ سَلَبَ الْقَتِيلِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Additional rewards, and ransoming muslims in return for prisoners','باب التَّنْفِيلِ وَفِدَاءِ الْمُسْلِمِينَ بِالأَسَارَى ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Ruling on Fai'' (Booty acquired without fighting)','باب حُكْمِ الْفَىْءِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The words of the Prophet (saws): "We (Prophets) have no heirs and whatever we leave behind is charity."','باب قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏"‏ لاَ نُورَثُ مَا تَرَكْنَا فَهُوَ صَدَقَةٌ ‏"‏ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'How booty is to be shared among the fighters','باب كَيْفِيَّةِ قِسْمَةِ الْغَنِيمَةِ بَيْنَ الْحَاضِرِينَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The support of the angels during the Battle of Badr, and the permissibility of the spoils','باب الإِمْدَادِ بِالْمَلاَئِكَةِ فِي غَزْوَةِ بَدْرٍ وَإِبَاحَةِ الْغَنَائِمِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Tying up and detaining captives, and the permissibility of releasing them without a ransom','باب رَبْطِ الأَسِيرِ وَحَبْسِهِ وَجَوَازِ الْمَنِّ عَلَيْهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Expulsion of the Jews from the Hijaz','باب إِجْلاَءِ الْيَهُودِ مِنَ الْحِجَازِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Expulsion of Jews and Christians from the Arabian Peninsula','باب إِخْرَاجِ الْيَهُودِ وَالنَّصَارَى مِنْ جَزِيرَةِ الْعَرَبِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Permissibility of fighting those who break a treaty; Permissibility of letting besieged people surrender, subject to the judgement of a just person who is qualified to pass judgement','باب جَوَازِ قِتَالِ مَنْ نَقَضَ الْعَهْدَ وَجَوَازِ إِنْزَالِ أَهْلِ الْحِصْنِ عَلَى حُكْمِ حَاكِمٍ عَدْلٍ أَهْلٍ لِلْحُكْمِ'),
('sahih-muslim',32,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hastening to fight, and giving precedence to the more urgent of two tasks when a choice must be made','باب مَنْ لَزِمَهُ أَمْرٌ فَدَخَلَ عَلَيْهِ أَمْرٌ آخَرُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Muhajirun returned to the Ansar the gifts of trees and fruits when they became independent of means through the conquests','باب رَدِّ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ إِلَى الأَنْصَارِ مَنَائِحَهُمْ مِنَ الشَّجَرِ وَالثَّمَرِ حِينَ اسْتَغْنَوْا عَنْهَا بِالْفُتُوحِ'),
('sahih-muslim',32,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Permissibility of eating food seized as booty in Dar Al-Harb','باب أَخْذِ الطَّعَامِ مِنْ أَرْضِ الْعَدُوِّ ‏‏'),
