('sahih-muslim',32,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prophet (saws) wrote to the Kings of the Kuffar, inviting them to Islam','باب كُتُبِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم إِلَى مُلُوكِ الْكُفَّارِ يَدْعُوهُمْ إِلَى اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ'),
('sahih-muslim',32,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Battle of Hunain','باب فِي غَزْوَةِ حُنَيْنٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Battle of At-Ta''if','باب غَزْوَةِ الطَّائِفِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Battle of Badr','باب غَزْوَةِ بَدْرٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The conquest of Makkah','باب فَتْحِ مَكَّةَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Removal of Idols from around the Ka''bah','باب إِزَالَةِ الأَصْنَامِ مِنْ حَوْلِ الْكَعْبَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'No man if Quraish is to be captured then killed, after the conquest','باب لاَ يُقْتَلُ قُرَشِيٌّ صَبْرًا بَعْدَ الْفَتْحِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The truce of Al-Hudaybiyah','باب صُلْحِ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ فِي الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Upholding Covenants','باب الْوَفَاءِ بِالْعَهْدِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Battle of Al-Ahzab (The Confederates)','باب غَزْوَةِ الأَحْزَابِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Battle of Uhud','باب غَزْوَةِ أُحُدٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,38,'38',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The intense wrath of Allah towards the one who was killed by the messenger of Allah (saws)','باب اشْتِدَادِ غَضَبِ اللَّهِ عَلَى مَنْ قَتَلَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,39,'39',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The persecution suffered by the prophet (saws) at the hands of the idolaters and hypocrites','باب مَا لَقِيَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم مِنْ أَذَى الْمُشْرِكِينَ وَالْمُنَافِقِينَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,40,'40',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The supplication of the Prophet (saws) and his steadfastness in the face of the hypocrites'' persecution','باب فِي دُعَاءِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم إِلَى اللَّهِ وَصَبْرِهِ عَلَى أَذَى الْمُنَافِقِينَ'),
('sahih-muslim',32,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The slaying of Abu Jahl','باب قَتْلِ أَبِي جَهْلٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,42,'42',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The slaying of Ka''b Bin Al-Ashraf, the Tagut of the Jews','باب قَتْلِ كَعْبِ بْنِ الأَشْرَفِ طَاغُوتِ الْيَهُودِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,43,'43',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Battle of Khaibar','باب غَزْوَةِ خَيْبَرَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,44,'44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Battle of Al-Ahzab (The Confederates), also known as Al-Khandaq (The Ditch)','باب غَزْوَةِ الأَحْزَابِ وَهِيَ الْخَنْدَقُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,45,'45',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Battle of Dhu Qarad and other battles','باب غَزْوَةِ ذِي قَرَدٍ وَغَيْرِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,46,'46',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The words of Allah, the Most High: "And He it is who has withheld their hands from you"','باب قَوْلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى: {وَهُوَ الَّذِي كَفَّ أَيْدِيَهُمْ عَنْكُمْ} الآيَةَ:'),
('sahih-muslim',32,47,'47',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Women participating in military expeditions with the men','باب غَزْوَةِ النِّسَاءِ مَعَ الرِّجَالِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',32,48,'48',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Women who take part in military expeditions are to be given a reward but not a regular share; And the prohibition of killing children of the enemy','باب النِّسَاءُ الْغَازِيَاتُ يُرْضَخُ لَهُنَّ وَلاَ يُسْهَمُ وَالنَّهْىُ عَنْ قَتْلِ صِبْيَانِ أَهْلِ الْحَرْبِ'),
('sahih-muslim',32,49,'49',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The number of campaigns of the Prophet (saws)','باب عَدَدِ غَزَوَاتِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم'),
('sahih-muslim',32,50,'50',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The campaign of Dhat Ar-Riqa','باب غَزْوَةِ ذَاتِ الرِّقَاعِ'),
('sahih-muslim',32,51,'51',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is disliked to seek the help of a disbeliever in wars (except in cases of necessity, or if he thinks well of the Muslims)','باب كَرَاهَةِ الاِسْتِعَانَةِ فِي الْغَزْوِ بِكَافِرٍ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The people follow the Quraish and the Caliphate belongs to the Quraish','باب النَّاسُ تَبَعٌ لِقُرَيْشٍ وَالْخِلاَفَةُ فِي قُرَيْشٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Appointing a successor or not doing so','باب الاِسْتِخْلاَفِ وَتَرْكِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of seeking or desiring a position of authority','باب النَّهْىِ عَنْ طَلَبِ الإِمَارَةِ، وَالْحِرْصِ، عَلَيْهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is disliked to be appointed to a position of authority unnecessarily','باب كَرَاهَةِ الإِمَارَةِ بِغَيْرِ ضَرُورَةٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of a just ruler and the punishment of a tyrant; Encouragement to treat those under one''s authority with kindness and the prohibition against causing them hardship','باب فَضِيلَةِ الإِمَامِ الْعَادِلِ وَعُقُوبَةِ الْجَائِرِ وَالْحَثِّ عَلَى الرِّفْقِ بِالرَّعِيَّةِ وَالنَّهْيِ عَنْ إِدْخَالِ الْمَشَقَّةِ عَلَيْهِمْ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Emphatic prohibition against stealing from the spoils of war (Ghulul)','باب غِلَظِ تَحْرِيمِ الْغُلُولِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of giving gifts to agents','باب تَحْرِيمِ هَدَايَا الْعُمَّالِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The obligation of obeying leaders in matters that do not involve sin, but it is forbidden to obey them in sinful matters','باب وُجُوبِ طَاعَةِ الأُمَرَاءِ فِي غَيْرِ مَعْصِيَةٍ وَتَحْرِيمِهَا فِي الْمَعْصِيَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The ruler is a shield from behind whom they fight and by whom they are protected','باب فِي الإِمَامِ إِذَا أَمَرَ بِتَقْوَى اللَّهِ وَعَدَلَ كَانَ لَهُ أَجْرٌ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The obligation of fulfilling oaths of allegiance is owed to the first of two Caliphs','باب الْوَفَاءِ بِبَيْعَةِ الْخُلَفَاءِ الأَوَّلِ فَالأَوَّلِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The command to be patient in the face of oppressive rulers and their selfishness','باب الأَمْرِ بِالصَّبْرِ عِنْدَ ظُلْمِ الْوُلاَةِ وَاسْتِئْثَارِهِمْ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Obeying Rulers even if they withhold the people''s rights','باب فِي طَاعَةِ الأُمَرَاءِ وَإِنْ مَنَعُوا الْحُقُوقَ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The obligation of staying with the Jama''ah (main body) of the muslims when Fitn (tribulations) appear, and in all circumstances. The prohibition of refusing to obey and on splitting away from the Jama''ah','باب الأَمْرِ بِلُزُومِ الْجَمَاعَةِ عِنْدَ ظُهُورِ الْفِتَنِ وَتَحْذِيرِ الدُّعَاةِ إِلَى الْكُفْرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The ruling on one who seeks to divide the muslims when they are united','باب حُكْمِ مَنْ فَرَّقَ أَمْرَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ وَهُوَ مُجْتَمِعٌ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'When allegiance has been sworn to two caliphs','باب إِذَا بُويِعَ لِخَلِيفَتَيْنِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The obligation to denounce rulers for that in which they go against Shari''ah, but they should not be fought so long as they pray regularly, etc','باب وُجُوبِ الإِنْكَارِ عَلَى الأُمَرَاءِ فِيمَا يُخَالِفُ الشَّرْعَ وَتَرْكِ قِتَالِهِمْ مَا صَلَّوْا وَنَحْوِ ذَلِكَ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The best and worst of rulers','باب خِيَارِ الأَئِمَّةِ وَشِرَارِهِمْ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended for the army to swear allegiance to the ruler when intending to fight, and an account of Bay''at Ar-Ridwan beneath the tree','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ مُبَايَعَةِ الإِمَامِ الْجَيْشَ عِنْدَ إِرَادَةِ الْقِتَالِ وَبَيَانِ بَيْعَةِ الرِّضْوَانِ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition against a Muhajir returning to settle in his former homeland','باب تَحْرِيمِ رُجُوعِ الْمُهَاجِرِ إِلَى اسْتِيطَانِ وَطَنِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Swearing Allegiance and Pledging to adhere to Islam, to engage in Jihad and to do Good, after the conquest of Makkah, and the meaning of the phrase: "There is No Hijrah (migration) after the Conquest."','باب الْمُبَايَعَةِ بَعْدَ فَتْحِ مَكَّةَ عَلَى الإِسْلاَمِ وَالْجِهَادِ وَالْخَيْرِ وَبَيَانِ مَعْنَى: «لاَ هِجْرَةَ بَعْدَ الْفَتْحِ»'),
('sahih-muslim',33,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'How women gave their oath of allegiance','باب كَيْفِيَّةِ بَيْعَةِ النِّسَاءِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Oath of allegiance pledging to hear and obey as much as possible','باب الْبَيْعَةِ عَلَى السَّمْعِ وَالطَّاعَةِ فِيمَا اسْتَطَاعَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The age of responsibility','باب بَيَانِ سِنِّ الْبُلُوغِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of travelling with the Mushaf to the land of the disbelievers if there is the fear that it may fall into their hands.','باب النَّهْىِ أَنْ يُسَافَرَ بِالْمُصْحَفِ إِلَى أَرْضِ الْكُفَّارِ إِذَا خِيفَ وُقُوعُهُ بِأَيْدِيهِمْ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Horse Races and Training Horses for Racing','باب الْمُسَابَقَةِ بَيْنَ الْخَيْلِ وَتَضْمِيرِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of horses; "Goodness is tied to their Forelocks."','باب الْخَيْلُ فِي نَوَاصِيهَا الْخَيْرُ إِلَى يَوْمِ الْقِيَامَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Disliked qualities in Horses','باب مَا يُكْرَهُ مِنْ صِفَاتِ الْخَيْلِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of Jihad and going out (to fight) in the cause of Allah','باب فَضْلِ الْجِهَادِ وَالْخُرُوجِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of Martyrdom in the cause of Allah','باب فَضْلِ الشَّهَادَةِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of going out in the morning or the evening in the cause of Allah','باب فَضْلِ الْغَدْوَةِ وَالرَّوْحَةِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The High Positions that Allah has prepared for the Mujahid in Paradise','باب بَيَانِ مَا أَعَدَّهُ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى لِلْمُجَاهِدِ فِي الْجَنَّةِ مِنَ الدَّرَجَاتِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If a person is killed in the cause of Allah, all his sins will be expiated except debt','باب مَنْ قُتِلَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ كُفِّرَتْ خَطَايَاهُ إِلاَّ الدَّيْنَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The souls of the martyrs are in Paradise, and they are alive with their Lord and they have provision','باب فِي بَيَانِ أَنَّ أَرْوَاحَ الشُّهَدَاءِ فِي الْجَنَّةِ وَأَنَّهُمْ أَحْيَاءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ يُرْزَقُونَ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of Jihad and keeping watch over the frontier','باب فَضْلِ الْجِهَادِ وَالرِّبَاطِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Two Men, one of whom kills the other, and both will enter Paradise','باب بَيَانِ الرَّجُلَيْنِ يَقْتُلُ أَحَدُهُمَا الآخَرَ يَدْخُلاَنِ الْجَنَّةَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One who kills a disbeliever then keeps to the right path','باب مَنْ قَتَلَ كَافِرًا ثُمَّ سَدَّدَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of Charity in the Cause of Allah, and its Manifold reward','باب فَضْلِ الصَّدَقَةِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ وَتَضْعِيفِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,38,'38',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of helping the warrior who is fighting in the cause of Allah with mounts etc., and looking after his family in his absence','باب فَضْلِ إِعَانَةِ الْغَازِي فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ بِمَرْكُوبٍ وَغَيْرِهِ وَخِلاَفَتِهِ فِي أَهْلِهِ بِخَيْرٍ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,39,'39',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The sanctity of the wives of the Mujahidin, and the sin of the one who betrays them with regard to them','باب حُرْمَةِ نِسَاءِ الْمُجَاهِدِينَ وَإِثْمِ مَنْ خَانَهُمْ فِيهِنَّ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,40,'40',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The duty of Jihad is waived for those who have excuses','باب سُقُوطِ فَرْضِ الْجِهَادِ عَنِ الْمَعْذُورِينَ، ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Affirmation of Paradise for the Martyr','باب ثُبُوتِ الْجَنَّةِ لِلشَّهِيدِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,42,'42',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One who fights so that the word of Allah will be supreme is fighting in the cause of Allah','باب مَنْ قَاتَلَ لِتَكُونَ كَلِمَةُ اللَّهِ هِيَ الْعُلْيَا فَهُوَ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,43,'43',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One who fights to show off and gain a reputation deserves Hell','باب مَنَ قَاتَلَ لِلرِّيَاءِ وَالسُّمْعَةِ اسْتَحَقَّ النَّارَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,44,'44',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The reward of those who fought and acquired spoils of war and those who did not acquire spoils of war','باب بَيَانِ قَدْرِ ثَوَابِ مَنْ غَزَا فَغَنِمَ وَمَنْ لَمْ يَغْنَمْ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,45,'45',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The words of the prophets saws: "Deeds are but with intentions" which includes fighting and other deeds','باب قَوْلِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏"‏ إِنَّمَا الأَعْمَالُ بِالنِّيَّةِ.‏"‏ وَأَنَّهُ يَدْخُلُ فِيهِ الْغَزْوُ وَغَيْرُهُ مِنَ الأَعْمَالِ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,46,'46',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to seek Martyrdom in the Cause of Allah, Exalted is He.','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ طَلَبِ الشَّهَادَةِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,47,'47',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Criticism of one who dies without having fought (in Jihad) or having thought of fighting','باب ذَمِّ مَنْ مَاتَ وَلَمْ يَغْزُ وَلَمْ يُحَدِّثْ نَفْسَهُ بِالْغَزْوِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,48,'48',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The reward of one who is kept from fighting by sickness or any other excuse','باب ثَوَابِ مَنْ حَبَسَهُ عَنِ الْغَزْوِ، مَرَضٌ أَوْ عُذْرٌ آخَرُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,49,'49',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of campaigning by sea','باب فَضْلِ الْغَزْوِ فِي الْبَحْرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,50,'50',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of guarding the frontier in the cause of Allah (Glorified and Exalted is He)','باب فَضْلِ الرِّبَاطِ فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,51,'51',NULL,NULL,NULL,'About the Martyrs','باب بَيَانِ الشُّهَدَاءِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,52,'52',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of Shooting and Encouragement to learn it, and criticism of the one who learns it and then forgets it','باب فَضْلِ الرَّمْىِ وَالْحَثِّ عَلَيْهِ وَذَمِّ مَنْ عَلِمَهُ ثُمَّ نَسِيَهُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,53,'53',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The words of the prophet saws: "A Group of my Ummah will continue to Prevail on the basis of the Truth, and They will not be Harmed by those who oppose them."','باب قَوْلِهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: «لاَ تَزَالُ طَائِفَةٌ مِنْ أُمَّتِي ظَاهِرِينَ عَلَى الْحَقِّ لاَ يَضُرُّهُمْ مَنْ خَالَفَهُمْ»'),
('sahih-muslim',33,54,'54',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Keeping animals'' well being in mind when traveling, and the prohibition of halting in the road at the end of the night.','باب مُرَاعَاةِ مَصْلَحَةِ الدَّوَابِّ فِي السَّيْرِ وَالنَّهْىِ عَنِ التَّعْرِيسِ فِي الطَّرِيقِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',33,55,'55',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Travel is a kind of torment, and it is recommended for the traveler to hasten back to his family after finishing his business','باب السَّفَرِ قِطْعَةٌ مِنَ الْعَذَابِ وَاسْتِحْبَابِ تَعْجِيلِ الْمُسَافِرِ إِلَى أَهْلِهِ بَعْدَ قَضَاءِ شُغْلِهِ'),
('sahih-muslim',33,56,'56',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is disliked to enter at night when coming home from a journey','باب كَرَاهَةِ الطُّرُوقِ وَهُوَ الدُّخُولُ لَيْلاً لِمَنْ وَرَدَ مِنْ سَفَرٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Hunting with trained dogs and arrows','باب الصَّيْدِ بِالْكِلاَبِ الْمُعَلَّمَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If the game disappears, then is found afterwards','باب إِذَا غَابَ عَنْهُ الصَّيْدُ ثُمَّ وَجَدَهُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of eating any wild animal with Fangs and any bird with Talons','باب تَحْرِيمِ أَكْلِ كُلِّ ذِي نَابٍ مِنَ السِّبَاعِ وَكُلِّ ذِي مِخْلَبٍ مِنَ الطَّيْرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Permissibility of dead animals from the sea','باب إِبَاحَةِ مَيْتَاتِ الْبَحْرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of eating the meat of domesticated donkeys','باب تَحْرِيمِ أَكْلِ لَحْمِ الْحُمُرِ الإِنْسِيَّةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The permissibility of eating horse meat','باب فِي أَكْلِ لُحُومِ الْخَيْلِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The permissibility of eating the Dabb (mastigure)','باب إِبَاحَةِ الضَّبِّ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The permissibility of eating Locusts','باب إِبَاحَةِ الْجَرَادِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The permissibility of eating Rabbit','باب إِبَاحَةِ الأَرْنَبِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The permissibility of using things that help in hunting and pursuing the enemy, but throwing small pebbles is disliked','باب إِبَاحَةِ مَا يُسْتَعَانُ بِهِ عَلَى الاِصْطِيَادِ وَالْعَدُوِّ وَكَرَاهَةِ الْخَذْفِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The command to be proficient in slaughtering and killing, and to sharpen the blade','باب الأَمْرِ بِإِحْسَانِ الذَّبْحِ وَالْقَتْلِ وَتَحْدِيدِ الشَّفْرَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',34,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of cornering animals in order to kill them (for sport)','باب النَّهْىِ عَنْ صَبْرِ الْبَهَائِمِ، ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',35,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The time for sacrifice','باب وَقْتِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',35,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The age of sacrificial animals','باب سِنِّ الأُضْحِيَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',35,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to select a good animal for the sacrifice and to slaughter it oneself, not delegating it to anyone else, and to say the name of Allah, and to say the Takbir','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ الضَّحِيَّةِ وَذَبْحِهَا مُبَاشَرَةً بِلاَ تَوْكِيلٍ وَالتَّسْمِيَةِ وَالتَّكْبِيرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',35,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The permissibility of slaughtering with anything that makes the blood flow, except teeth and other bones','باب جَوَازِ الذَّبْحِ بِكُلِّ مَا أَنْهَرَ الدَّمَ إِلاَّ السِّنَّ وَالظُّفُرَ وَسَائِرَ الْعِظَامِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',35,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of eating sacrificial meat for more than three days, which applied at the beginning of Islam but was then abrogated, and now it is permissible to eat it as long as one wants.','باب بَيَانِ مَا كَانَ مِنَ النَّهْىِ عَنْ أَكْلِ لُحُومِ الأَضَاحِيِّ بَعْدَ ثَلاَثٍ فِي أَوَّلِ الإِسْلاَمِ وَبَيَانِ نَسْخِهِ وَإِبَاحَتِهِ إِلَى مَتَى شَاءَ'),
('sahih-muslim',35,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Fara'' and ''Atirah','باب الْفَرَعِ وَالْعَتِيرَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',35,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'When the first ten days of Dhul-Hijjah begin, it is forbidden for the one who wants to offer a sacrifice to remove anything from his hair, nails or skin','باب نَهْيِ مَنْ دَخَلَ عَلَيْهِ عَشْرُ ذِي الْحِجَّةِ وَهُوَ مُرِيدُ التَّضْحِيَةِ أَنْ يَأْخُذَ مِنْ شَعْرِهِ أَوْ أَظْفَارِهِ شَيْئًا'),
('sahih-muslim',35,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of slaughtering a sacrifice for anything other than Allah, and the one who does that is cursed','باب تَحْرِيمِ الذَّبْحِ لِغَيْرِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى وَلَعْنِ فَاعِلِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of Khamr, which may be made from the juice of grapes, dried dates, unripe dates, raisins and other things that intoxicate','باب تَحْرِيمِ الْخَمْرِ وَبَيَانِ أَنَّهَا تَكُونُ مِنْ عَصِيرِ الْعِنَبِ وَمِنَ التَّمْرِ وَالْبُسْرِ وَالزَّبِيبِ وَغَيْرِهَا مِمَّا يُسْكِرُ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of making vinegar from wine','باب تَحْرِيمِ تَخْلِيلِ الْخَمْرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of using Khamr as a remedy; It is not a remedy','باب تَحْرِيمِ التَّدَاوِي بِالْخَمْرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Everything that is taken from the date palm or grape vine and steeped is called Khamr','باب بَيَانِ أَنَّ جَمِيعَ مَا يُنْبَذُ مِمَّا يُتَّخَذُ مِنَ النَّخْلِ وَالْعِنَبِ يُسَمَّى خَمْرًا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is disliked to make Nabidh by mixing dried dates and raisins','باب كَرَاهَةِ انْتِبَاذِ التَّمْرِ وَالزَّبِيبِ مَخْلُوطَيْنِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of making Nabidh in Al-Muzaffat, Ad-Dubba'' (Gourds), Al-Hantam and An-Naqir; This has been abrogated and now it is permitted, so long as it does not become intoxicating','باب النَّهْيِ عَنْ الاِنْتِبَاذِ فِي الْمُزَفَّتِ وَالدُّبَّاءِ وَالْحَنْتَمِ وَالنَّقِيرِ وَبَيَانِ أَنَّهُ مَنْسُوخٌ وَأَنَّهُ الْيَوْمَ حَلاَلٌ مَا لَمْ يَصِرْ مُسْكِرًا'),
('sahih-muslim',36,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Every intoxicant is Khamr and all Khamr is Haram','باب بَيَانِ أَنَّ كُلَّ مُسْكِرٍ خَمْرٌ وَأَنَّ كُلَّ خَمْرٍ حَرَامٌ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The punishment of one who drinks Khamr if he does not repent from it: he will be denied it in the hereafter','باب عُقُوبَةِ مَنْ شَرِبَ الْخَمْرَ إِذَا لَمْ يَتُبْ مِنْهَا بِمَنْعِهِ إِيَّاهَا فِي الآخِرَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The permissibility of Nabidh so long as it has not become strong and has not become intoxicating','باب إِبَاحَةِ النَّبِيذِ الَّذِي لَمْ يَشْتَدَّ وَلَمْ يَصِرْ مُسْكِرًا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The permissibility of drinking milk','باب جَوَازِ شُرْبِ اللَّبَنِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Drinking Nabidh and covering vessels','باب فِي شُرْبِ النَّبِيذِ وَتَخْمِيرِ الإِنَاءِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to cover vessels, tie up waterskins, close doors and mention the name of Allah over them, extinguish lamps and fires when going to sleep, and keep children and animals in after maghrib','باب الأَمْرِ بِتَغْطِيَةِ الإِنَاءِ وَإِيكَاءِ السِّقَاءِ وَإِغْلاَقِ الأَبْوَابِ وَذِكْرِ اسْمِ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهَا وَإِطْفَاءِ السِّرَاجِ وَالنَّارِ عِنْدَ النَّوْمِ وَكَفِّ الصِّبْيَانِ وَالْمَوَاشِي بَعْدَ الْمَغْرِبِ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The etiquette of eating and drinking, and rulings thereon','باب آدَابِ الطَّعَامِ وَالشَّرَابِ وَأَحْكَامِهِمَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Drinking while standing','باب كَرَاهِيَةِ الشُّرْبِ قَائِمًا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Drinking zamzam water while standing','باب فِي الشُّرْبِ مِنْ زَمْزَمَ قَائِمًا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is disliked to breathe into the vessel, and it is recommended to take three breaths, outside the vessel','باب كَرَاهَةِ التَّنَفُّسِ فِي نَفْسِ الإِنَاءِ وَاسْتِحْبَابِ التَّنَفُّسِ ثَلاَثًا خَارِجَ الإِنَاءِ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to pass water and milk etc., to the right of the one who drinks first','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ إِدَارَةِ الْمَاءِ وَاللَّبَنِ وَنَحْوِهِمَا عَنْ يَمِينِ الْمُبْتَدِئِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to lick one''s fingers and wipe the bowl, and to eat a piece of food that is dropped after removing any dirt on it. It is disliked to wipe one''s hand before licking it, because of the possibility that the blessing of the food may be in that remaining part. The Sunnah is to eat with three fingers','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ لَعْقِ الأَصَابِعِ وَالْقَصْعَةِ وَأَكْلِ اللُّقْمَةِ السَّاقِطَةِ بَعْدَ مَسْحِ مَا يُصِيبُهَا مِنْ أَذًى وَكَرَاهَةِ مَسْحِ الْيَدِ قَبْلَ لَعْقِهَا'),
('sahih-muslim',36,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'What the guest should do if he is accompanied by someone who was not invited by the host; it is recommended for the host to give permission to the one who has accompanied the guest','باب مَا يَفْعَلُ الضَّيْفُ إِذَا تَبِعَهُ غَيْرُ مَنْ دَعَاهُ صَاحِبُ الطَّعَامِ وَاسْتِحْبَابُ إِذْنِ صَاحِبِ الطَّعَامِ لِلتَّابِعِ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to take someone else to the house of one who you are certain will approve of that and will not mind. It is recommended to gather to eat','باب جَوَازِ اسْتِتْبَاعِهِ غَيْرَهُ إِلَى دَارِ مَنْ يَثِقُ بِرِضَاهُ بِذَلِكَ وَيَتَحَقَّقُهُ تَحَقُّقًا تَامًّا وَاسْتِحْبَابِ الاِجْتِمَاعِ عَلَى الطَّعَامِ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to eat soup, and it is recommended to eat squash, And for the people eating together to show preference to one another even if they are guests, so long as the host does not object to that','باب جَوَازِ أَكْلِ الْمَرَقِ وَاسْتِحْبَابِ أَكْلِ الْيَقْطِينِ وَإِيثَارِ أَهْلِ الْمَائِدَةِ بَعْضِهِمْ بَعْضًا وَإِنْ كَانُوا ضِيفَانًا إِذَا لَمْ يَكْرَهْ ذَلِكَ صَاحِبُ الطَّعَامِ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to take the stones out of dates, and it is recommended for the guest to pray for the host and to ask a righteous guest to supplicate, and he should respond to that request','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ وَضْعِ النَّوَى خَارِجَ التَّمْرِ وَاسْتِحْبَابِ دُعَاءِ الضَّيْفِ لأَهْلِ الطَّعَامِ وَطَلَبِ الدُّعَاءِ مِنَ الضَّيْفِ الصَّالِحِ وَإِجَابَتِهِ لِذَلِكَ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Eating cucumbers with fresh dates','باب أَكْلِ الْقِثَّاءِ بِالرُّطَبِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is recommended to be humble when eating, and how to sit','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ تَوَاضُعِ الآكِلِ وَصِفَةِ قُعُودِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The prohibition of eating two dates etc., at a time when eating with a group, except with the permission of one''s companions','باب نَهْيِ الآكِلِ مَعَ جَمَاعَةٍ عَنْ قِرَانِ تَمْرَتَيْنِ وَنَحْوِهِمَا فِي لُقْمَةٍ إِلاَّ بِإِذْنِ أَصْحَابِهِ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Storing dates and other provisions for one''s children','باب فِي ادْخَالِ التَّمْرِ وَنَحْوِهِ مِنَ الأَقْوَاتِ لِلْعِيَالِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of the dates of Al-Madinah','باب فَضْلِ تَمْرِ الْمَدِينَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of truffles, and treating the eyes with them','باب فَضْلِ الْكَمْأَةِ وَمُدَاوَاةِ الْعَيْنِ بِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of the black fruit from the Arak tree','باب فَضِيلَةِ الأَسْوَدِ مِنَ الْكَبَاثِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of vinegar and using it as a condiment','باب فَضِيلَةِ الْخَلِّ وَالتَّأَدُّمِ بِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It is permissible to eat garlic, but the one who is going to address prominent people should refrain from eating it, and the same applies to other, similar foods','باب إِبَاحَةِ أَكْلِ الثُّومِ وَأَنَّهُ يَنْبَغِي لِمَنْ أَرَادَ خِطَابِ الْكِبَارِ تَرْكُهُ وَكَذَا مَا فِي مَعْنَاهُ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Honoring guests and the virtue of showing preference to one''s guest','باب إِكْرَامِ الضَّيْفِ وَفَضْلِ إِيثَارِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The virtue of sharing a small amount of food, and the food of two is sufficient for three, and so on.','باب فَضِيلَةِ الْمُوَاسَاةِ فِي الطَّعَامِ الْقَلِيلِ وَأَنَّ طَعَامَ الاِثْنَيْنِ يَكْفِي الثَّلاَثَةَ وَنَحْوِ ذَلِكَ'),
('sahih-muslim',36,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The believer eats in one intestine and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines.','باب الْمُؤْمِنُ يَأْكُلُ فِي مِعًى وَاحِدٍ وَالْكَافِرُ يَأْكُلُ فِي سَبْعَةِ أَمْعَاءٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',36,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Do not criticize food','باب لاَ يَعِيبُ الطَّعَامَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Using Vessels Of Gold And Silver For Drinking Etc., For Men And Women','باب تَحْرِيمِ أَوَانِي الذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ فِي الشُّرْبِ وَغَيْرِهِ عَلَى الرِّجَالِ وَالنِّسَاءِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Using Vessels Of Gold And Silver For Men And Women, And Gold Rings And Silk For Men, But They Are Permissible For Women. Permissibility Of Silken Borders On Garments For Men, But It Should Not Be More Than Four Fingers Wide','باب تَحْرِيمِ اسْتِعْمَالِ إِنَاءِ الذَّهَبِ وَالْفِضَّةِ عَلَى الرِّجَالِ وَالنِّسَاءِ وَخَاتَمِ الذَّهَبِ وَالْحَرِيرِ عَلَى الرَّجُلِ وَإِبَاحَتِهِ لِلنِّسَاءِ وَإِبَاحَةِ الْعَلَمِ وَنَحْوِهِ لِلرَّجُلِ مَا لَمْ يَزِدْ عَلَى أَرْبَعِ أَصَابِعَ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Permissibility Of Wearing Silk For Men, If A Man Has A Skin Disease Or Similar Problem','باب إِبَاحَةِ لُبْسِ الْحَرِيرِ لِلرَّجُلِ إِذَا كَانَ بِهِ حِكَّةٌ أَوْ نَحْوُهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of A Man Wearing A Garment Dyed With Safflower','باب النَّهْىِ عَنْ لُبْسِ الرَّجُلِ الثَّوْبَ الْمُعَصْفَرَ، ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Virtue Of Wearing The Hibarah','باب فَضْلِ لِبَاسِ ثِيَابِ الْحِبَرَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Humility In Dress And Sticking To Coarse And Simple Clothes, Furnishings Etc., Permissibility Of Wearing Clothes Made From Camel Hair And Those On Which There Are Markings','بَاب التَّوَاضُعِ فِي اللِّبَاسِ وَالِاقْتِصَارِ عَلَى الْغَلِيظِ مِنْهُ وَالْيَسِيرِ فِي اللِّبَاسِ وَالْفِرَاشِ وَغَيْرِهِمَا'),
('sahih-muslim',37,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Permissibility Of Using Blankets','باب جَوَازِ اتِّخَاذِ الأَنْمَاطِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Disliked To Have More Furniture And Bedding Than One Needs','باب كَرَاهَةِ مَا زَادَ عَلَى الْحَاجَةِ مِنَ الْفِرَاشِ وَاللِّبَاسِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Letting One''s Garment Drag Out Of Pride, And The Extent To Which It Is Permissible To Let It Hang Down And The Extent To Which It Is Recommended','باب تَحْرِيمِ جَرِّ الثَّوْبِ خُيَلاَءَ وَبَيَانِ حَدِّ مَا يَجُوزُ إِرْخَاؤُهُ إِلَيْهِ وَمَا يُسْتَحَبّ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Against Strutting With Pride, And Being Amazed With One''s Clothes','باب تَحْرِيمِ التَّبَخْتُرِ فِي الْمَشْىِ مَعَ إِعْجَابِهِ بِثِيَابِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Gold Rings For Men, And Abrogation Of Their Allowance After The Beginning Of Islam','بَاب تَحْرِيمِ خَاتَمِ الذَّهَبِ عَلَى الرِّجَالِ وَنَسْخِ مَا كَانَ مِنْ إِبَاحَتِهِ فِي أَوَّلِ الْإِسْلَامِ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prophet (SAW) Wore A Ring Of Silver On Which Was Inscribed The Words Muhammad Rasul Allah (Muhammad the Messenger of Allah), And The Caliphs Wore It After He Died','بَاب لُبْسِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ خَاتَمًا مِنْ وَرِقٍ نَقْشُهُ مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ وَلُبْسِ الْخُلَفَاءِ لَهُ مِنْ بَعْدِهِ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prophet (SAW) Acquired A Ring When He Wanted To Send Letters To The Non-Arabs','باب فِي اتِّخَاذِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم خَاتَمًا لَمَّا أَرَادَ أَنْ يَكْتُبَ إِلَى الْعَجَمِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Discarding Rings','باب فِي طَرْحِ الْخَوَاتِمِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Silver Ring With An Abyssinian Stone','باب فِي خَاتَمِ الْوَرِقِ فَصُّهُ حَبَشِيٌّ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Wearing Rings On The Little Finger','باب فِي لُبْسِ الْخَاتَمِ فِي الْخِنْصَرِ مِنَ الْيَدِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Wearing Rings On The Middle Finger And The One That Is Next To It','باب النَّهْىِ عَنِ التَّخَتُّمِ، فِي الْوُسْطَى وَالَّتِي تَلِيهَا ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Wear Sandals et','بَاب اسْتِحْبَابِ لُبْسِ النِّعَالِ وَمَا فِي مَعْنَاهَا'),
('sahih-muslim',37,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Put Shoes On The Right Foot First, And To Take Them Off From The Left Foot First, And It Is Disliked To Walk In One Shoe','بَاب اسْتِحْبَابِ لُبْسِ النَّعْلِ فِي الْيُمْنَى أَوَّلًا وَالْخَلْعِ مِنْ الْيُسْرَى أَوَّلًا وَكَرَاهَةِ الْمَشْيِ فِي نَعْلٍ وَاحِدَةٍ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Ishtimal As-Samma'' (Wrapping Oneself Up Entirely In One''s Garment With No Room For The Arms To Emerge), And Al-Ihtiba'' (Wrapping Oneself Up) In A Single Garment With The Legs Drawn Up To The Belly Exposing Part Of The ''Awrah','باب النَّهْىِ عَنِ اشْتِمَالِ الصَّمَّاءِ، وَالاِحْتِبَاءِ، فِي ثَوْبٍ وَاحِدٍ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Ruling On Lying On Ones Back With One Leg On Top Of The Other','باب فِي مَنْعِ الاِسْتِلْقَاءِ عَلَى الظَّهْرِ وَوَضْعِ إِحْدَى الرِّجْلَيْنِ عَلَى الأُخْرَى ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Permissibility Of Lying Down And Placing One Leg On Top Of The Other','باب فِي إِبَاحَةِ الاِسْتِلْقَاءِ وَوَضْعِ إِحْدَى الرِّجْلَيْنِ عَلَى الأُخْرَى ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of A Man Dyeing From With Saffron','بَاب نَهْيِ الرَّجُلِ عَنْ التَّزَعْفُرِ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Dye White Hair With Yellow Or Red Dye, But Black Dye Is Haram','بَاب اسْتِحْبَابِ خِضَابِ الشَّيْبِ بِصُفْرَةٍ أَوْ حُمْرَةٍ وَتَحْرِيمِهِ بِالسَّوَادِ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Differing From The Jews With Regard To Dyeing','باب فِي مُخَالَفَةِ الْيَهُودِ فِي الصَّبْغِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Making Images Of Living Beings, And The Prohibition Of Using Images That Are Not Subjected To Disrespect In Furnishings And The Like; The Angels (Peace Be Upon Them) Do Not Enter A House In Which There Is An Image Or A Dog','بَاب تَحْرِيمِ تَصْوِيرِ صُورَةِ الْحَيَوَانِ وَتَحْرِيمِ اتِّخَاذِ مَا فِيهِ صُورَةٌ غَيْرُ مُمْتَهَنَةٍ بِالْفَرْشِ وَنَحْوِهِ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Disliked To Take Dogs And Bells On A Journey','باب كَرَاهَةِ الْكَلْبِ وَالْجَرَسِ فِي السَّفَرِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Disliked To Hang Garlands On The Necks Of Camels','باب كَرَاهَةِ قِلاَدَةِ الْوَتَرِ فِي رَقَبَةِ الْبَعِيرِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Striking Or Branding Animals On The Face','باب النَّهْىِ عَنْ ضَرْبِ الْحَيَوَانِ، فِي وَجْهِهِ وَوَسْمِهِ فِيهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Permissibility Of Branding Animals Anywhere But On The Face, And This Is Recommended In The Case Of Animals Given As Zakat Ot Jizyah','بَاب جَوَازِ وَسْمِ الْحَيَوَانِ غَيْرِ الْآدَمِيِّ فِي غَيْرِ الْوَجْهِ وَنَدْبِهِ فِي نَعَمْ الزَّكَاةِ وَالْجِزْيَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Disliked To Shave Part Of The Head And Leave Part','باب كَرَاهَةِ الْقَزَعِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Sitting In The Street; And Giving The Street Its Rights','باب النَّهْىِ عَنِ الْجُلُوسِ، فِي الطُّرُقَاتِ وَإِعْطَاءِ الطَّرِيقِ حَقَّهُ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Adding Hair Extensions, Having Them Added, Tattooing, Being Tattooed, An-Namisah, Al-Mutanamisah, Separating Teeth, And Changing The Creation Of Allah','بَاب تَحْرِيمِ فِعْلِ الْوَاصِلَةِ وَالْمُسْتَوْصِلَةِ وَالْوَاشِمَةِ وَالْمُسْتَوْشِمَةِ وَالنَّامِصَةِ وَالْمُتَنَمِّصَةِ وَالْمُتَفَلِّجَاتِ وَالْمُغَيِّرَاتِ خَلْقِ اللَّهِ'),
('sahih-muslim',37,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Women Who Are Clothed Yet Naked, Turning Away From Righteousness And Leading Others Astray','باب النِّسَاءِ الْكَاسِيَاتِ الْعَارِيَاتِ الْمَائِلاَتِ الْمُمِيلاَتِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',37,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Wearing A Garment Of Falsehood Etc., And Pretending To Have That Which Has Not Been Given To One','باب النَّهْىِ عَنِ التَّزْوِيرِ، فِي اللِّبَاسِ وَغَيْرِهِ وَالتَّشَبُّعِ بِمَا لَمْ يُعْطَ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',38,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Taking The Kunyah Abul-Qasim, And The Names Which Are Recommended','باب النَّهْىِ عَنِ التَّكَنِّي، بِأَبِي الْقَاسِمِ وَبَيَانِ مَا يُسْتَحَبُّ مِنَ الأَسْمَاءِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',38,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Disliked To Use Objectionable Names And Names Such As Nafi'' (Beneficial) Etc','باب كَرَاهَةِ التَّسْمِيَةِ بِالأَسْمَاءِ الْقَبِيحَةِ وَبِنَافِعٍ وَنَحْوِهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',38,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Change Bad Names To Good Names, And To Change The Name Barrah To Zainab, Juwayriyah And The Like','بَاب اسْتِحْبَابِ تَغْيِيرِ الِاسْمِ الْقَبِيحِ إِلَى حَسَنٍ وَتَغْيِيرِ اسْمِ بَرَّةَ إِلَى زَيْنَبَ وَجُوَيْرِيَةَ وَنَحْوِهِمَا'),
('sahih-muslim',38,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of The Names Malik Al-Amlak Or Malik Al-Muluk "King Of Kings"','باب تَحْرِيمِ التَّسَمِّي بِمَلِكِ الأَمْلاَكِ وَبِمَلِكِ الْمُلُوكِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',38,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Perform Tahnik For The Newborn When He Is Born And To Take Him To A Righteous Man To Perform Tahnik For Him; It Is Permissible To Name Him On The Day He Is Born, And It Is Recommended To Use The Names ''Abdullah, Ibrahim, And The Names Of All Other Prophets, Peace Be Upon Them','بَاب اسْتِحْبَابِ تَحْنِيكِ الْمَوْلُودِ عِنْدَ وِلَادَتِهِ وَحَمْلِهِ إِلَى صَالِحٍ يُحَنِّكُهُ وَجَوَازِ تَسْمِيَتِهِ يَوْمَ وِلَادَتِهِ وَاسْتِحْبَابِ التَّسْمِيَةِ بِعَبْدِ اللَّهِ وَإِبْرَاهِيمَ وَسَائِرِ أَسْمَاءِ الْأَنْبِيَاءِ عَلَيْهِمْ السَّلَام'),
('sahih-muslim',38,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Permissible To Say: "O My Son" To Someone Other Than One''s Son, And It Is Recommended To Speak Kindly','باب جَوَازِ قَوْلِهِ لِغَيْرِ ابْنِهِ يَا بُنَىَّ وَاسْتِحْبَابِهِ لِلْمُلاَطَفَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',38,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Seeking Permission To Enter A House','باب الاِسْتِئْذَانِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',38,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Disliked For The Person Who Is Seeking Permission To Say "Me" When Asked "Who Is It?"','باب كَرَاهَةِ قَوْلِ الْمُسْتَأْذِنِ أَنَا ‏إِذَا قِيلَ مَنْ هَذَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',38,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Looking Into A House','باب تَحْرِيمِ النَّظَرِ فِي بَيْتِ غَيْرِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',38,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'An Accidental Glance','باب نَظَرِ الْفَجْأَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The One Who Is Riding Should Greet The One Who Is Walking, And The Smaller Group Should Greet The Larger Group','باب يُسَلِّمُ الرَّاكِبُ عَلَى الْمَاشِي وَالْقَلِيلُ عَلَى الْكَثِيرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One Of The Duties Of Sitting In The Street Is To Return Salam','باب مِنْ حَقِّ الْجُلُوسِ عَلَى الطَّرِيقِ رَدُّ السَّلاَمِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'One Of The Rights Of One Muslim Over Another Is (The Greeting Of) Salam','باب مِنْ حَقِّ الْمُسْلِمِ لِلْمُسْلِمِ رَدُّ السَّلاَمِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Initiating The Greeting With The People Of The Book, And How To Respond To Them','باب النَّهْىِ عَنِ ابْتِدَاءِ، أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ بِالسَّلاَمِ وَكَيْفَ يَرُدُّ عَلَيْهِمْ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Greet Children With Salam','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ السَّلاَمِ عَلَى الصِّبْيَانِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Permissible To Give Permission To Enter By Raising The Curtain Or Giving Some Other Sign','باب جَوَازِ جَعْلِ الإِذْنِ رَفْعَ حِجَابٍ أَوْ نَحْوَهُ مِنَ الْعَلاَمَاتِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Permissibility Of Women Going Out To Relieve Themselves','باب إِبَاحَةُ الْخُرُوجِ لِلنِّسَاءِ لِقَضَاءِ حَاجَةِ الإِنْسَانِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Being Alone With A Non-Mahram Woman Or Entering Upon Her','باب تَحْرِيمِ الْخَلْوَةِ بِالأَجْنَبِيَّةِ وَالدُّخُولِ عَلَيْهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended For The One Who Is Seen Alone With A Woman Who Is His Wife Or Mahram, To Say; "This Is So-And-So,'' To Ward off Suspicion','باب بَيَانِ أَنَّهُ يُسْتَحَبُّ لِمَنْ رُئِيَ خَالِيًا بِامْرَأَةٍ وَكَانَتْ زَوْجَةً أَوْ مَحْرَمًا لَهُ'),
('sahih-muslim',39,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If A Man Comes To A Gathering And Finds A Space. Let Him Sit There, Otherwise Let Him Sit Behind Them','باب مَنْ أَتَى مَجْلِسًا فَوَجَدَ فُرْجَةً فَجَلَسَ فِيهَا وَإِلاَّ وَرَاءَهُمْ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Making A Man Get Up From A Place That He Reached First','باب تَحْرِيمِ إِقَامَةِ الإِنْسَانِ مِنْ مَوْضِعِهِ الْمُبَاحِ الَّذِي سَبَقَ إِلَيْهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'If A Man Gets Up From His Spot Then Comes Back To It, He Has More Right To It','باب إِذَا قَامَ مِنْ مَجْلِسِهِ ثُمَّ عَادَ فَهُوَ أَحَقُّ بِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Forbidding A Hermaphrodite From Entering Upon Non-Mahram Women','باب مَنْعِ الْمُخَنَّثِ مِنَ الدُّخُولِ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ الأَجَانِبِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Permissible To Seat A Non-Mahram Woman Behind One (On A Mount) If She Is Exhausted On The Road','باب جَوَازِ إِرْدَافِ الْمَرْأَةِ الأَجْنَبِيَّةِ إِذَا أَعْيَتْ فِي الطَّرِيقِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Two People Conversing Privately To The Exclusion Of A Third Without His Consent','باب تَحْرِيمِ مُنَاجَاةِ الاِثْنَيْنِ دُونَ الثَّالِثِ بِغَيْرِ رِضَاهُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Medicine, Sickness And Ruqyah','باب الطِّبِّ وَالْمَرَضِ وَالرُّقَى ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Witchcraft','باب السِّحْرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Poison','باب السَّمِّ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Recite Ruqyah For One Who Is Sick','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ رُقْيَةِ الْمَرِيضِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Reciting Al-Mu''awwidhat As Ruqyah For The Sick, And Blowing Over Them','باب رُقْيَةِ الْمَرِيضِ بِالْمُعَوِّذَاتِ وَالنَّفْثِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Recite Ruqyah For The Evil Eye, Pustules, And Stings','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ الرُّقْيَةِ مِنَ الْعَيْنِ وَالنَّمْلَةِ وَالْحُمَةِ وَالنَّظْرَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'There Is Nothing Wrong With Ruqyah That Does Not Involve Shirk','باب لاَ بَأْسَ بِالرُّقَى مَا لَمْ يَكُنْ فِيهِ شِرْكٌ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Permissibility Of Accepting A Reward For Reciting Ruqyah With Qur''an And Supplications','باب جَوَازِ أَخْذِ الأُجْرَةِ عَلَى الرُّقْيَةِ بِالْقُرْآنِ وَالأَذْكَارِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Put Ones Hand On The Site Of The Pain When Supplicating','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ وَضْعِ يَدِهِ عَلَى مَوْضِعِ الأَلَمِ مَعَ الدُّعَاءِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Seeking Refuge With Allah From The Devil Who Whispers During Prayer','باب التَّعَوُّذِ مِنْ شَيْطَانِ الْوَسْوَسَةِ فِي الصَّلاَةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'For Every Disease There Is A Remedy, And It Is Recommended To Treat Disease','باب لِكُلِّ دَاءٍ دَوَاءٌ وَاسْتِحْبَابُ التَّدَاوِي ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Disliked To Administer Medicine In The Side Of The Mouth Forcibly','باب كَرَاهَةِ التَّدَاوِي بِاللَّدُودِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Treatment With Indian Aloeswood, Which Is Costmary','باب التَّدَاوِي بِالْعُودِ الْهِنْدِيِّ وَهُوَ الْكُسْتُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Healing Sickness With The Black Seed','باب التَّدَاوِي بِالْحَبَّةِ السَّوْدَاءِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Talbinah Gives Comfort To The Sick Person','باب التَّلْبِينَةُ مَجَمَّةٌ لِفُؤَادِ الْمَرِيضِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Treating Sickness With A Drink Of Honey','باب التَّدَاوِي بِسَقْىِ الْعَسَلِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Plague, Ill Omens, Soothsaying And The Like','باب الطَّاعُونِ وَالطِّيَرَةِ وَالْكَهَانَةِ وَنَحْوِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'There Is No ''Adwa, No Tiyarah (Evil Omens), No Hamah. No Safar, No Nawa'', And No Ghoul, And No Sick Camel Should Be Brought To A Healthy Camel','باب لاَ عَدْوَى وَلاَ طِيَرَةَ وَلاَ هَامَةَ وَلاَ صَفَرَ'),
('sahih-muslim',39,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'(Evil) Omens And Al-Fa''l, And That Which May Be Regarded As Inauspicious','باب الطِّيَرَةِ وَالْفَأْلِ وَمَا يَكُونُ فِيهِ الشُّؤْمُ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Soothsaying And Going To Soothsayers','باب تَحْرِيمِ الْكِهَانَةِ وَإِتْيَانِ الْكُهَّانِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Avoiding Lepers Etc.','باب اجْتِنَابِ الْمَجْذُومِ وَنَحْوِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Killing Snakes Etc.','باب قَتْلِ الْحَيَّاتِ وَغَيْرِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,38,'38',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Recommended To Kill Geckos','باب اسْتِحْبَابِ قَتْلِ الْوَزَغِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,39,'39',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Killing Ants','باب النَّهْىِ عَنْ قَتْلِ النَّمْلِ، ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,40,'40',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Killing Cats','باب تَحْرِيمِ قَتْلِ الْهِرَّةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',39,41,'41',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Virtue Of Giving Food And Water To Animals Which Are Unlawful To Eat','باب فَضْلِ سَاقِي الْبَهَائِمِ الْمُحْتَرَمَةِ وَإِطْعَامِهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',40,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Cursing Time','باب النَّهْىِ عَنْ سَبِّ الدَّهْرِ، ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',40,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Disliked To Call Grapes Karm','باب كَرَاهَةِ تَسْمِيَةِ الْعِنَبِ كَرْمًا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',40,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Ruling On Using The Words ''Abd And Amah (For Slaves) And Mawla And Sayyid (For Masters)','باب حُكْمِ إِطْلاَقِ لَفْظَةِ الْعَبْدِ وَالأَمَةِ وَالْمَوْلَى وَالسَّيِّدِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',40,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'It Is Disliked For A Man To Say: "Khabuthat Nafsi" (I Feel Bad)','باب كَرَاهَةِ قَوْلِ الإِنْسَانِ خَبُثَتْ نَفْسِي ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',40,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Using Musk, Which Is The Best Of Perfume. It Is Disliked To Refuse A Gift Of Scent Or Perfume','باب اسْتِعْمَالِ الْمِسْكِ وَأَنَّهُ أَطْيَبُ الطِّيبِ وَكَرَاهَةِ رَدِّ الرَّيْحَانِ وَالطِّيبِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',41,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'باب ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',41,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prohibition Of Playing Nardashir','باب تَحْرِيمِ اللَّعِبِ بِالنَّرْدَشِيرِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',42,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Words Of The Prophet (SAW): "Whoever Sees Me In A Dream Has Indeed Seen Me."','باب قَوْلِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏"‏ مَنْ رَآنِي فِي الْمَنَامِ فَقَدْ رَآنِي ‏"‏ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',42,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'No One Should Speak Of How The Shaitan Toyed With Him In His Sleep','باب لاَ يُخْبِرُ بِتَلَعُّبِ الشَّيْطَانِ بِهِ فِي الْمَنَامِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',42,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Interpretation Of Dreams','باب فِي تَأْوِيلِ الرُّؤْيَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',42,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Dreams Of The Prophet (SAW)','باب رُؤْيَا النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,1,'1',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Superiority Of The Prophet''s Lineage, And The Stone That Greeted Him Before His Prophethood','باب فَضْلِ نَسَبِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَتَسْلِيمِ الْحَجَرِ عَلَيْهِ قَبْلَ النُّبُوَّةِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,2,'2',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Superiority Of Our Prophet (SAW) Over All Of Creation','باب تَفْضِيلِ نَبِيِّنَا صلى الله عليه وسلم عَلَى جَمِيعِ الْخَلاَئِقِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,3,'3',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Miracles Of The Prophet (SAW)','باب فِي مُعْجِزَاتِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,4,'4',NULL,NULL,NULL,'He Put His Trust In Allah And Allah Protected Him From The People','باب تَوَكُّلِهِ عَلَى اللَّهِ وَعِصْمَةِ اللَّهِ تَعَالَى لَهُ مِنَ النَّاسِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,5,'5',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Likeness Of The Guidance And Knowledge With Which The Prophet (SAW) Was Sent','باب بَيَانِ مَثَلِ مَا بُعِثَ بِهِ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم مِنَ الْهُدَى وَالْعِلْمِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,6,'6',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Compassion Towards His Ummah, And His Intense Concern To Warn Them Against That Which May Harm Them','باب شَفَقَتِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم عَلَى أُمَّتِهِ وَمُبَالَغَتِهِ فِي تَحْذِيرِهِمْ مِمَّا يَضُرُّهُمْ ‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,7,'7',NULL,NULL,NULL,'He (SAW) Was The Seal Of The Prophets','باب ذِكْرِ كَوْنِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم خَاتَمَ النَّبِيِّينَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,8,'8',NULL,NULL,NULL,'When Allah Wants To Show Mercy To A Nation, He takes Their Prophet Before Them','باب إِذَا أَرَادَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى رَحْمَةَ أُمَّةٍ قَبَضَ نَبِيَّهَا قَبْلَهَا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,9,'9',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Cistern Of Our Prophet (SAW) And Its Attributes','باب إِثْبَاتِ حَوْضِ نَبِيِّنَا صلى الله عليه وسلم وَصِفَاتِهِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,10,'10',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Angels Fought Alongside Him (SAW)','باب فِي قِتَالِ جِبْرِيلَ وَمِيكَائِيلَ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,11,'11',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Courage','باب فِي شَجَاعَةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَتَقَدُّمِهِ لِلْحَرْبِ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,12,'12',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Generosity','باب كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم أَجْوَدَ النَّاسِ بِالْخَيْرِ مِنَ الرِّيحِ الْمُرْسَلَةِ'),
('sahih-muslim',43,13,'13',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Good Manners','باب كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم أَحْسَنَ النَّاسِ خُلُقًا ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,14,'14',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Generosity','باب مَا سُئِلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم شَيْئًا قَطُّ فَقَالَ لاَ ‏ وَكَثْرَةِ عَطَائِهِ'),
('sahih-muslim',43,15,'15',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Compassion Towards Children And His Humbleness, And The Virtue Of That','باب رَحْمَتِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم الصِّبْيَانَ وَالْعِيَالَ وَتَوَاضُعِهِ وَفَضْلِ ذَلِكَ ‏‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,16,'16',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Great Modesty','باب كَثْرَةِ حَيَائِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,17,'17',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Smile And Easy Going Attitude','باب تَبَسُّمِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَحُسْنِ عِشْرَتِهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,18,'18',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Compassion Towards Women And His Command To Treat Them Kindly','باب فِي رَحْمَةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم لِلنِّسَاءِ وَأَمْرِ السُّوَّاقِ مَطَايَاهُنَّ بِالرِّفْقِ'),
('sahih-muslim',43,19,'19',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Closeness To The People, Their Seeking Blessing From Him And His Humility Towards Them','باب قُرْبِ النَّبِيِّ عَلَيْهِ السَّلاَمُ مِنَ النَّاسِ وَتَبَرُّكِهِمْ بِهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,20,'20',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Avoidance Of Sin, His Choosing The Easier Of Permissible Things, And His Vengeance For The Sake Of Allah If His Sacred Limits Were Transgressed','باب مُبَاعَدَتِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم لِلآثَامِ وَاخْتِيَارِهِ مِنَ الْمُبَاحِ أَسْهَلَهُ وَانْتِقَامِهِ ل'),
('sahih-muslim',43,21,'21',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Good Fragrance And Soft Touch, And Seeking Blessing From His Touch','باب طِيبِ رَائِحَةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَلِينِ مَسِّهِ وَالتَّبَرُّكِ بِمَسْحِهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,22,'22',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Fragrance Of His Sweat, And Seeking Blessing Therefrom','باب طِيبِ عَرَقِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَالتَّبَرُّكِ بِهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,23,'23',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prophet (SAW) Sweated When It Was Cold, And When The Revelation Came To Him','باب عَرَقِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم فِي الْبَرْدِ وَحِينَ يَأْتِيهِ الْوَحْىُ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,24,'24',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Description Of His Hair, Attributes And Appearance','باب فِي سَدْلِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم شَعْرَهُ وَفَرْقِهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,25,'25',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Description Of The Prophet (SAW); He Was The Most Handsome Of People','باب فِي صِفَةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَأَنَّهُ كَانَ أَحْسَنَ النَّاسِ وَجْهًا ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,26,'26',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Description Of His Hair','باب صِفَةِ شَعْرِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,27,'27',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Mouth, Eyes And Heels Of The Prophet (SAW)','باب فِي صِفَةِ فَمِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَعَيْنَيْهِ وَعَقِبَيْهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,28,'28',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Prophet (SAW) Was White With An Elegant Face','باب كَانَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم أَبْيَضَ مَلِيحَ الْوَجْهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,29,'29',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Grey Hairs','باب شَيْبِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,30,'30',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Seal Of Prophethood, Its Attributes And Its Location On The Body Of The Prophet (SAW)','باب إِثْبَاتِ خَاتَمِ النُّبُوَّةِ وَصِفَتِهِ وَمَحِلِّهِ مِنْ جَسَدِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,31,'31',NULL,NULL,NULL,'How Long He (SAW) Lived, And How Long He Stayed In Makkah And Al-Madinah','باب فِي صِفَةِ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَمَبْعَثِهِ وَسِنِّهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,32,'32',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Age Of The Prophet (SAW) When He Died','باب كَمْ سِنُّ النَّبِيِّ صلى الله عليه وسلم يَوْمَ قُبِضَ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,33,'33',NULL,NULL,NULL,'How Long Did The Prophet ft Stay In Makkah And Al-Madinah?','باب كَمْ أَقَامَ النَّبِيُّ صلى الله عليه وسلم بِمَكَّةَ وَالْمَدِينَةِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,34,'34',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Names','باب فِي أَسْمَائِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,35,'35',NULL,NULL,NULL,'His Knowledge Of Allah And His Great Fear Of Him','باب عِلْمِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم بِاللَّهِ تَعَالَى وَشِدَّةِ خَشْيَتِهِ ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,36,'36',NULL,NULL,NULL,'The Obligation To Follow Him (SAW)','باب وُجُوبِ اتِّبَاعِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم ‏.‏'),
('sahih-muslim',43,37,'37',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Respecting Him And Not Asking Him Unnecessary Questions','باب تَوْقِيرِهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم وَتَرْكِ إِكْثَارِ سُؤَالِهِ عَمَّا لاَ ضَرُورَةَ إِلَيْهِ أَوْ لاَ
