--
-- A bab is keyed by its page position inside the kitab (seq), not by its
-- number: numbers restart per surah in Bukhari kitab 65, and a few babs carry
-- no number. kitab_num 0 is Muslim's Introduction. Babs with no hadith are
-- kept: they are real headings of the book.
--
-- Tafseer (Bukhari kitab 65): 10 surahs hold hadiths directly under the surah
-- heading, before any bab. Each such run gets a bab of its own, titled with the
-- surah and with no bab number, so every Tafseer hadith still sits in a bab.
